Dr. Aun Porn Moniroth Chairs a Meeting of Public Financial Management Reform Commission
(Phnom Penh): The Public Financial Management Reform Commission held a meeting of the Public Financial Management Reform Commission of the Ministry of Economy and Finance on May 19, 2020 at the Ministry of Economy and Finance.
The meeting was chaired by Dr. Aun Porn Moniroth, Deputy Prime Minister, Minister of Economy and Finance and Chairman of the Public Financial Management Reform Steering Committee, with the participation of the management and the Public Financial Management Reform Working Group. Of units under the Ministry of Economy and Finance.
The meeting was videotaped using the Ministry of Economy and Finance's Intranet with the following agenda:
1: Review the progress in 2019 of the implementation of the Public Financial Management Reform Program, Phase 3 and 2: Review the progress of the implementation of the Joint Action Plan, Phase 3, 2016-2019 and the preparation of the Joint Action Plan Framework, Phase 4 .
The main contents of each agenda are as follows:
* Financial Accountability System is being developed through the introduction of Information Technology for Public Financial Management (FMIS) Phase 1 and 2. To date, FMIS has been officially launched at the central level of the Ministry of Economy and Finance, the Capital-Provincial Treasury, the Capital-Provincial Department of Economy and Finance, and 37 ministries.
Strengthening and expanding the implementation of program budgets as a basis for developing and defining changes to the Cambodian budget system as a tool for linking budgets to policies. As of 2019, the program budget has been implemented in all 18 ministries, institutions and provincial administrations, and other capital-provincial administrations will be implemented continuously until 2021.
* For next step readiness or accountability, the Ministry of Economy and Finance has been preparing a new law on the financial system, revising Sub-Decree No. 81 dated 16 November 1995 on the Establishment of Financial Supervision. Expenditure of the state budget in the ministries, provinces, municipalities, autonomous cities of Phnom Penh and public organizations and Sub-Decree No. 82 dated 16 November 1995 on the General Regulations of Public Accounts.
* As a mechanism for supporting the implementation of a successful and sustainable public financial management reform program, CJV Trained civil servants of CJV And 1059 ministries and institutions on economic and financial skills and are conducting online training and strategic planning on capacity building and capacity development within the framework of the fourth phase of the Public Financial Management Reform Program.
2: Examine the progress of the implementation of the Joint Action Plan for the third phase of 2016-2019 and the preparation of the framework of the Joint Action Plan for the fourth phase of the implementation of the public financial management reform program, the third phase of 2016-2019 has achieved progress. As planned, especially on the preparation of strategies, plans and guidelines that form the basis to strengthen the effective and efficient management of public finances.
The Deputy Prime Minister recommended all units under the auspices of the CJV. Continue to promote the implementation of the third phase of the Joint Action Plan and the coordination work between the three plus one reform sites (public financial management reform, decentralization and deconcentration, public administration and law and justice system). Homeless Veteran Wife Receives New Home from Samdech Techo Hun Sen
