Secretary General of the Lao People's Revolutionary Party sends a letter to Samdech Techo Hun Sen to share his condolences on the death of his mother-in-law
According to a letter from the Secretary General of the Lao People's Revolutionary Party to Fresh News on May 20, 2020, "I and my family would like to express our deepest condolences, sadness and condolences to Samdech Akka Moha Sena Padei." Techo Hun Sen received the news that the Duke of the Supreme Disciple Vivathana Bun Seangly passed away on May 4, 2020.
The death of Duke Prit Moha Upasika Thommanhan Vivathana Bunseangly was not only the loss of the prince's beloved mother-in-law, but also the loss of an important person who was loved and sacrificed for the sake of his relatives. And the Cambodian people as well.
In this sad time, once again, I would like to share my deepest condolences and sorrows with the Prince and his family, as well as pray to the sacred objects in the world and the power of the Buddha, the Dharma, the monks, please help to take care of the soul. The Duke of the Supreme Master Ching Hai Vivathana Bun Seangly has gone to eternal death.
(Prey Veng): A freshwater Australian shrimp farm in Prey Veng is attracting the market as this type of lobster is popularly bought for cooking because of its delicious taste, thus inspiring a farmer who is a civil servant Retired Take a career as a freshwater Australian shrimp farmer to earn extra income after his retirement salary.
In an interview with Fresh News, farmer Yun Sophal, who lives in Village 4, Sangkat Kampong Leav, Prey Veng City, said that raising freshwater Australian lobsters was easy and not difficult, and now the market is easy to sell. He claims that as long as there are lobsters for sale, people buy them all at once, making the income from this business help the family considerably.
The farmer added that today he has not yet reached the point of raising shrimp for meat to supply the market, but he has raised shrimp for breeding, he sells only as offspring and breeders, and he will continue to promote Create a pond to raise lobsters for future sales.
Mr. Yun Sophal also mentioned that the average number of lobsters he sells per month is 1,500, and the main breeder is 120, with one lobster costing 2,000 riel and the main breeder $ 10 per pair. For ordering more lobster seedlings and broilers from Mondulkiri, Ratanakiri and Kratie provinces.
Mr. Ouk Samnang, Director of Prey Veng Provincial Department of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, said that the shrimp farming of the people in Prey Veng Province is not very rich, only one family in Village 4, Sangkat Kampong Leav, Prey Veng City. Having traveled for more than a year.
After the process, it was found that the market and raising of this family's lobster was going smoothly without any hindrance, and on behalf of the department, he would like to support any farmer who intends to raise lobster and even provide professional staff. To show the technique of how to raise more.
APSARA Authority encourages the preservation of traditional Buddhist structures at a pagoda behind Banteay Kdei
(Siem Reap): The Apsara Authority has allowed the Chief Bishop of Wat Ket Kanyaram, located behind the Banteay Kdei temple, to build a new traditional Buddhist temple on a single-story concrete structure and draw a free plan. Request after checking that the old church is very dilapidated.
The purpose of this permit is to preserve the ancient pagoda architecture that is facing extinction in order to fulfill its role in accordance with the requirements of the Buddhist use, maintaining the traditional Khmer religious form that reflects the national culture in contributing to attracting visitors. National and international tourism.
Regarding the preservation of traditional religious buildings, the pagoda work team of APSARA Authority always inspects the construction to be in accordance with the technical characteristics and layout of traditional Khmer architecture.
As of May 20, 2020, the construction of the new church is about 35 percent complete. The team of APSARA Authority will continue to inspect until the construction is 100% complete to avoid any mistakes of construction. UPDATE: Voluntary Salary Contribution from Public Officials to Kovid 19 Fund to 40,760,629,908 Riels
