66 Vulnerable Families in Champou Prek Commune, Oudong District, Kampong Speu Province Receive Humanitarian Donations from the Cambodian Red Cross
(Kampong Speu): Mr. Vy Samnang, Governor of Kampong Speu Province and Chairman of the Kampong Speu Provincial Branch of the Cambodian Red Cross, this morning, May 20, 2020, led a working group to visit and bring the humanitarian donations of the Cambodian Red Cross to the people. Sixty-six vulnerable families are located in Champou Prek and Prey Krasang communes, Oudong district, Kampong Speu province.
On that occasion, Mr. Vy Samnang brought a message of greetings and memories from Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen, President of the Cambodian Red Cross, who always thought about the well-being of poor people who are suffering. Vulnerable people of all kinds, regardless of caste, race, color or political affiliation.
(Preah Vihear): 99 out of 1045 families living in Thom Cheat village, Sra Em commune, Choam Ksan district, Preah Vihear province, this morning, May 20, 2020, participated in the lottery to receive agricultural land, which is a social land concession granted by the Royal Government. Delivered through Preah Vihear Provincial Authority.
The draw for the agricultural land was held in the presence of Mr. Prak Sovann, Governor of Preah Vihear Province and Chairman of the Provincial State Land Management Committee, with the participation of provincial leaders, heads of relevant departments and local authorities of villages, communes and districts. More.
Mr. Prak Sovann stated that the agricultural land given to the people started from Sub-Decree No. 2, dated January 6, 2016 on the zoning of the community area within the Kulen Prom Tep Wildlife Sanctuary area. 5,000 hectares in Yeang and Kantuot communes, Choam Ksan district.
He confirmed that Preah Vihear province received a sub-decree to define community areas in 2016 in the previous mandate of the provincial governor. In particular, in 2020, during his term as the provincial governor, he assigned the working group of the Provincial Land Allocation and Use Committee to provide social land concessions (agricultural land) to 1045 families who have already received residential land in natural villages.
At the same time, Mr. Prak Sovann also instructed the local authorities and relevant authorities to comply with the laws, regulations and laws in force as well as the regulations of the Royal Government effectively and with a high sense of responsibility to prevent encroachment. New states are strictly prohibited in order to preserve the country's natural resources for future generations.
