Construction of Wastewater Treatment System and Drainage System in Kampot City at a Cost of Nearly 10 Million USD
(Kampot): Mr. Vong Piseth, Undersecretary of State, Ministry of Public Works and Transport, and Mr. Chiao Tay, Governor of Kampot Province, on May 20, 2020, led a technical delegation from the Ministry and the Provincial Department of Public Works and Transport, as well as project technical advisors and authorities. Relevant bases to find out and check the results of the project of construction of wastewater collection and treatment system and drainage system in Kampot city, Kampot province.
On that occasion, the Governor of Chiao Tai expressed his congratulations and hopes for this important achievement, which will be completed in the near future. Because these achievements can respond to alleviate the concerns of the provincial authorities as well as the people from the problem of flooding the city when it rains and can improve the environment in Kampot.
It should be noted that the Kampot Municipality Wastewater Treatment and Drainage Collection and Treatment Sub-Project is a corridor development project of the Greater Mekong Subregion II using ADB credit. The project started in October 2019 and will be completed in October 2021. It is planned to spend more than 9.96 million dollars.
The project has three different water treatment plants, the first in Kampong Bay, the second in Kraing Ampil in Kampot, and the third in the last. Trapeang Kanchet village, Samrong commune, Teuk Chhou district, Kampot province.
