1: The 3rd National Policy and Action Plan on the Prevention of Violence against Women 2: The 53rd Rattanak Women's Plan: Strengthening the Capacity of the Multidisciplinary Working Group to Respond to Gender-Based Violence and 4: Supporting the Establishment of Places Provide a variety of services to help victims of violence.
Meanwhile, the Minister of Women's Affairs said that during the 19 outbreaks of Kovid, according to the World Health Organization (WHO), up to 31 million women in the world are at risk of violence.
She said the increase in the number of women victims of violence during the 19-year-old virus was due to restrictions on gatherings to prevent infection, which resulted in the closure of some workplaces or reduced working hours and low pay. More fear of being infected. Chief Bank launches "Chief Mobile" to make cash transactions easier, safer and better
