(Banteay Meanchey): According to a report from Banteay Meanchey provincial authorities, on the evening of May 19, 2020, two Cambodian workers crossed the border from Thailand to Cambodia in front of Cambodian territory in front of a pine tree in the casino area. Five Star is located in Kbal Spean 1 Village, Sangkat Poipet, Poipet City, Banteay Meanchey Province.
According to the report, at the time of the incident, the Cambodian workers met with the Thai black-clad soldiers and tried to escape arrest. Thai barbed wire injures left leg The victim was taken by Thai black-clad soldiers to Aranya Hospital in Sa Kaeo Province, Thailand, after Thailand found 16 more Cambodian workers crossing the border illegally.
According to the report, one of the 16 workers detained by Thailand was a 30-year-old broker named Khan Phean alias Ou Kong Pros, who lives in Kdei Svit village, Sre Kdok commune, Kandieng district, Pursat province. The commander of the first direction in Banteay Meanchey province is interrogating the broker at Obi Choan and then sending him to the authorities for legal proceedings, and all 16 workers will be sent to O'Chrov district for recruitment.
Meanwhile, on the night of May 19, 2020, soldiers guarding the eastern border of Boeung Trakoun border arrested 24 Cambodian workers who cheated brokers to bring them across the border illegally to Thailand at Phnom Chhat checkpoint. Twenty-six Cambodians who cheated brokers to work in Thailand were sent to work on two targets: the first one in Thmar Puok district and the second one in Svay Chek district.
Lt. Gen. Chhun Mao also appealed to all Cambodians not to be deceived by brokers by guaranteeing illegal immigration to work in Thailand, as it is very dangerous at this stage as Thailand and Cambodia are Restrict border crossings to prevent illegal immigrants from entering Thai territory in order to prevent the spread of Kovid-19 disease.
