Wing and the new "Techo" Business Training Center develop digital payments, promote new digital businesses in Cambodia
The new "Techo" Business Training Center was established in late 2018, located on the campus of the Royal University of Phnom Penh, with the aim of helping the country to fully develop its digital economy.
Through a partnership with Wing Specialized Bank, the Center and its members can use the latest digital payment technology to explore new opportunities for further innovation.
"This partnership will reflect the center's commitment to the new technology training center," said Dr. Taing Nguonly, executive director of the new Techo Business Center.
"The center's new business members will also be able to connect and learn from innovative (innovative) companies like Wing, as well as benefit from Wing's technical expertise and digital payment solutions." Also.
The new "Techo" Business Training Center was established to support entrepreneurs and develop plans to transform and diversify the economy. Designed as a bridge between entrepreneurs and other stakeholders, the center will provide its members with the tools they need to help the country adapt to new technological trends and access to innovation.
Both Wing and the new "Techo" business training center share the same goal of using the latest technology to boost Cambodia's economic growth and improve people's daily lives.
Wing is recognized as a specialized bank with a network of more than 7,500 agents nationwide and offers digital payment services through the Wing smartphone app with many features that are essential to everyone's daily life. At the same time, the new business training center "Techo" aims to accelerate and provide training services designed for new businesses and small and medium enterprises.
