Two new roads to the Techo Heritage National Stadium will be built before the 2023 SEA Games
(Phnom Penh): Two new roads will be speeded up to connect to the Techo Heritage National Stadium to welcome the 32nd SEA Games 2023. This was confirmed at the meeting of the National Organizing Committee for the 2023 SEA Games (CAMSOC) at the National Olympic Committee of Cambodia on May 19, 2020.
The meeting was held in the presence of Mr. Thong Khon, Minister of Tourism and Deputy Chairman of the Standing Committee of CAMSOC, and discussed two main agendas: First, to discuss the infrastructure connected to the Techo National Stadium and second, to talk about Directions and roles of six of the 14 expert committees.
On that occasion, Mr. Thong Khon also urged the six expert committees to understand their roles and responsibilities and to prepare a clear work plan for effective implementation in accordance with the strategic plan for the 2023 SEA Games.
In addition, on behalf of the CAMSOC Standing Committee, the Minister intended to hold a weekly review meeting to review the progress of Samdech Pichey Sena Tea Banh, Chairman of the National Committee for the 2023 SEA Games.
