(Phnom Penh): The APSARA Authority on May 19, 2020, held a ceremony to refer to the fragments of the Buddha statues that were excavated near the Angkor Wat temple in the past to be repaired.
The reference to all the Buddha statues from the excavation pit is to study, assemble, repair, preserve and enhance the value of the artifacts, as well as allow archaeologists to complete the excavation work.
