The Royal Government of Cambodia prepares a draft sub-decree governing the use of "drones"
(Phnom Penh): The Royal Government of Cambodia has been preparing a draft sub-decree on the management of drones to ensure safety, security and public order in Cambodia.
The Ministry of Interior is responsible for preparing the draft sub-decree. On the afternoon of May 19, 2020, Mr. Bun Hon, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Interior, held a meeting with the Secretary of State, Undersecretary of State, General Commission of the National Police, General Secretariat and other relevant General Departments, as well as other relevant officials to discuss the drafting. This.
On that occasion, Mr. Bun Hon said that the draft sub-decree on the management of "drones" had already been discussed once on July 12, 2019. This sub-decree also requested the professional officers to continue the study and today it was discussed further.
Mr. Bun Hon said that the draft sub-decree is very important because there is no clear management today. He added that the use of drones in agriculture or in the commercial sector is not a concern, but if used to affect national security, this is a serious concern.
The Secretary of State added that after the meeting to draft the sub-decree, it will be possible to meet with the relevant inter-ministerial ministries such as the Ministry of National Defense, the Secretariat of Civil Aviation to discuss how to make this sub-decree better and more applicable.
During the meeting, Lt. Gen. Pang Rasy, Deputy Chairman of the Legislative Council of the Ministry of Interior, made a report on the drafting process of the "Drone" sub-decree held during the first meeting. At that meeting, the meeting decided to revise some additional definitions.
On the other hand, the meeting revised the training of drones and decided to add some conditions for the manufacturer or processor to register the technical or have a technical plan to put To the authorities as well.
Please note that the draft sub-decree on the management of "drones" aims to control the use of all "drones" to ensure safety, security and public order in Cambodia. The draft sub-decree also aims to determine the registration, production, processing and use of "drones".
