The Asian Development Bank (ADB) has stated that the major projects and programs that ADB has provided loans and assistance to Cambodia, which began in 2019 and are continuing to date, include:
* First, the $ 7.6 million Solar National Park project to reduce electricity costs by investing in the private sector in renewable energy.
These power plants are expected to emit at least 148,650 tonnes of carbon dioxide emissions a year.
* Second: Eco-Financial Development Program (Sub-Program 2) worth $ 40 million to increase access to finance and provide new financial services to poor communities, including: rural areas, agriculture and business. Small and medium.
The program supports the adoption of key national financial environment strategies, key laws such as confidence building laws, consumer protection laws, and the inclusion of financial literacy in the curriculum.
* Third: $ 60 million Competitive Strengthening Skills Project to develop human resources into a skilled workforce in four priority areas: manufacturing, construction, electricity and electronics.
The ADB's 2019 operations will reach nearly $ 34 billion to support developing countries in the Asia-Pacific region.
