(Kandal): In the case of a machine that cut off 5 roads in Trapeang Russey village, Tumnup Thom commune, Ponhea Leu district, Kandal province, and caused a violent protest by the people, it was found that the road that the people used to do This trip is really a lot on private land.
However, Deputy Governor of Ponhea Leu District, Mr. Sam Ol Chamroeun Udom, under the command of District Governor Thorn Sovanna, intervened carefully, asking the land owner, Mr. Pheng Song Kay, to remove the land connecting the road. The detached body was re-issued to allow the people to travel temporarily, and the district administration and the relevant authorities will certainly resolve it fairly for the landowners and the people.
The intervention took place on the morning of May 18, 2020, after the cases of villagers and village chiefs of Chhwang commune, Tumnup Thom commune and Chrey Las commune, Ponhea Leu district, protested and asked the district authorities to help solve the problem. Pheng Song took the machine to cut off five roads.
Residents and village chiefs alike say that this one-lane road dates back to before the Pol Pot era. Recently, a philanthropist named Svay Sam Oeun paid for the road to be paved with red stone.
Through the authority to measure and set up border posts along the plots of the people and the boundaries of their respective villages and communes. After the road was completed, Pheng Song took the machine and cut it off, claiming that the road was built on his land.
After the incident, the Ponhea Leu District Administration assigned Mr. Sam Ol Chamroeun, Deputy District Governor, to lead the inspection to the actual location. As a result, the team researched and found that "this road is really in Mr. Pheng Song's land" because during the first road construction, the road builder did not communicate with the landowners and village authorities to check. Clear geography.
After finding the root of the problem, the Deputy District Governor asked Mr. Pheng Song, the landowner, to reconnect this road so that people can travel temporarily, and the district authorities will coordinate to find a solution and leave. To stay long. The landowners and the people also agreed to this compromise. Senior Minister Yim Nola sends condolence message to Senior Minister Him Chhem
