At the same time, the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports also promotes online education in all levels and types of educational institutions by introducing students, parents and educational institutions to organize teaching and scheduling assessments for students. Students can continue their studies and earn a diploma officially recognized from this study (MoEYS, 2020b).
In response to these announcements, the ACLEDA Institute of Business (AIB) has been working diligently and diligently to develop teaching methods, tools and materials for turning direct learning into online learning.
Since the end of March 2020, ACLEDA Business Institute has been offering online learning to all available students and trainees from ACLEDA Bank Plc. And other institutions or companies.
Mr. Sop Sophea, Chairman of the Sub-Committee on Economic Research and Analysis of Cambodia, ACLEDA Business Institute, said that the online study at ACLEDA Business Institute is easy and efficient because:
3. Learning Management System (LMS) Today, there are many options for users to download for free.
The URM program for recording and reporting student attendance to parents and stakeholders, as well as disseminating academic results to students, and the Telegram program for communication and sending of study materials (lessons, images, audio, video, etc.), while the e-library is used for Save files, audiobooks, pictures and videos, etc. Related to teaching and learning.
Mr. So Sophea added that the Board, Management, Teachers-Trainers and staff of AIB have agreed to organize:
1. Revise strategic plans, action plans, as well as operating principles, procedures, and guidelines for continuing operations in the context of the Kovid Outbreak 19 to achieve a business plan.
2: A series of training sessions, workshops and meetings for teachers, administrators and staff to share training and / or discussions regarding the organization of lectures, assessments and student facilitation online.
3. Establish a digital forum development and development committee as well as a technical committee composed of technical teams at AIB and parent company (ACLEDA Bank Plc.) To support management, teachers, staff and students in providing educational services. Electronic systems.
4: Edit detailed curriculum, equip tools and develop additional materials for teaching.
5: Inform students on the preparation of tools and materials for study.
6: Continue to monitor, encourage, support and listen to students to make online learning smoother and more effective as in the classroom.
In order to maintain the sustainability and effectiveness of this online study, Mr. Sophea has made the following recommendations:
1. The Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports should continue to maintain the recognition of this online education, as in developed countries around the world, even if the epidemic of Kovid 19 has ended.
2. All parties should continue to work together and support each other to benefit from online learning and further develop it in line with practical needs.
3. All stakeholders should continue to study, find and equip the necessary equipment and train teachers on the use of that equipment, especially the teaching and evaluation of students for this study to ensure the provision of their educational services. By the highest quality.
4: All stakeholders should continue to disseminate and provide education in this way in addition to face-to-face education for students who are still in need, despite the Ministry of Education announcing the reopening of all institutions after the outbreak. Is completed.
5: All stakeholders should seek to learn more and take advantage of online learning as a basis for decision making and improve the quality of work and services as much as possible to maximize benefits as well as compete with local competitors. And the universe.
