Mr. Kun Nhim continued to distribute donations to Children's Kitchen and advised to strengthen the implementation of Kovid disease prevention measures
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Kun Nhem, Royal Government Delegate in charge of the Director General of the General Department of Customs and Excise of Cambodia, accompanied by leaders and officials of the General Department of Customs and Excise of Cambodia, visited and brought donations on May 18, 2020. Support for Children's Kitchen Organization in Sangkat Boeung Keng Kang 3, Khan Boeung Keng Kang, Phnom Penh.
According to Mr. Ngov Chhiv, President of Children's Kitchen, this organization has been receiving 300-350 children per day to get a snack (not staying permanently), read, write, cut hair, cut nails. And bathing.
Currently, due to the Kovid 19 crisis, in order to help prevent the spread of the disease in the community, Children's Kitchen has suspended the cooking process for children as usual, but has distributed food to children who come to the organization and at the accommodation instead. In addition, the organization has a mission to encourage and motivate children to attend public schools.
Please be informed that Children's Kitchen is the fourth goal of the support of the Charity Fund of the General Department of Customs and Excise to support the poor, orphans, vulnerable and small informal economic groups affected. Due to the outbreak of Kovid-19 disease.
The Ministry of Public Works requests the ministries, institutions, organizations and embassies to change the license plate and license plate of new vehicles before October 30.
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Public Works and Transport (MPWT) has requested the ministries, state institutions as well as national and international organizations, embassies and heads of UN missions in Cambodia to exchange vehicle identification cards and vehicle registration plates in accordance with Royal Government sub-decrees and new prakas. Of the Ministry on the change of vehicle license plate before October 30, 2020.
According to the announcement of the Ministry of Public Works and Transport on May 18, 2020, it was highlighted that in June 2019, the Royal Government issued a sub-decree on "Registration, issuance of vehicle identification cards and equipping of vehicle license plates". In April 2020, the Ministry of Public Works and Transport also issued a proclamation on "Identification of Vehicle Identification Cards as State Property of Ministries and Institutions".
The issuance of this sub-decree and prakas for the purpose of managing vehicles as state property of ministries and institutions to ensure security, order, safety and ownership rights of vehicles of ministries and institutions, especially to facilitate the management of vehicle license plates.
The statement added that for this reason, the Royal Government has decided to revise and redefine the license plates of some ministries and institutions in the order of ID numbers from 01 state to 36 states.
In this announcement, the Ministry strongly hopes that the owners of vehicle management belong to all relevant ministries and institutions will cooperate in implementing the content of this notice to use vehicle identification cards and vehicle identification plates in accordance with the law. Wing Specialized Bank and Jet Straight Royal Bank launch microfinance account
(Phnom Penh): You can now open a Jetstar Royal Bank savings account for just $ 5 and get high interest rates by using the Wing smartphone app, which takes just a few minutes and can be used at any time. Everywhere with Wing smartphone apps and Wing agents nationwide.
Recently, Wing Specialized Bank (Cambodia) Limited and Jet Royal Bank have partnered to offer one of the first new products that allows customers to open a high-interest savings account through the Wing smartphone app in just a few minutes. Just minutes and enjoy high interest rates and can easily operate through the Wing smartphone app.
The first new offering from Wing Specialized Bank and Jet Strait Royal Bank is unprecedented in the smartphone payment market and helps Cambodians with ID cards to open an official bank account with just two or three clicks. On the button in the Wing smartphone app.
Customers will receive interest on the money they have deposited in Jetr Royale Bank micro-savings account, which can be operated anytime, anywhere through the Wing smartphone app.
More importantly, customers who make a deposit into a micro-savings account will receive a special interest rate of 1.35% per annum.
The use of this new product is even easier. Wing customers simply click to launch the Wing smartphone app on their mobile phone, go to the Savings Product button and select the desired deposit amount, the minimum balance is only $ 5.
Immediately, their savings account will start earning interest as well. They can also withdraw this savings at any time by simply transferring it back to their WING account and withdrawing money from over 7,500 WING agents nationwide.
Transferring money between Wing account and Jet Bank Royal account can be done easily, securely and quickly.
Toru Myochin, CEO of Jet Royal Bank, said: “Among Jet Bank Royal's commitment is to provide high quality and widely used financial services in the Kingdom of Cambodia.
It is our privilege to partner with Wing Specialized Bank on this innovative offering for the first time on the market.
This innovative Wing Specialized Bank product is developed with the support of Jetrot Royal Bank.
