Minister of Justice: Campaign to resolve case congestion is not an interference and impairment of the independence of the judiciary (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): Mr. Keut Rith, Minister of Justice, stated that the campaign to resolve case congestion in The Capital-Provincial Courts issued by the Ministry of Justice at this time are not interfering with or undermining the independence of the judiciary.
The announcement of the Minister of Justice was made at a press conference organized by the Ministry of Justice this morning, May 18, 2020, regarding the resolution of case congestion in Cambodian courts.
Mr. Keut Rith stated that the officials of the Ministry of Justice who carry out the campaign to solve the case of congestion in the courts in the capital-province must be done in accordance with the law and strictly, without interfering with or affecting the independence of the judiciary.
"Based on this legal basis, the Ministry of Justice does not interfere in the decision of the judge, which is an independent power, so his discretion is exercised, but it is an authority that he must use in accordance with the law," he said. .
The Cambodian Red Cross would like to thank HE Samorn Bandith and Lok Chumteav for donating 1 million Riels to the Cambodian Red Cross for May 8, 2020.
(Phnom Penh): The Cambodian Red Cross would like to thank HE Samorn Bandith, Undersecretary of State, Ministry of Information and Lok Chumteav for donating 1,000,000 Riels (One Million Riels) to the Cambodian Red Cross to celebrate its anniversary. 157 World Red Cross and Red Crescent Day, May 8, 2020 under the theme "I love peace and the Cambodian Red Cross."
This confirmation was made at a press conference announcing the campaign to resolve the case congestion at the Capital-Provincial Court at the Ministry of Justice this morning, May 18, 2020.
At the same time, the Minister of Justice said that the four working groups were set up to help promote the implementation of the campaign, especially to solve the congestion of the case is the work of judges and prosecutors in the Capital-Provincial Courts. . However, these four working groups also act as monitoring mechanisms.
Speaking at a press conference on the morning of May 18, 2020, Mr. Keut Rith said that in order to ensure rigor, integrity and accuracy in the implementation of this campaign, the Ministry of Justice has set out two approaches:
Mr. Keut Rith stated: "There is one last point to inform the public that in order to ensure firmness, the Ministry of Justice has set out two approaches: the first approach is to resolve all congestion cases. The law is strictly in accordance with all the rules. "There is no campaign to deal with it illegally, there is no justice."
The Minister of Justice continued, "The second approach of this campaign is for the four working groups and the Capital-Provincial Courts to adhere to a major principle in order to avoid the situation of dried fish spawning." It means adhering to the principles of honesty, integrity and non-corruption.
Based on the data collected only at the Phnom Penh Municipal Court, the remaining cases have not been resolved since 2019, up to 12,000 cases, and the average number of new cases is about 700 to 900 per case. The month that made the Phnom Penh Municipal Court in the current situation unable to solve this challenge on its own.
On May 18, 2020, the new Minister of Justice, Mr. Keut Rith, announced the launch of a campaign to resolve congestion cases in the Capital-Provincial Courts in order to expedite the pursuit of justice as soon as possible and to enhance the capacity of the judiciary. To provide better justice services to the people. The campaign is also to help reduce the current overcrowding in prisons.
For the success of this campaign, he instructed the President of the Capital-Provincial Court to focus on three principles, including: principles in the prosecution phase, principles in the investigation phase and principles in the trial phase. Chip Monglen Groundbreaking Ceremony for Grand Phnom Penh City Grand Renovation Project
(Phnom Penh): Leading real estate developer Chip Monglen held a groundbreaking ceremony for the Grand Phnom Penh City project this morning, May 18, 2020.
The Grand Phnom Penh City project, which covers an area of up to 260 hectares, has been aesthetically modified, which will extend the lives of today's clients to a greater extent.
The project is building a series of wide twin lanes that provide ease of driving and pedestrians, accompanied by large greenery on either side of the road from the entrance to the house.
What's more, Grand Phnom Penh City will build unprecedented new style housing in Chip Monglen projects to meet the needs of customers and the luxury of this project itself.
In addition, a huge business and sports center will be present at the Grand Phnom Penh City project, accompanied by the Grand Phnom Penh City Golf Course to provide civility, comfort and confidence in living.
The Grand Phnom Penh City project was acquired by Chip Monglen on October 16, 2019.
Waiting for the sale! This great Grand Phnom Penh City project will be officially launched to its customers in the near future.
(Prey Veng): A huge house fire occurred on the night of May 17, 2020 in Ponhea Leang village, Angkor Reach commune, Preah Sdach district, Prey Veng province, causing a house fire and loss of property. A large number and the death of an elderly grandmother, the most tragic.
Preah Sdach district police said that the fire burned a house made of galvanized iron, measuring 6 × 7 meters, owned by Phan Kun, 46, and his wife Khim Hon, 45, and caused an old woman. Eang Soth, an 85-year-old woman, died in the blaze, along with a bicycle, a motorcycle and $ 1,000 in cash.
