In a press conference after the announcement of the campaign to solve the case of congestion in the court, Minister Keut Rith, who has just been appointed Minister of Justice, claimed that judges and prosecutors who commit professional misconduct may face immediate termination. .
"We do not allow cases of dried fish spawning, which means that we do not allow the campaign to be used illegally or for personal gain," said Minister Keut Rith. "With this approach, we will take a firm stand, judges, prosecutors, clerks who have committed wrongdoing will be returned with a firm response, both legal and professional."
The Minister of Justice also stressed that the Ministry of Justice has helped the Anti-Corruption Unit (ACU), which means that if there is a case of corruption in the campaign, the Ministry of Justice will take strict action.
He added that the Ministry of Justice has also met with the Supreme Court and will continue to meet with the Supreme Council of the Magistracy to ensure that professional misconduct is addressed with the same professional responsibility. The biggest professional discipline that can be found is dismissal.
At the same time, Minister Keut Rith also called on the people and journalists to provide information to the Ministry of Justice in case of any irregularities that occurred in the campaign to resolve the case of congestion in this court to provide justice. To the victim.
At the same time, the Minister of Justice saw that the Prosecutor's Office of the Capital-Provincial Court did not use the method of indictment for misdemeanors by sending to trial or appearing immediately, but always used the method of indictment to This type of crime through the investigation, which in turn leads to a significant increase in the number of cases in the interrogation phase.
Based on the data collected only at the Phnom Penh Municipal Court, the remaining cases have not been resolved since 2019, up to 12,000 cases, and the average number of new cases is about 700 to 900 per case. The month that made the Phnom Penh Municipal Court in the current situation can not answer this challenge on its own.
This historic campaign in the Cambodian justice system aims to accelerate the search for justice and enhance the capacity of the judiciary to provide better justice services to the people. The campaign is also to help reduce the current overcrowding in prisons.
Mr. Keut Rith issued an instruction to the President of the Capital-Provincial Court to ensure that the campaign runs smoothly and achieves good results and is based on the spirit of the Code of Criminal Procedure, Criminal Code and related circulars.
For the success of this campaign, Mr. Keut Rith instructed the President of the Capital-Provincial Court to focus on three principles, including: principles in the prosecution phase, principles in the investigation phase and principles in the trial phase.
