(Kandal): Village chiefs and residents in Chhwang commune, Tumnup Thom commune and Chrey Las commune, Ponhea Leu district, Kandal province, this weekend protested and asked the district authorities to help solve the problem after Pheng Song took five roadblocks. .
The protest came after a section of red cobblestone road was cut off and impassable, while commune authorities were unable to resolve it by pushing each other and arguing that it was overcrowded.
Residents and village chiefs alike say that this road has been a cart road since before the Pol Pot regime, but recently a philanthropist named Svay Sam Oeun paved it with red gravel. At the request of the people.
The construction of this road through the authority to measure and set up border posts along the people's plots and bordering their respective villages and communes. After Mr. Svay Sam Oeun finished building the road, Pheng Song took the machine and cut it off, claiming to build the road on his land. This was confirmed by Mr. Sam Oun, Member of Tumnup Thom Commune Council, Ponhea Leu District.
Residents and village chiefs have urged the district authorities to help Pheng Songkay clear the road, otherwise when the rain and the rainy season arrives can not travel due to slippery And flooding.
In addition, this road is very important for people to travel from one village to another, especially factory workers, without having to travel to work around Route 51, because this road is a shortcut for factory workers when they take a break from work. Straight can come to eat at home. But if you travel to Street 51, it is too far to come and eat at home and take a break from work at noon.
He also added that the poles erected on both sides of the road were set up by a company named Pheng Song, and that the poles erected on both sides of the road were to mark the road. He also requested that the body be made clean so that the people as well as those who work in the factory can travel easily and easily for the people to transport various agricultural products.
Mr. Phan Phoeun, a resident of Ta Kork village, also said that this road is very important. He has difficulty traveling and if the rainy season is over, he requests that the road be re-connected so that they, as well as the people in the commune, can travel more easily.
Regarding this request, Mr. Thorn Sovanna, Governor of Ponhea Leu District, said on May 18, 2020 that he also received this information and on May 18, 2020, he will arrange for the Deputy District Governor to inspect the location. That way to report to him.
