(Phnom Penh): The Asian Development Bank's (ADB) development programs and programs for developing countries in the Asia-Pacific region will reach $ 33.74 billion in 2019, demonstrating its commitment. Dedicated to its vision to achieve prosperity, environment, resilience and sustainability.
ADB achieved its goal a year ahead of schedule to double its annual investment in the climate sector, which in 2014 was just $ 3 billion. This demonstrates ADB's strong commitment to climate change-related activities. The 2030 strategy sets a target of achieving a total of $ 35 billion in climate financing by 2024 and $ 80 billion by 2030.
ADB is also moving towards achieving its 2030 Strategic Goal of promoting gender equality in at least 75% of its operations.
