On May 15, 2020, the Royal Government of Thailand issued a proclamation to ease further austerity measures to facilitate people's daily lives and economic recovery, which is valid from May 17, 2020 onwards, with the following main contents:
* A: Economics and daily life
* Restaurants, food parks, food centers and general canteens, but alcohol is not allowed * Supermarkets, grocery stores and community shops are only for the sale of groceries and services that are required to be open by 8pm * Retail / Wholesale or Large wholesale market * Maintenance facilities, accommodation or daycare for children and the elderly * Recording of TV shows, movies and videos * Meeting rooms in hotels and conference centers.
* B: Sports and Health Care
* Fifth: Employees or site owners as in points A and B are required to follow the communicable disease prevention measures in accordance with the instructions, conditions and time set by the mayor / province or state and the authority has the right to inspect, advise, warn and prohibit; Take legal action.
As mentioned above, all Cambodians in Thailand, please continue to cooperate with the Thai authorities in implementing this declaration to prevent the spread of Kovid 19.
