Minister of Justice Encourages Civil Society to Participate in Campaign to Solve Case Congestion at Capital-Provincial Courts (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): Mr. Keut Rith, Minister of Justice, on May 18, Encourage all civil society to work with the Ministry of Justice regarding the campaign to resolve case congestion at the Capital-Provincial Court.
Mr. Keut Rith's remarks were made after the opening ceremony of the campaign to resolve the case congestion at the Capital-Provincial Court on the morning of May 18, 2020. The opening ceremony of the campaign took place at the Ministry of Justice.
Mr. Keut Rith said: "I urge that civil society should work with the Ministry of Justice to avoid illegal entry into a work that can be seen by the public as an avoidance of work that is Jurisdiction of judges and prosecutors.
Mr. Keut Rith said that the Ministry of Justice is open for civil society to work with the ministry's secretariat and to communicate freely with the ministry's page or with a spokesperson.
The Minister of Justice added that the Ministry is open, but we do not want him to use his unlawful power to enter the court and make another report without knowing what his report is based on.
At the same time, Mr. Keut Rith said that the Ministry of Justice also met with the United Nations High Commissioner for Human Rights in Cambodia (UNOCHR) and raised the issue of congestion in the courts. The capital-province as well.
Mr. Keut Rith said that during the meeting, not only did the issue be raised, but the Ministry of Justice also requested that the United Nations High Commissioner for Human Rights in Cambodia be involved in resolving the case.
On May 11, 2020, the Minister of Justice, Mr. Keut Rith, decided to set up a steering committee to solve the case of congestion in the Capital-Provincial Courts.
The Steering Committee for Solving Case Congestion at the Capital-Provincial Courts has the following duties:
* 1: Lead and coordinate the joint work on the implementation of the campaign to solve the problem of congestion in the court and the Prosecutor of the Capital and Provincial Courts
* 2: Establish guidelines, rules and action plans necessary to implement the campaign effectively to contribute to improving the institutional capacity to better serve the judiciary as well as to reduce overcrowding in prisons.
* 3: Set out solutions to the challenges that arise from the implementation of the campaign
Mr. Loo, Director of Sing Bay Otec, reported to the Minister of Agriculture and the delegation that the company has started to implement the project to develop the state forest plantation industry under the cooperation with the Forestry Administration since 2011 on 34 areas. , 000 hectares of Boeung Char Forest Promotion and Restoration Station in Sambo District, Kratie Province and Siem Bok District, Stung Treng Province.
The President thanked the Forestry Administration, especially the Minister of Agriculture, for his cooperation, encouragement and support for the development of the plantation industry from the beginning to the present, and he hoped and believed that the Forestry Administration as well as the Ministry would Continue to provide cooperation so that the company can achieve the investment plan as expected.
During the visit, Mr. Veng Sakhon, Minister of Agriculture, met with 150 company workers, bringing a message from Samdech Techo Prime Minister of the Kingdom of Cambodia to the workers and wished the people. Every citizen, every family here, to meet only happiness, prosperity, happiness in the family and stay healthy, stay away from the global communicable disease Kovid-19.
Afterwards, the Minister praised the achievements of the company, including planting, nursery, and especially the establishment of a seed research and planting institute in Kampong Thom, which has been contributing significantly to the development of the forestry sector. Cambodia through research, dissemination, nursery and reforestation in accordance with the policy of the Ministry of Agriculture and especially the Royal Government of Cambodia.
At the same time, the Minister instructed the company to make more efforts in collaboration with the Forestry Administration, the Provincial Department of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries to accelerate activities on planting to meet the planned plan.
He also called on the forest communities in the area to participate in planting trees and maintaining state forest lands for the benefit of forest products and by-products, as well as raising livestock and other mixed crops to improve living standards.
It should be noted that in addition to investing in tree planting cooperation with the Forestry Administration as a raw material for the production of concrete and furniture to supply the local and foreign markets, there is a shortage of raw materials now and in the future. Extremely when the market demands a lot. That is why the company strives to plant trees as a local raw material, avoiding the use of natural forest as a raw material.
According to the company representative, the company also lacks land for investment in planting industrial trees, tens of thousands of hectares now and in the future.
