(Phnom Penh): Many rare species have been found in the Virachey National Park in Ratanakkiri province through 12 automatic cameras taken by park rangers from April 2019 to April 2020.
Mr. Neth Pheaktra, Secretary of State and Spokesperson of the Ministry of Environment, said on May 17, 2020 that from May 6 to 13, 2020, park rangers collected the automatic cameras that the team set up. Wildlife is present in Virachey National Park, and through the images captured by the automatic machine, significant results are obtained.
The camera captures many rare species of wildlife, including leopards, tigers, leopards, lizards, deer, lizards or lizards, wild boars, bears and rare birds such as the silver rooster and lizard. High attention to protection and conservation.
The Secretary of State for the Ministry of Environment noted that in the last five years, the presence of wildlife has increased, including some rare and endangered species, due to the efforts of the authorities to conserve and protect wildlife habitats.
Mr. Neth Pheaktra said that the presence of all these wildlife is full of hope for the people of Cambodia and for the benefit of the world's biodiversity, because some species are endangered but present in the forests of Cambodia.
"The wildlife and plants on this planet are invaluable in terms of ecosystems, genetics, society, economics, science, education, culture, linked to human life and sustainable development," he said. Also. The Secretary of State for the Ministry of Environment pointed out that some of the world's endangered wildlife and birds are present in Cambodia.
Mr. Neth Pheakdra reiterated Cambodia's high commitment to join the fight against illegal wildlife trafficking. "Cambodia, as a member of the United Nations, is ready to cooperate internationally with all countries in conserving natural resources and preventing and combating illegal wildlife trafficking."
Mr. Neth Pheaktra added, "Cambodia has been actively involved in the fight against illegal wildlife trafficking, and Cambodia is also cooperating as an international partner with the United Kingdom to prevent and suppress illegal wildlife trafficking." The law in the world.
He stated that Cambodia has established mechanisms as well as laws and practices on a regular basis to prevent and combat such illegal wildlife trafficking, has cracked down on many crimes and freed many wildlife from the clutches of criminals. Both were arrested, sent to court for sentencing, as well as fines and contract termination.
