The demarcation of the activities of the Supreme Advisory Council on this land issue was made at the Plenary Meeting of the Council of Ministers on May 15, 2020 at the Peace Palace.
According to the announcement of the results of the Plenary Meeting of the Council of Ministers, which was received by Fresh News, Samdech Techo Hun Sen determined that the Secretariat and the members of the Supreme Advisory Council should fulfill the following duties:
A: It is not allowed to settle all disputes that Samdech Techo Hun Sen has resolved and the notification of the Office of the Council of Ministers is already there.
B: Not allowed to resolve all land disputes that are being processed by the court.
C: It is not allowed to settle any disputes ended by the judiciary with a final verdict or judgment.
D: The Secretariat of the Supreme Advisory Council shall examine the objectives and objectives that the members and members of the Supreme Advisory Council go to solve without issuing a mission letter in the cases mentioned above. At the same time, the case of land dispute between individuals must not be sent to Samdech Techo for resolution.
