(Takeo): Two officials of the Department of Education, Youth and Sports of Takeo Province, Mr. Pho Keo Raksmey, Director of the Office of Accounting and Mr. Yun Yong, Deputy Director of the Secondary Office, were posted on the Facebook account "Takeo Provincial Education" on Facebook. Conspiracy to commit corruption through mission money and also formed a family faction in the department.
According to the Facebook icon above, Pho Keo Raksmey, the head of the accounting office, conspired with Yun Yong to steal a mission payment for Nuth Sokuntheary, Pho Keo Raksmey's wife, for 1,280,000 riel a month. For 10 months, the state budget was 11,280,000 Riels. Not only that, Mr. Pho Keo Raksmey formed a faction of families in the Department of Education, as well as used the role of oppressing and using inappropriate words against officials.
Separately, Mr. Yun Yong, Deputy Director of the Secondary Education Office, was accused by the Facebook icon of Takeo Provincial Education that he had stolen the bilingual exam subject for the candidate (Exam session (22/07/2019) at that time, Mr. Puth Phalla, Director of the Office of Finance Department The object was captured and returned, and Yun Yong conspired with Pho Keo Raksmey to plan to pay for the mission for more than 10 million riels in 10 months.
The Facebook icon also asked Takeo Provincial Governor Ouch Phea, Education Minister Hang Chun Naron and Anti-Corruption Minister Om Yentieng to launch an investigation into the two officials.
In relation to the above allegations, Mr. Pho Keo Raksmey, Director of the Accounting Office of the Takeo Provincial Department of Education, also categorically denied the allegations, saying, "It is untrue because all the allegations "This requires a plan and a letter, a visa, a clear report and a lot of signatures, so we can not do this."
According to Mr. Pho Keo Raksmey, the official who leaked the documents was someone who wanted to be the director of the Secondary Education Office, and this case was rejected by the department and a complaint was filed in court.
In connection with the corruption scandal at the Department of Education, Takeo provincial governor Ouch Phea said that provincial authorities had not opened an investigation or summoned the accused for questioning. A letter of explanation has already been issued on this issue.
