Siem Reap Province Introduces Some Key Plans to Re-Accept Domestic Tourists After Affected by Kovid 19
(Siem Reap): As the Kovid 19 crisis continues to adversely affect tourism businesses such as hotels, guesthouses, restaurants and transportation services, the Siem Reap Tourism Development Commission has launched a number of key plans to attract National tourists visit Siem Reap to help those involved in tourism.
The key mechanisms that the commission plans to set out to attract national tourists include encouraging districts, especially those with tourism potential, to widely publicize their tourism destinations through simple means such as Facebook. Small-scale tourism, such as camping, cycling, cleaning, environmental clean-up, infrastructure and food standards that ensure the safety of consumers.
During a meeting to find a mechanism to attract national tourists on the morning of May 12, 2020 at Siem Reap Provincial Hall, Mr. Pov Piseth, Deputy Governor of Siem Reap said that the current situation can not wait for international tourists, but to find ways to Many national tourists visit the tourist area. Although it is not possible to replace international tourists, national tourists can help promote some tourism services.
Mr. Sok Sangvar, Deputy Director General and Deputy Chairman of the Commission, supported the mechanism proposed by the meeting to promote the tourism movement among national visitors. However, he reminded the meeting that the organization of tourism events should take into account the prevention of the spread of Kovid 19 in accordance with the principles of the Royal Government, because the disease is not completely calm.
(Phnom Penh): The Plenary Meeting chaired by Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, on Friday morning, May 15, 2020, was approved by the Council of Ministers without amendment on the “Draft Law on Anti-Money Laundering”. And terrorist financing. ” This was announced by Mr. Phay Siphan, Minister Delegate to the Prime Minister and Chairman of the Government Spokesperson Unit.
Mr. Phay Siphan said that in June 2004, Cambodia drafted a legal framework, enacting the Law on Anti-Money Laundering and Terrorist Financing on June 24, 2007, and established law enforcement mechanisms such as the Coordinating Committee: National Anti-Money Laundering and Terrorist Financing and the Cambodian Financial Intelligence Unit.
Today's Plenary Meeting of the Council of Ministers was chaired by Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia.
The draft law aims to ensure the prevention of money laundering and terrorist financing by identifying measures to control, prevent, suppress and eliminate money laundering and terrorist financing.
Mr. Phay Siphan added that the "Draft Law on Anti-Financing of Genocide" has the following contents:
Objective: This law aims to guarantee against money laundering and terrorist financing by defining measures to control, prevent, suppress and eliminate money laundering and terrorist financing.
3. Scope: This law applies to all money laundering and terrorist financing activities in the Kingdom of Cambodia. The Council of Ministers has approved and amended three points on the "Draft Law on Mutual Legal Aid in the Criminal Sector".
(Phnom Penh): The Plenary Meeting chaired by Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, on Friday morning, May 15, 2020, the Council of Ministers decided to approve and revise three points on the "Draft Law on Mutual Assistance." "Back to the legal field in the field of criminal." This was announced by Mr. Phay Siphan, Minister Delegate to the Prime Minister and Chairman of the Royal Government Spokesperson Unit.
Mr. Phay Siphan added that the "Draft Law on Mutual Legal Aid in the Criminal Sector" has the following contents:
Within the framework of legal cooperation in the field of criminal law, the Kingdom of Cambodia has signed bilateral and multilateral treaties with many countries, in particular treaties related to extradition, transfer of prisoners and mutual legal assistance in Criminal sector.
The purpose of this law is to provide legal assistance in the field of criminal affairs between the Kingdom of Cambodia and foreign states in connection with criminal proceedings, as well as to freeze, seize and confiscate property in order to strengthen And expand international cooperation.
