(Kampong Speu): Mr. Veng Sakhon, Minister of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, on May 14, 2020, requested the people to make more efforts to grow vegetables, increase production volume, ensure quality, improve packaging processing capacity. Compete to meet market needs and consumer preferences and especially reduce imports.
The request was made on the occasion of Mr. Veng Sakhon, accompanied by the Secretary of State, Undersecretary of State and the Provincial Governor, inspecting the status and progress of the implementation of the new Agricultural Technology Program for Resilience to Climate Change (ASPIRE) in Daun Tip Village. Pram Bei Mom commune, Thpong district, Kampong Speu province, on the morning of May 14, 2020.
According to Chuob Kheang, the owner of the plantation, he and 30 other families have been growing vegetables as their core business for more than 10 years since the construction of the eight-corner dam. Currently, with the technical support of the ASPIRE program, the vegetable business has been growing steadily, with an average of more than 20 million riel per year.
After seeing the achievements of the project, especially the results of farmers now, the family income, Minister Veng Sakhon asked people to make more efforts to grow vegetables, increase production, quality assurance, improve capacity. Process packaging to meet market demand and consumer preferences, and especially reduce imports.
At the same time, the Minister of Agriculture also instructed the Department to provide additional technical training, focusing on the use of nets and vegetable irrigation systems, the implementation of GAP, the implementation of contract agricultural production, how to increase customer trust through quality. And safety.
In addition, the department should study the possibility of establishing additional vegetable collection points to ensure the supply quantity, strengthen packaging techniques and provide clear labels to avoid fraud or counterfeiting of products.
