(Phnom Penh): The Indian Council for Cultural Relations (ICCR) has brought together famous poets, musicians and singers from their respective countries to produce songs from their respective homes in India entitled "Together to Fight Kovid ”to help strengthen Cambodia, which has been a friend for thousands of years, as well as the whole world.
This song is:
The virus has had a devastating effect on humanity, which has been cutting off human-to-human communication, and the virus is contagious, regardless of race, color, religion, or creed. But we stand together to help share knowledge, experience, cooperation and coordination with each other and fight together as a whole to fight the Kovid virus.
Light a candle to encourage frontline workers to donate to the needy and the elderly, be ready to volunteer in any way, we hope you enjoy the interpretation of this song and will be encouraged to continue. Fight together again.
This song is a dedication of the Indian Ministry of Foreign Affairs to the whole world. The ICCR is an autonomous body of the Indian Ministry of Foreign Affairs, which has the authority to raise international awareness and enhance closer cultural ties between India and other countries and demonstrate its power of attraction on international charities.
