Kampong Cham Provincial Governor Continues to Call on People to Take Care of Their Health to Prevent Kovid 19
(Kampong Cham): Mr. Un Chanda, Chairman of Kampong Cham Provincial Anti-Kovid 19 Commission and Governor of Kampong Cham Province, appealed and reminded the people.
Once again, continue to clean up, take care of your health, prevent the spread of Kovid 19, even though the disease situation in Cambodia is now declining.
Mr. Un Chanda made this call on the morning of May 14, 2020, when he met and distributed Ramadan gifts to 460 Cambodian Muslim families in Village 13, Koh Sotin Commune, Koh Sotin District, Kampong Cham Province.
Mr. Un Chanda said that although so far the situation of the 19 cases of Kovid in Cambodia has slightly decreased, and in Kampong Cham province, 16 patients have been cured, but we are still concerned about Outbreaks of Kovid 19 in the second wave as the disease continues to threaten in some parts of the world.
Therefore, on behalf of the Chairman of the Provincial Commission for the Fight against Kovid 19, I would like to call on the people here and in Kampong Cham province as a whole to join together to prevent the spread of Kovid 19 by following the rules of the Ministry of Health as well as health organizations. The world will continue to take care of hygiene, cleanse the body, wash hands regularly and use masks or scarves when coughing or sneezing, and reduce gatherings and travel to other areas.
The provincial governor also requested local authorities at all levels to continue to pay attention to disseminate measures to prevent the spread of Kovid 19 through mobile loudspeakers in cities, towns and districts at commune halls. Churches will be preached in the backyard and in public places.
