The Phnom Penh Municipal Police Commissioner stressed that: "During the implementation of the traffic law, if any officer acts in violation of the instructions of the leadership, the officer will be fined, as well as the implementation of force discipline. On the other hand, the commissioner advised all law enforcement officers to have high patience, have the right attitude and speech with the people.
Lt. Gen. Thet made it clear to all officers that they must set a good example for citizens in obeying traffic laws, must wear helmets, have license plates, wear seat belts and do not talk on the phone while driving (can use headphones) .
