Samdech Preah Boromneath Norodom Sihamoni is the eldest son of Prince Norodom Sihanouk and Queen Norodom Monineath Sihanouk. He has a younger brother, Norodom Norinpong, who died in 2003.
From 1959 to 1962, His Majesty Norodom Sihamoni attended Norodom Primary School, Descartes High School in Phnom Penh. He was then sent by his father to Prague, Czechoslovakia in 1962. There he attended elementary school, high school, and music school, where he studied classical music and dance until 1975.
In 1975, he left Prague to study film in North Korea. In 1977, he returned to Cambodia. The Khmer Rouge, who came to power through the war, immediately detained him in the royal palace with his royal family and his parents.
Before the National Liberation Front liberation army liberated the country from the genocidal regime on January 7, 1979, he fled to Beijing with his parents. He later traveled to Paris to teach ballet and was given the role of president of the Khmer Dance Association.
He lived in France for almost 20 years, but during that time he also traveled frequently to Prague, where he spent much of his youth. He was the only king who had the ability to have Sovanny in the Czech language clearly. In addition to the national language, he has the ability to have Sovanny in French, English and Czech.
The royal name of His Majesty King Norodom Sihamoni is "His Majesty King Norodom Sihamoni has a national village, religion, province, Khemara State, Puthintra Thera, King Khemarajana, Mohapheas, Preah Vihear, Independence, Monarchy, Preah Vihear. The mayor of Cambodia.
It means "Servants of the motherland, religion, nation and people of Cambodia with loyalty and devotion." King supported by Buddha and Indra. You unite all Cambodians. "Defenders of Cambodia's independence, territorial integrity and peace, as well as the happiness, freedom and prosperity of the Cambodian people."
Prior to his accession to the throne, in 1993 he was appointed Cambodian Delegate to UNESCO, headquartered in Paris, France, where he was known for his hard work and devotion to Cambodian culture.
In December 2014, His Majesty King Norodom Sihamoni was awarded the title of "Goddess Thomic Reach" by the International Buddhist Organization at the 6th World Buddhist Congress. This royal title means that the king has the highest virtues as a model in the practice and dissemination of the Buddha's Dharma throughout the world.
During the more than 15 years of his reign, His Majesty King Norodom Sihamoni has given his highest priority to fulfilling his constitutional duties in the service of religion, humanitarianism, education, social welfare and well-being of the people of Cambodia. All over the country, especially in rural areas.
