Minister of Agriculture inspects the progress of the project on joint management to protect and restore the services of wetlands and ecosystems in the Cardamom Mountains
After inspecting the actual supply and use of community pond water, community forestry and vegetable production, Minister Veng Sakhon and the provincial governor and his colleagues met with 50 families.
In a series of get-togethers, Mr. Mon Sam Ath, Community President, Mr. Chheang Tola, Director of the Provincial Department of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, reported on the activities of the community, community forest management, conservation and protection, the benefits of water use, and the benefits of the project. Combined forests and crops, early rainy season cropping, agricultural and forestry community status throughout the province.
In particular, Dr. Nick Beresford also noted the progress of the project, emphasizing the feasibility of water supply and use, alleviating day-to-day problems, facilitating planting, protection and conservation of community forests, improving and conserving forest cover and Agricultural land and especially the livelihoods of community members have been improved.
In addition, in order to transform the community of Rasmei Samaki protected area to grow, maintain the sustainability of protection, maintenance and management of natural forests in this area to increase and increase productivity of crop production, the Minister asked the project director and UNDP to help Training on new agricultural techniques that are resistant to climate change, create additional agricultural activities such as raising chickens, low water crops.
