On May 13, 2020, Mr. Pan Sosak, Minister of Commerce, chaired the meeting of these eight working groups to review and monitor the progress of each working group on policy formulation and negotiation strategy to establish a free trade agreement. This.
The Minister said at the meeting that the preparation of free trade agreements with partner countries is the main task that the Royal Government has entrusted to the Ministry of Commerce to strengthen the competitiveness and diversify Cambodia's trade economy.
Minister Pan Sosak said that this work was set in a conducive environment for the implementation of the Royal Government's Rectangular Strategy Phase 4, which determined that Cambodia's progress was required to continue to strengthen its ability to integrate. In the regional and global economy.
"These integrations are aimed at expanding and opening up markets for exports more widely, based on a permanent free trade agreement, rather than relying on bilateral trade preferences. It could be easy to get lost. ” This is the confirmation of Mr. Pan Sosak.
During the meeting, Mr. Pan Sorsak also expressed his pleasure to see that some of the negotiation and study work that has already begun has yielded satisfactory results, including the negotiation of the Cambodia-China Free Trade Agreement. Possibility of establishing a Cambodia-Korea Free Trade Agreement and discussions with the Eurasian Economic Union.
For the working group that has not yet started its work, the Minister encouraged to start its work as soon as possible, thinking and planning its activities clearly.
Please note that the Free Trade Agreement (FTA) is an agreement between countries that sign the agreement. This agreement will be facilitated with tariff barriers, limiting the amount of goods which can be understood as a free market economy or in the sense of a unified economy.
Free trade agreements are expected to help expand trade between the signatories and also attract investment between the signatories.
Cambodia is currently negotiating with China to sign a free trade agreement as soon as possible. It is expected that after the free trade agreement between Cambodia and China emerges, it will contribute to the expansion of trade volume between the two countries. It is also expected that Cambodia will be able to attract more Chinese investment.
