As an outstanding student, Ms. Borami will graduate with a Bachelor of International Affairs from AUPP at the end of May 2020. She is an outstanding student with a high level of commitment and commitment to her studies and social work.
"I am pleased and thankful for the opportunity to pursue a Master's degree in International Affairs at the LKYU School of Public Policy (LKY SPP)," Borami said in an online interview. "Seeing people around me go through hardships caused by poverty and lack of education motivates me to make a positive difference in my community and country."
She added, “During my summer vacation, I volunteered as an English teacher in the countryside of Cambodia under the auspices of a small NGO where I was able to get a clear picture. "From education in rural communities, especially the problems that occur in those communities."
"That was also the time when I began to expand my interest in rural development beyond education," Borami said. Therefore, I intend to use my academic skills in international economics and development to contribute to solving social problems in Asia. I hope to be able to play a small role in creating positive change for society, focusing on poverty, education and rural development in Cambodia. ”
