Chinese team sprayed 19 Kovidi on 1.5 million square meters in Cambodia during a 15-day mission
(Phnom Penh): A group of 10 volunteer experts from the Blue Sky Rescue Organization of the People's Republic of China completed their 15-day operation to spray Kovid 19 vaccine (COVID-19) in the capitals and provinces. 10 in Cambodia. This mission was carried out at the request of Mr. Kem Rath Viseth, Secretary of State of the Office of the Council of Ministers and Chairman of the Board of the Civil Society Forum (CSF).
The Secretary-General of the Ministry of Health took the opportunity to thank the Ministry of Health and local authorities and all relevant parties for their support and assistance until the end of the spraying operation.
He added: "What we see is that they work hard, no matter how hot or sweaty. We see that our Chinese friend cares so much for us, and all I want to say is that I can't find the words to say it. My heart represents the whole Cambodian people, thank you very much. ”
The head of the mission team in Cambodia, Mr. Vong E, said that during his 15 days in this work, what he noticed was the motivation of the Cambodian people to treat his team as friends, coordinating the work under all circumstances. . He hopes that the Cambodian people will be free from Kovid 19 and safe together.
He said that Cambodia is a good friend of China and his team will help in all circumstances. The team leader promised to return to Cambodia in the event of a disaster or other natural disaster to show encouragement in joining the Cambodian people in the fight against those difficulties.
Mr. Vong E stated, "In particular, I would like to express my appreciation and appreciation to the Royal Government of Cambodia and the people, as we see it as an extension of the good relations between the two nations of our two countries from the leadership to People from urban to rural. At the same time, we continue to encourage Cambodians to continue to work together to fight Kovid 19. Finally, I have a short word that all persevere.
Arrest of a young man on the complaint of the mother of the victim of the case of child torture a year ago
The arrested youth is Thuon Phanna, alias Hon, 34 years old, living in Sangkat Samrong, Samrong City, Oddar Meanchey Province. The victim's mother is Ken Theary, 29 years old, and the victim is 1 year and 7 months old named Phi Veasna. The suspect is the second husband of the victim's mother and the child is the child of the previous husband.
According to the authorities, according to the victim's complaint, this case of torture occurred on April 28, 2019 in Chhouk village, Samrong commune, Samrong city, Oddar Meanchey province. The suspect violently grabbed her son and her ex-husband, who was only seven months old at the time, and severely injured him, breaking his arm and leg.
Although this happened a year ago, the victim only filed a complaint to the authorities on May 19, 2020, with some evidence. Following the filing of the complaint, the Anti-Human Trafficking Office of the Oddar Meanchey Provincial Police arrested Thuon Phanna at around 6 am on May 13, 2020.
Until now, the victim is still under questioning by the authorities.
Two employees of "Sinniv" scratch lottery company were arrested by the police in connection with taking more than 30,000 dollars from the company
(Phnom Penh): Two employees of a scratch lottery company were arrested by the company and handed over to the relevant police for more than 30,000 USD without any payment. This incident happened on the afternoon of May 12, 2020 at the "Sinniv" scratch lottery company on Concrete Road, Group 78, Village 14, Sangkat Tonle Bassac, Khan Chamkarmon.
The first suspect is Prak Cheat, male, 36 years old, a private company lottery employee living in Samhan village, Sangkat Toul Sangke I, Khan Russey Keo, the second suspect is Ath Bunthoeun, male, 21 years old, a private company lottery employee living in Sangkat Kakap I, Khan Por Sen Chey Phnom Penh.
Sal Sandos, chief of the Tonle Bassac Administrative Police Station, said he had received two lottery workers who had been sued by their Chinese boss for taking $ 32,150 from the company.
The two suspects, who are employees of the company, still lacked 29,750 money from May 2019 until now, for only one year, there is still no money to pay, so the company decided to take legal action.
According to the complaint, the suspect was sent to the Chamkar Mon District Inspectorate for legal action.
