Please be informed that Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, on March 30, 2020, issued an order to suspend the export of white rice and rice from 23:59 on March 5, 2020 to ensure Cambodia's food security at a time of crisis 19 for Kovid.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen confirmed that the ban on the export of rice is only white rice and rice, while fragrant rice is allowed to export normally.
Samdech Techo stated that most of Cambodia's white rice and paddy is exported to neighboring countries such as Vietnam and Thailand. However, in order to ensure domestic supply, Cambodia needs to store rice and white rice, which are in high demand in the country, and for fragrant rice, which is small in quantity and low in domestic demand, is still allowed to be exported as usual.
