"Kralan" food in Kampong Chhnang province, there are not many people left to continue this career
(Kampong Chhnang): Kralan is a kind of food that Khmer people like and this kind of food is also left by our ancestors. At present, 3 families living in Trea Tbong village, Sre Thmei commune, Rolea Bier district continue the tradition of burning kralan from their ancestors. Another family abandoned this business a long time ago.
The department is proposing to revitalize this business to strengthen tourism. Three families living in Trea Tbong village, Sre Thmei commune, Rolea Bier district, continue to burn cars to improve their livelihoods in addition to farming, while many other families have given up.
The provincial tourism department has called on them to continue this ancestral business to strengthen the local tourism sector as well as attract national and foreign visitors to visit our village, especially to taste the car food, which is the food of Our ancestors.
Chhon Sokhim, 39, said this morning, May 13, 2020, that she has inherited this property from her parents for 20 years now, burning cars to support her family. He now has six children who depend on farming and grow a small business, burning cars to sell.
In the beginning, there were more than 10 families in Trea Tbong village who started a car-burning business like him, but after they had a comfortable life because their children went abroad to work, they stopped, leaving only three. Only families continue to pursue this career because they get paid to support a decent family.
He said that on average he sells from 60 to 70,000 riel or more per day, sometimes Cambodian expats from abroad order him to burn the car as needed, such as putting a lot of coconuts through the pipe. Long bamboo, etc. They took his car to distribute to other countries such as the United States, France and Australia, because it is known that his car is very delicious.
Please note that kralan is a delicious food, this dish is made with sour rice mixed with red beans and coconut, a little sugar, a little salt, and put in a bamboo tube about 3 to 4 meters long, put it upright and burn it. Just brought to drink. In 8 days, people rushed to make 951 cars in Svay Rieng province after the traffic law was tightened
