Baby dolphin weighing more than 13 kg found dead in Preah Rumkel dolphin canyon, Stung Treng province
(Stung Treng): It is very sad that another Mekong River dolphin died at Preah Rumkel Dolphin Canyon without knowing the cause.
The dolphin is 1 meter long and weighs more than 13 kilograms along the upper Mekong River in Preah Rumkel commune, Borey Ou Svay Sen Chey district, Stung Treng province, near the border with Laos. This is according to the statement of the Preah Rumkel Dolphin Community confirmed to Fresh News Agency in Stung Treng Province on May 13, 2020.
The dead dolphin, 1 meter long and weighing more than 13 kilograms, was found dead at Preah Rumkel Dolphin Canyon at 5:00 pm on May 11, 2020, according to Preah Rumkel Dolphin Community officials. Along the Upper Mekong River in Preah Rumkel commune, Borey Ou Svay Sen Chey district, Stung Treng province, near the border of Laos.
Preah Rumkel dolphin community officials said that the cause of death of the baby dolphin, no one knows the cause. When they came to pick up their dead baby, the professional officers went out to see the dead dolphin.
Please note that this is the third dolphin and died at Preah Rumkel dolphin cave in Preah Rumkel commune, Borey Ou Svay Sen Chey district, Stung Treng province in recent years.
