Court issues arrest warrant for man involved in embezzlement case
(Phnom Penh): The Investigating Judge of the Phnom Penh Municipal Court on the afternoon of May 12, 2020, issued a detention order for 33-year-old Hy Panha alias Top to be remanded in custody pending trial. Sentencing later in accordance with legal procedures.
The decision to detain the accused came after Phnom Penh Municipal Court Prosecutor Soeur Lundy completed his investigation and decided to charge the accused with "breach of trust" (embezzlement). ) Committed at the company named "Fast Investment Trading" located at Building 22, Street 490, Sangkat Phsar Doeum Thkov, Khan Chamkar Mon, Phnom Penh during 2019 under the provisions of Article 391 and Article 392 of the Penal Code.
When there was a suspicion on the part of the company, he sent another employee to meet with the customer, only to find out that Hy Panha had come to collect all the money and show the payment documents.
The company contacted Hy Panha to discuss the collection and did not pay the company. However, the name escaped, so the company filed a complaint with the Phnom Penh Military Police to detain Hy Panha and send him to court for legal action.
According to the suspect's confession, during 2018, he joined Vennova Company in Phsar Doeum Thkov Sangkat, Khan Chamkar Mon, Phnom Penh, as a marketing staff (selling motor oil).
During 2019, when collecting money from customers, he did not pay the company, taking the money to spend a total of $ 13,000, and the company called him to mediate, promising to take The money came to repay the company, but without trust, the company handed itself over to the military police in Chamkarmon district.
