Phnom Penh Military sends suspect to court over breach of trust
(Phnom Penh): The competent authorities of the Criminal Investigation Office of the Phnom Penh Municipal Gendarmerie on the afternoon of May 11, 2020, sent a suspect to court in connection with a case of breach of trust (embezzlement of company money) in 2019.
Hy Panha alias Top, 33 years old, Occupation: Employee of Fast Investment Trading Company, Hometown: Kampong Cham Province, Present address: 193, Street 31BT, Sonsom Kosal 2 Village, Sangkat Boeung Tumpun, Khan Meanchey, Phnom Penh. 2020.
The arrest was made in response to a complaint filed by Lim Sam Oeun, 37, a lawyer representing Fast Investment Trading Company, residing at Building 22, Street 590, Sangkat Phsar Doeum Thkov, Khan Chamkarmon, Phnom Penh.
During 2019, when collecting money from customers, he did not pay the company, taking the money to spend a total of $ 13,000, and the company called him to mediate, promising to take The money came to repay the company, but without trust, the company handed itself over to the military police in Chamkarmon district.
Currently, the above suspects are under the jurisdiction of the Office of Criminal Investigation of the Phnom Penh Municipal Gendarmerie to build a case to be sent to court for legal proceedings.
