The Red Temple during the reign of Jayavarman II on the ridge of Kulen Mountain has just been completed for the first time.
(Siem Reap): The Red Temple, built in the 9th century during the reign of Jayavarman II on Phnom Kulen, has been completed for the first time by experts from the Apsara Authority of the Department of Preservation of Temples Outside Angkor Park under Led by Mr. Chhean Ratha and led by Mr. Puth Soth recently.
For the first renovation, the team excavated the accumulated earth, searched for artefacts and tidied up the bricks and made a drainage slope. Clean the plants, trees that grow on the walls and roof of the temple. Repair cracked walls and repair damaged walls. Repair and strengthen the roof that was intended to fall, repair and re-install the east gate.
Mr. Chhean Ratha said that in the future, the department will propose the second phase of the renovation project, which is to repair the roof, strengthen the structure of the brick foundation for the penis and vagina, and repair the additional art objects found. See around the temple to make the temple strong, long-lasting and research to know more information about this temple.
