APSARA Authority opens 3 more application sites to facilitate the construction requests of the people in the Angkor Park area
(Siem Reap): Three new application centers have just been set up, the first at the former Angkor Tourist Service Center, the second at the Angkor Thom District OWSO, and the third at Banteay Srei. And to facilitate the various construction requests of people living in Angkor Park.
In fact, during the last week of April, APSARA Authority received 52 applications for new construction and renovation, and the specialized team of the Department of Land Management and Housing Management in Angkor Park inspected 24 applications for these constructions. 6 cases to facilitate and prepare the layout for the people, wishing the people to build properly and maintain the Khmer style architecture.
APSARA Authority always pays attention and checks and strengthens its work from the stage of receiving requests to the stage of responding to the people, that is, to make the services of APSARA Authority closer to the people.
In particular, the establishment of application counters in these three areas will alleviate difficulties, reduce time and travel costs.
(Siem Reap): Srah Srang and Banteay Kdei are likely to be the first of Jayavarman VII's royal achievements before the construction of Ta Prohm in 1186.
In the middle of Srah Srang is also a small temple, but it collapsed hundreds of years ago. To date, the Apsara Authority has reopened the temple, which is scheduled to be completed by the end of 2020.
Recently, the team of APSARA Authority found some archeological excavations under the central temple of Srah Srang, including many white or crystals, stone carvings, a large dragon's head, a trident made of metal. Four, one still in good shape and the other remaining only one sharp piece on one side.
Two more turtle statues have also been unearthed, while the team is analyzing further evidence for the origins and causes of these archeological sites.
