New Siem Reap Angkor International Airport to be Completed in 2023
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Lu Wei, Chairman of the Board of Directors of the Siem Reap Angkor Thmey International Airport (AIAI) Construction Company, confirmed to Mr. Mao Ha Vannal, Minister in Charge of the Secretariat of State for Civil Aviation, on 11 May 2020 that Siem Reap International Airport Angkor Thmey will be completed in 2023.
This assertion was made on the occasion of Mr. Louie's courtesy call and discussion with General Dr. Mao Havannal at the Secretariat of State for Civil Aviation.
During the meeting, Mr. Louie reported on the progress of the construction of the new Siem Reap Angkor International Airport that the company has now started the construction of the new Siem Reap International Airport since March 15, 2020 and plans to complete the construction. Completed on March 14, 2023, using a total time of 36 months.
He said that the construction process of the company worked closely with the technical team of the Secretariat of Civil Aviation, focusing on the technical equipment and layout of the airport.
General Dr. Mao Havanal confirmed that on behalf of the leadership of the Secretariat of State for Civil Aviation, we always fully support and promote the construction of the new Siem Reap International Airport as planned.
The Minister urged and agreed that the construction company of Siem Reap Angkor International Airport (AIAI) and the technical working group of the Secretariat of State for Civil Aviation would work together on a regular basis to review the work, challenges and solutions, and to hold daily meetings on the 25th of every month. Review the progress of technical work and construction of the airport.
At the same time, Mr. Louvy respectfully invited Minister Mao Havannal to visit and inspect the construction work at an appropriate time in the near future.
Please be informed that the new Siem Reap Airport is an investment by the Chinese company Yunnan with more than 980 million dollars, located in Tayek commune, Sot Nikum district on an area of 1,700 hectares.
