Banteay Meanchey Provincial Governor Presides Over the Groundbreaking Ceremony for 3 Rubber Roads in Mongkul Borey District
(Banteay Meanchey): Mr. Ou Rathrey, Governor of Banteay Meanchey Province, on May 11, 2020, accompanied by Mr. Rath Dasinang, Governor of Mongkul Borei District, authorities, government officials and local authorities inaugurated the construction site of 3 rubber roads in Mongkul Borei district.
The construction of these 3 roads includes: Road in Neang Ket village, Russey Krok commune, 1 line, 1636 meters long, paved with rubber and 2,000 meters long, connected to Bat Trang commune, paved with red gravel, the second line from Samrong village, connected to the village Anchanh, Russey commune, 2440 meters long, paved with rubber, and another line from Chumteav village, connected to Talom commune, 2,000 meters long, paved with rubber.
Mr. Ou Rath said that the Royal Government of Cambodia, as well as the provincial authorities, together with the relevant units, have made efforts to serve and solve local problems as a high priority.
He said that under the leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia has considered the road as a high priority area is important and has been gradually changing from a dirt road to a paved road and is changing to pour. Rubber or concrete in accordance with the strategic principles of the Royal Government, so the road is an important economic artery for the benefit of the people, society, there is a path of hope and prosperity.
Finally, the provincial governor instructed the people to cooperate, such as cutting down trees to make the road wider, and also forbidding trucks to pass through to avoid damage to the road.
In opening the road construction site, Mr. Ouk Kanha distributed one sarong to each participant.
