(Battambang): Police in Battambang province on the morning of May 11, 2020, sent the suspect with more than 1 kg of drugs to the provincial court after the police arrested for actual crimes at 15:45 pm May 10, 2020 at the rented house, Group 6, Watkor village, Watkor commune, Battambang city, Battambang province.
Lt. Col. Sok Nimol, Director of the Anti-Drug Police Office, said that the suspect who was detained by the police was named Ly Issa, alias Pov, male, 32 years old, living in a rented house in Group 6, Wat Kor Village / Sangkat, Battambang City, and confiscated the following exhibits: 15 bags of ice equal to 1,027.57 grams, a motorcycle and some other equipment.
The director of the office confirmed that after the suspect confessed, Major General Ouch Sokhon, the provincial police commissioner, ordered the specialized office to build a case file and send the suspect and the evidence to the provincial court for legal action.
