General Neth Savoeun strictly forbids the police to stop the driver to check the documents, except for the actual crime (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): General Neth Savoeun, the National Police Commissioner General, has strictly ordered the officers not to stop The traffic police summoned or detained the drivers of all types of vehicles to check the documents, except for the actual offenses specified in the new sub-decree.
This was confirmed by General Him Yan, Deputy Commissioner General of the National Police, to the media after the meeting to disseminate measures to strengthen the implementation of the law on road traffic on the morning of May 11, 2020.
The meeting was held at the General Commission of the National Police with the participation of the Deputy Commissioner, the Capital-Provincial Commissioner, the Deputy Commissioner for Traffic.
General HIM Yan stated that "This case has been clearly instructed by His Excellency the General of the National Police, following the recommendation of Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng, that all vehicles to be inspected are vehicles that have violated the law." " We will not allow any detention if no specific crime is found."
At this point, General Him Yan emphasized that if there is any crime and is detained by the authorities, the authorities have the right to inspect the various documents required by law. If the driver lacks a place to be fined, the traffic police officer will add up the offense and fine all at once.
According to General Him Yan, during the meeting, General Dr. Neth Savoeun set out eight directions for further implementation, including command, patrol and day-to-day monitoring. That this work must be done seriously and responsibly.
Gen. Dr. Neth Savoeun also affirmed that the enforcement of the law on road traffic must be further strengthened until the reduction of traffic accidents and the adherence to the law and ensure order. And road safety order throughout the country.
It is noteworthy that the vast majority of road users across the country have actively participated in the implementation of the law on road traffic, which reflects the rule of law and is a source of encouragement for law enforcement forces to continue to perform their duties more actively. More than before.
