(Ratanakkiri): On May 10, 2020, 75 people with 40 motorbikes rushed to set fire to two Vorachey National Park posts at O'Lapong point in Ta Bok village, Ta Veng Leu commune. Ta Veng District, Rattanakiri Province.
The same source said that due to resentment with the park rangers, they gathered nearly 100 people to burn the Vorachey National Park headquarters. Damaged items include: 1 bag of rice, 6 pots, 4 hammocks, 1 battery, 3 water tanks, 2 wooden planks.
The following is a detailed explanation of the Ministry of Tourism:
Krouch Chhmar district is located along the Mekong River in Tbong Khmum province, most of the people are engaged in fishing and farming. Every day, the people there bring fish, vegetables, fruits to sell at the market in Stung Trang district, Kampong Cham province, traveling by small boat, boat, and for the last 3 years, there is a ferry to help copy instead.
Ms. Chrech Saem is a resident of Kdol Kandal village, Trea commune, Krouch Chhmar district since her ancestors. She describes her homeland as an isolated island separated by a large river. The 43-year-old shopkeeper added that because her district is far from the Kizuna Bridge, locals often travel across the Mekong River in small boats.
In addition to the risks, boating also costs a lot of money, leading to an increase in the cost of bringing goods to market, causing people to lose income. Not only that, if people travel across the river and do not return, they have to charter a boat to travel back home, which costs an additional 60,000, otherwise people are forced to rest on the other side and wait. In the morning, there are passengers passing by.
Mr. Chhin Hor Chea described that the construction of the Cambodia-China Stung Trang-Krouch Chhmar Friendship Bridge is not difficult compared to the other three bridges across the river that the company has already built. However, the Stung Trang-Kroch Chhmar bridge has to have a foundation pillar deeper than the previous three bridges, with a depth of up to 103 meters, because the riverbed in that area has a lot of sand.
Mr. Chhin Hor Chea also claimed that attention is paid to the construction of this bridge to ensure long-lasting and strong quality. To ensure the quality of the bridge, the company's engineers, as well as representatives of the Ministry of Public Works and consulting companies, regularly inspect the construction process once a month.
Currently, the Stung Trang-Kroch Chhmar bridge is more than halfway down the river, and one can see the shape of the bridge standing firmly on the river gradually. The people of Stung Trang and Kroch Chhmar, who take the ferry across the Mekong River, often look at the bridges that have never been on their land.
The presence of the Stung Trang-Kroch Chhmar bridge has made the people who used to have difficulty in childbirth very excited, some even excited to tears. The people of Stung Trang and Kroch Chhmar districts consider the bridge as a great achievement for their life. In particular, they expect the bridge to contribute to a better life.
Ms. Chrech Saem: “Thank you to our Cambodian government for its efforts to build the nation and ask for help from China to help build a bridge across me. I am very happy, the villagers are all happy. "Thanks to the prince and the Chinese government for their cooperation, this bridge was built across Kroch Chhmar district."
Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng Donates a 3-hectare Pond for Storing Water in the Dry Season in Koas Kralor District
(Battambang): A joint working group of Battambang Provincial Administration led by Mr. Nguon Rattanak inspected the excavation of a giant pond of 3 hectares in Koas Kralor district, which was donated by Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng, Deputy Prime Minister of the Ministry of Interior. Up for storage of water for use in the dry season.
The inspection of the canal excavation on May 10, 2020, accompanied by the Deputy Governor, Advisor Samdech Krala Hom, Director of the Department, local authorities and other officials.
Mr. Mao Sochan, Governor of Koas Kralor District, said that in Koas Kralor District, there are 6 communes, of which 5 communes are always short of water during the dry season, including Hop Commune, Chna Moan Commune, Daun Ba Commune. Koas Kralor and Preah Phos communes, as these communes also have a difficult commune to bring water through the canal system for people to use, must pump continuously because those communes in the high hills far from the main canal.
Mr. Mao Sochan added that about 5,000 families in Koas Kralor district, Battambang province, more than 20,000 people in the dry season, always face the risk of lack of water for daily use, and they also The water transport authority to distribute and intervene to bring water from various sources pumped for use in the past.
Taking the opportunity to inspect the pond, Mr. Nguon Rattanak urged the authorities of Koas Kralor district to speed up the excavation of this pond as soon as possible in June 2020 to bring the rainy season rainwater into Samdech Krala Hom Lake for use in the dry season. In the future, for the benefit of the people, use it daily so that they do not have the same difficulties as in the past.
After inspecting the excavation of the lake, Mr. Nguon Rattanak and the accompanying delegation inspected the performance of the working group by measuring and verifying the land dispute data as a basis for resolving land disputes in Chhnal Moan and Preah Phos communes. Some food items, as well as the budget to the team of land surveyors. SATHAPANA Bank announces the launch of an online bank account by creating a mobile banking application!
(Phnom Penh): SATHAPANA Bank on May 11, 2020, officially launched the online banking account creation service through the mobile banking application, and this program will make setting up a bank account with SATHAPANA Bank more convenient. Another level of convenience, as customers can create a bank account in just 2 minutes through Sathapana Bank's mobile banking application.
In just a few minutes, customers can also open a bank account and start using SATHAPANA Bank's banking services such as bill payment, local and international money transfer, money transfer to partners such as Wing Pay Petronium. Ly Hour, Money, Money and Bakong and many other services.
With an online banking account, customers can make transactions for up to $ 250 per transaction, but customers can easily convert this type of account into an account that can transact with a larger amount by simply going to any SATHAPANA Bank branch. Also among more than 170 branches throughout the Kingdom of Cambodia and comes with a mobile phone used when opening an online account, as well as an identity card or passport.
In addition, from May 13, Sathapana Bank will offer customers a new option, which is to open a bank account through face-to-face meetings with Sathapana Bank staff who will visit the customer's home or office. To open a bank account and be able to operate immediately.
It should be noted that SATHAPANA Bank is one of the leading commercial banks in the Kingdom of Cambodia with total assets of over 1.7 billion US dollars and more than 4,000 employees. SATHAPANA Bank has the second largest branch network with more than 170 branches and more than 220 ATMs with full capacity such as deposit, withdrawal and payment.
