Ministry of Health: Cambodia has spent more than 7 million dollars to buy equipment to fight against Kovid 19 (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): Ms. Youk Sambath, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Health confirmed that currently Cambodia has spent more than 7 million dollars to Purchased 19 anti-Kovid weapons and had $ 5,900,000 in his bank account.
Ms. Youk Sambath made this statement when she was invited as a speaker at a press conference on "Current 19 Kovid Diseases in Cambodia" in the presence of Dr. Mam Bunheng, Minister of Health.
She said that for the equipment, there are 2 warehouses for storage, and at present, the materials in the Samdech Techo Strategic Warehouse on National Road 6A, we have managed all the materials, including 13,500 ordinary masses. 1,000 masks, 695,000 N95 masks, 5,000 PPE garments, and 5,000 blankets, blankets, mats, all of which are in stock in stock, as well as strategic supplies.
