(Phnom Penh): As of the beginning of May 2020, the Royal Government of Cambodia has not yet restored all types of educational institutions, which makes the private education sector in Cambodia has been trying to find ways to improve the quality of education. At the time, Kovid 19 was spreading across the country and the world.
"The purpose of this collaboration is not only to improve the quality of online education for students during the 19 crisis, but also to improve the quality of education for students," said Peck Bolen, WEG CEO. It also provides benefits for the preparation of modern education and methods of learning and teaching in the future.
He added that the benefits of this cooperation include:
1: Edemy: Digital classes and online learning. Students can watch video lessons, read lesson texts, evaluate homework or homework on their own, track their own learning process, increase teacher-student communication effectively.
2: Maxbit: Online learning and online business advice to parents can help improve their parents' business, and schools can adapt to modern teaching tools more effectively.
3: VConnect: VConnect Smart School Management System helps parents and schools communicate more effectively, including managing their students' learning.
4: DTP (DTP): e-library and digital learning program. Parents and students can use home study programs to improve their English language skills.
