If we apply the principle of autonomy to individuals, such mutual assistance is considered illegal. For this reason, as an exception to the principle of autonomy of the private sector, the Civil Code of the Kingdom of Cambodia provides that it is illegal to interfere in the affairs of others, which the law defines as "painful administration." "
What is pain management? Therefore, in order to better understand the meaning of pain management, Fresh News' legal awareness program in collaboration with the Cambodian Bar Association for International Cooperation would like to raise the topic of "pain management" to explain and share with you. All students are as follows:
In the spirit of Article 729 of the Civil Code, it is defined that "initiating the management of affairs for the sake of another person or interfering in the affairs of others by unauthorized assistance is" painful management. " Individuals who perform pain management are called pain managers. In other words, in order for that action to be painfully controlled, the manager needs to be willing to manage that activity for the benefit of others.
In the event that the person in control of the trauma is unwilling to manage, that control activity is not considered traumatic and the manager will not be able to claim a refund for the cost of management.
If the manager fails to perform the management duties carefully as an honest manager, the management action is considered illegal and the manager is liable for compensation for damages caused by failure. That. In other words, the task of managing carefully as an honest manager means managing the work with high attention.
In short, painful management is the action of others who have helped each other in a sense of solidarity, no matter what the circumstances, as long as the help or management is most appropriate. In particular, individuals who perform pain management operations must be honest and sincere.
(Tbong Khmum): The 7-day Merit Ceremony dedicated to Kosal Phal, the funeral of the late Duke Prit Moha Upasika Vivathana Bun Seangly, ended this Sunday morning, May 10, 2020.
This morning's ceremony was held in accordance with the Buddhist tradition of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, and Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen and relatives, as well as children and grandchildren. The monk gave birth to a child. After that, 96 monks were invited to dedicate to the soul of the late Duke Prit Moha Upasika Dhammhanavivathana.
After holding the ceremony for two nights and three days, with the invitation of national and international guests, leaders of ministries, institutions and ambassadors, ambassadors and close relatives Buried in his hometown in the second village, Rokar Knor commune, Krouch Chhmar district, Tbong Khmum province on May 6, 2020.
In order to dedicate the festival to the mother, child, mother and grandmother, Samdech Techo and Samdech Kittipritthbandit, as well as relatives, children, son-in-law, grandchildren and great-grandchildren, organized the ceremony according to the traditional Khmer Buddhism. Invite monks to recite the bowls continuously until the 7-day festival plan on Saturday, May 9th.
On the afternoon of May 9, 2020, the 7-day anniversary of the death of Duke Prith Moha Upasika Dhammhanavivathana, Samdech Techo and Samdech Kittipritthbandit, as well as their children and grandchildren, unanimously agreed to celebrate the festival. 7-day nursing devotion to the soul of Duke Prit Moha Upasika Thommanhan Vivathana Bun Seangly.
In this religious ceremony, the children, daughters-in-law, grandchildren and great-grandchildren were invited by Samdech Preah Reachea Kanhak 9 and the monks to light the fire of Chamroeun Preah Berit, recite the Preah Ratanatray and give a sermon under the leadership of Duke Pheakdey Preah Sdach Heng Kim Kun Cult and Religion of the Royal Palace.
The religious ceremony, which took place in the home village of Duke Prit Moha Upasika Thomman Vivathana in Village 2, Rokar Khnor Commune, Krouch Chhmar District, Tbong Khmum Province, was also attended by Samdech, Ladies and Gentlemen, senior dignitaries representing all institutions of God. The Kingdom of Cambodia, relatives of all the families of the Duke, the Supreme Master Ching Hai, many evolutionary monks.
In that religious ceremony, Samdech Preah Vorn Rath Noy Chrek, the second Deputy Prime Minister of the Kingdom of Cambodia, delivered a sermon on the 7-day Merit Ceremony.
A sermon on the merits of breast milk, the price of the mother is invaluable in that the mother is merciful, gives birth, cares for and nurtures her children from birth to adulthood, has a high livelihood. High face in society. Samdech Preah Vanrath's sermon expressed the value of expensive breast milk that both of you are grateful for, parents who are grateful as a field that all children can not reciprocate to you who are grateful parents.
Samdech Preah Van Rath also wished the great sage to the body of the corpse of the Duke, Priest Moha Upasika Dhammhanavivathana, referring to the heavenly paradise without any hesitation. In particular, he escaped from all the misery while the Duke, the Supreme Disciple, and the Vipassana Dharma were still alive.
Father's name is Ok Bun, mother's name is Nai Houy. Neak Oknha Prit Moha Upasika Thommanhan Vivathana is the second daughter of four siblings, including three girls and one boy. When he was a child, the Duke of the Supreme Master Ching Hai Vivathana Bun Seangly did not go to school, and he spent his youth to help his parents in the family farm work.
At a young age, Duke Prit Maha Upasika Dhammanyan Vivathana, a Buddhist full of generosity, contributed to the construction of many achievements for the benefit of Buddhism. In addition to being a great supporter of Buddhism, Duke Prit Moha Upasika Dhammhanavivathana has also participated in many humanitarian activities in society.
The death of Oknha Prit Moha Upasika Thommanhan Vivathana Bunseangly is also the loss of a pious and loving mother-in-law who nurtured, cared for, cared for and provided for the family as well as provided education and guidance. Good people make their children good citizens, intellectuals and top leaders of Cambodia, bring peace, stability and development, which is an indispensable principle for the nation and people of Cambodia.
