(Stung Treng): Police Inspectorate of Siem Pang District, Stung Treng Province launched an operation to crack down on drug trafficking and illegal possession of two consecutive cases of the same crime on May 9 and 10, 2020. .
The first case took place at Nhang Som village, Sekong commune, Siem Pang district, and the second case at Hang Koban village, Samaki commune, Stung Treng city. This is according to the report of the Anti-Drug Office of Stung Treng Provincial Police, which was obtained by Fresh News.
According to the report, in the first case, the police confiscated 6 small packages of methamphetamine, Ice powder, weighing 1.74 grams, and arrested one suspect, Bang Sokea. Male, 41 years old, Nationality Khmer, Occupation Farmer, Residing in Nhang Som Village, Sekong Commune, Siem Pang District at 13:05 on May 09, 2020.
According to the police, the second case was cracked down after the confession of the suspect Bang Sokea on the morning of May 10, the police continued to search the house of Sok Chivin, male, 40 years old, a salesman. In Hang Koban village, Samaki commune, Stung Treng city. In that case, the police found 2 more packages of methamphetamine (Ice) weighing 3.67 grams.
According to the report, the suspect, Sok Chivin, was an old subject who had been besieged three times by the police, but the police could not crack down, as the perpetrators used drones to monitor the activities of the police. This is why the authorities can not separate the case. So far, based on the confession of the accomplice and the evidence of the actual crime, the police have arrested the suspect.
