He also advised them that if there is a lack of funds to expand farming, Deputy Prime Minister Ke Kim Yan and she has set up a fund to help those who want to expand farming can get a loan with the lowest interest rate to help farmers.
Om Srey Mak Salim, 44, a frog farmer in Kantuot village, Phneat commune, Serey Sophorn city, said she started raising frogs five years ago. Raising to this day, which makes his life better, has a budget for his children to study.
Um Srey said that she currently raises 20 frogs, each of which contains more than 1,000 frogs, for a total of more than 20,000 frogs. For the market, he sells locally and out of the province by order. And this breeding is necessary to change the water regularly, otherwise the sewage affects the frogs in the veil.
Mr. Huot Saveth, Phneat commune chief, confirmed that most of the people in Phneat commune, in addition to farming, grow vegetables to support their families as well as sell at the city market. There are 47 families raising frogs in Phneat commune.
