Samdech Sar Kheng announces further implementation of measures to tighten traffic law enforcement after seeing a decrease in traffic accidents (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng, Deputy Prime Minister, Minister of Interior and Chairman of the National Road Safety Committee Note that a week of implementation of measures to tighten the enforcement of road traffic laws has significantly reduced the rate of traffic accidents in Cambodia.
Through the Facebook page on May 9, 2020, Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng expressed his deep gratitude to the people who participated in respecting the implementation of the road traffic law. Samdech also thanked the competent forces as well as all relevant officials who performed their duties well.
Samdech Krala Hom also thanked the people who sent messages and comments on Samdech's Facebook page, which are all messages and comments with content to build and improve.
Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng encouraged people to continue to provide constructive opinions and improve in order to continue to better implement the road traffic law. Samdech said that the better implementation of the road traffic law will reduce the rate of traffic accidents, the number of fatalities will be less, public order will be better for the country and civilized people.
It should be noted that the Royal Government of Cambodia started to introduce measures to restrict the implementation of the road traffic law with high fines to help reduce the rate of traffic accidents and bring order to the streets on May 1, 2020.
On May 08, Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng also led a member of the National Road Safety Committee to review the results of the implementation of measures to restrict the implementation of this traffic law.
During the meeting, the National Road Safety Committee said that as a result of the implementation of measures to tighten the enforcement of the road traffic law for a week, the road traffic police inspected the offense and fined the offending vehicle. A total of 13,968 cases, including 10,815 cases of vehicles and tricycles, equivalent to 77%, and 3,153 cases of all types of vehicles and 23%.
The report also shows that traffic conditions have improved. During the week, there were 43 traffic accidents, a decrease of 52 times, or 54 percent compared to the same period in May 2019. In the 43 traffic accidents, 24 people were killed, a decrease of 16 people or 40%, and 56 people were injured, a decrease of 59 people.
In particular, compared to the last week of April 2020, the rate of traffic accidents during the tightening of traffic law enforcement this week decreased 12 times or 22%, of which 11 deaths decreased by 31 The percentage of casualties decreased by 2 to 3%.
The National Road Safety Committee report notes that the vast majority of road users across the country have actively participated in the implementation of the Road Traffic Law, which reflects the rule of law and is a source of encouragement to the forces. Law enforcement has the spirit to continue to perform its duties more actively.
The National Road Safety Committee also emphasized that the enforcement of the law on road traffic is to protect the body, life and property of all citizens, as well as to promote the honor, dignity and morality of the society.
This measure is the best option among the other priority measures that the Royal Government has set to reduce traffic accidents that often result in people with disabilities losing their lives and property damage due to traffic or road use. Obey the road traffic law.
The National Committee for Road Safety also stated that the Royal Government has always paid attention and is concerned about the aftermath of traffic accidents that have occurred in the past and did not intend to demand fines from any citizen. We want the people to have a prosperous life and security for everyone, including traffic.
The National Road Safety Committee emphasized that the Road Traffic Law Enforcement Force will continue to strictly enforce the Road Traffic Law in a strict and professional manner.
