Mr. Duong Dara and Governor of Kampot Province Hand over the Royal Decree of Khmer Nationality to American Mr. Tom alias Sen Samnang
(Kampot): The Kampot Provincial Administration has issued a Royal Decree granting Cambodian citizenship to an American named O'Brien Enz Allen, alias Tom, who has the right to reside and reside in Cambodia.
The handing over and receiving of the Royal Decree took place on the afternoon of May 8, 2020 at the Kampot Provincial Hall in the presence of Mr. Chiao Tay, Provincial Governor and Mr. Duong Dara, Personal Assistant to Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia and Deputy The Secretary of State of the Office of the Council of Ministers, as well as the presence of the Deputy Governors, leaders of units under the provincial hall and relevant local authorities.
Along with this ceremony, the Kampot Provincial Administration also provided relevant documents on the land tenure rights belonging to Mr. Bryan Allen alias (Tom) or alias Sen Samnang, which has six locations in Kampot Province.
Mr. Duong Dara, Samdech Techo Hun Sen's personal assistant, stated that in accordance with the instructions of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, who has always considered the United States as a good friend of Cambodia. And in the case of Mr. Tom in the past, there has been abuse from business partners together and there is a solution to find justice according to the principle of win-win, which this solution is highly appreciated and supported by Samdech Techo.
Mr. Duong Dara also expressed his hope that from now on, Mr. Tom will work in accordance with the laws of Cambodia, and where there is a shortage, he hopes that the Kampot provincial administration will facilitate to make Mr. Tom's life in Cambodia. We are all well.
Mr. Tom also thanked Samdech Techo Hun Sen for helping to find justice and granting Cambodian citizenship for the right to live legally in Cambodia, the land he loved with all his heart for the rest of his life.
