ADB plans to provide $ 1.3 billion to Cambodia to meet Cambodia's development needs from 2021-2023
Mr. Vongsey Visoth said that in the context of the spread of Kovid-19, the Royal Government has given high priority to the fight against Kovid-19 to prevent the transmission, transmission and protection of people's lives. . In fact, the number of infections is only 122, most of which are imported or from external sources, and a small number are transmitted to local people.
At the same time, the Royal Government focuses on interventions to stabilize the living standards of the people, especially for the poor and vulnerable, as well as the unemployed, through the introduction of policies and assistance programs. Society, the continued implementation of labor cash projects and the organization of soft skills training and the provision of workers' allowances when factories suspend business.
In addition, the Royal Government has put in place a number of practical measures to ensure that all ongoing development programs and projects and a list of new proposed projects are implemented in a timely and efficient manner to support and support recovery. Of the Cambodian economy during and after the end of the crisis.
He also mentioned that the Ministry of Economy and Finance has been currently preparing a draft plan for economic stimulus based on the evolving situation and four main principles:
* First: Global trends after the Kovid-19 crisis * Second: Identifying and selecting areas of high priority and potential * Third: Deep and realistic structural reforms * Fourth: Increasing budget expenditures More and more efficient by increasing the volume of borrowing from both development partners and by issuing local bonds in the future.
He stressed that Cambodia still has room for new borrowing because all of Cambodia's key debt ratios are still low compared to international benchmark ratios.
He said that this program / development project and technical assistance is partly the result of a comprehensive discussion between ministries, institutions of the Royal Government and ADB on March 6, 2020 and partly a request. Of the Royal Government urgently and the recent developments of Cambodia itself.
It should be noted that through the Program / Development and Technical Assistance (COBP) 2021-2023, ADB plans to provide about 1.3 billion US dollars, which will actively contribute to the implementation of the partnership strategy. For the development of Cambodia, ADB 2019-2023 was successful as well as to meet the needs of Cambodia's development.
Including co-financing from various development partners, as well as the contribution of the Royal Government, ADB's 2021-2023 Development Program / Technical Assistance Program / Technical Assistance, amounting to approximately US $ 1.5 billion.
Once again, Mr. Vongsey Visoth thanked the ADB for its trust and confidence in the leadership of the Royal Government of Cambodia by approving more and more cooperative financing for development in Cambodia. Time at Cambodia's request, which will greatly contribute to the development of Cambodia, aims to revitalize the Cambodian economy in the context of Kovid-19 disease.
From 1992 to the present, ADB has provided co-financing to Cambodia for development projects totaling approximately US $ 3,485 million, of which approximately US $ 2,983 million in concessional loans and grants. About $ 502 million.
