Australia's three-step plan to reopen economy and lift social restrictions after COVID-19 calms down
Morrison announced the plan on Friday after a meeting with government leaders of states and territories in Australia. According to the Australian Prime Minister, the country's economic activity is expected to return to full operation in July, and the governments of the states and territories of Australia will decide when each step of the plan takes effect. .
Mr Morrison said that under the first phase of the national economic recovery plan, restaurants and cafes would be allowed to reopen and Australians would be allowed up to five home visitors. And can meet up to 10 people in public.
In addition, by the second stage, the maximum number of gatherings will be increased to 20, and cross-state travel in some form will be allowed, as well as gyms, cinemas, art exhibition centers and beauty salons. Will be allowed to open the door. Upon reaching the third and final step, all cross-state travel will be allowed, plus an increase in the number of gatherings to 100 and the reopening of the bar.
