Pailin Governor Urges Law Enforcement Officials to Eliminate Law Enforcement Inaction
(Pailin): Mr. Phan Chanthul, Governor of Pailin Province and Chairman of the Provincial Unity Command, instructed all forces to eliminate all inactivity, especially traffic police officers to implement the new traffic law to be polite with the people. Citizens, however, must be firm before the law in order for law enforcement to be effective to ensure the safety and public order on the streets for the people.
Mr. Phan Chanthul made such a call on May 7, 2020, yesterday at the handover ceremony of the Pailin Provincial Police.
"We are law enforcement officers, so we must strictly respect the discipline of the forces to become a model officer with a good work ethic, responding to all current job requests, especially to strengthen good cooperation," he said. With authorities at all levels, taking the law as the basis and being fair and impartial to the people.
