The Criminal Police Department has arrested a man posing as a two-star police officer at the Ministry of Interior for threatening to kill, threatening to defame, using a weapon illegally and defrauding. The suspect was arrested on May 4, 2020 in Sangkat Chroy Changva, Khan Chroy Changva, Phnom Penh.
The arrest was also mediated by Mr. Keo Sothea, Prosecutor of the Phnom Penh Municipal Court.
The suspect confessed that he had indeed disguised himself as a two-star national police officer at the Ministry of Interior and took $ 10,500 from the victim to run for the National Police, but was unable to do so. When the victim called to ask for money, he sent a threatening death message if he continued to ask for money. On May 4, 2020, he was arrested along with a Glock 26 handgun without a license.
General Sao Sokha and Donors Donate Nearly 800 Large Solar Lighting Lamps to Romeas Hek District Administration in Svay Rieng Province
(Svay Rieng): In order to improve the beauty of Romeas Hek district, Svay Rieng province to be more attractive, Mr. Sao Sokha, Chairman of the working group of the Cambodian People's Party to help Romeas Hek district, supported 300 large solar light poles to illuminate both sides of public roads at The district, which has never existed before, also has the support of philanthropists to provide an additional 498 light poles to the district administration to address the main goals.
Mr. Sumol, Governor of Romeas Hek District, told Fresh News Agency in Svay Rieng Province this morning, May 8, with the high attention of Mr. Sao Sokha as the Chairman of the Working Group to make the district development. The team leader also supported the improvement of the aesthetics of the district to be attractive and have lighting at night.
Mr. Soumol confirmed that 300 high wattage solar light poles were donated by Mr. Sao Sokha and also supported 498 ordinary light poles from a total of 798 light poles to the district administration to be placed on both sides of the road. Important public places such as: commune halls, markets, schools, health centers, inspectors, district halls, etc.
He added that the Romeas Hek District Administration is proud to have received many new achievements in addition to many other achievements, and on behalf of the people of Romeas Hek District, would like to express his deep gratitude to Mr. Sao Sokha for supporting the district administration and Thank you to all the philanthropists who have cooperated and provided funds and other materials to support all district development projects.
