On the morning of May 08, 2020, Samdech Techo, the head of the Royal Government of Cambodia, through Facebook, reminded the Cambodian people to continue to pay attention to health care, especially not to neglect the spread of Kovid 19 disease.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen warned, "Even though the rate of 19 cases of Kovid has been reduced in our country and the rate of treatment of this patient has been reduced to two, we must not be negligent. And think lightly that the disease is okay in Cambodia or think that Cambodia is a hot country is not contagious is not so. "Because this disease is a vicious disease and can be transmitted from one person to another very quickly."
Samdech Techo added that so far, both Cambodia and the world are working together to fight Kovid 19 and no cure has yet been found. So this deadly disease continues to plague the lives of people all over the world, with a large number of countries still shutting down their countries.
Samdech Techo reminded people in the capital and in the provinces to continue to wear masks or scarves and wash their hands with alcohol or cleansing gel to get rid of germs and bacteria on a regular basis to avoid infection from one person to another One that brings regret for a lifetime.
It should be noted that as of this morning, May 08, 2020, Cambodia has only 19 patients with Kovid, only two more are recovering while 120 patients have been cured. For more than three weeks, Cambodia has had no new 19 cases of Kovid.
Although Cambodia has no new cases, the global epidemic has not slowed down and remains acute.
Health officials have warned that Kovid 19 has not yet been eradicated and could be transmitted at any time. Experts called on people to remain vigilant and continue to follow the rules recommended by the Ministry of Health.
