Takhmao residents request authorities to strengthen sand spill on Street 21A and large drivers to be effective
(Kandal): Residents of Takhmao City, especially those traveling on National Road 21A, complained that the sand trucks and land transporters were very arrogant and that the sand always spilled on the road, causing dust to enter the eyes and nose. And cause them great anger.
Through Fresh News Agency, on May 8, the people requested the Kandal Provincial Authority to have Mr. Ney Chary as the Deputy Governor in charge, Mr. Chea Sarith, Director of the Department of Mines and Energy, Mr. Ven Sovin, Deputy Commissioner for Traffic Planning. , Mr. Moeung Youleng, Director of the Department of Public Works and Transport, and especially requested the Governor of Takhmao, Mr. Nou Sovannara to take action for this for the environment and for traffic safety.
Residents added that they did not dare to reject the word 'development' and applauded the development without fail, but the important thing is to respect the law and ask law enforcement to work thoroughly and clearly. Avoid debt, which leads to inefficient work.
"Of course, our society is a developing society and law enforcement needs to be effective as traffic restrictions have been in place, but big trucks are less likely to use metal fists," he said. "It's up to the people, which makes them wonder and expect that the group of relevant authorities is no longer a 10-foot official." Citizens confirm.
"Unfortunately, Takhmao is a clean ASEAN tourist city, but it has lost its reputation because of violators and law enforcers who ignore it," he said. "People are optimistic that things will get better in the future if there is a solution."
Regarding this issue, Mr. Chea Sarith, Director of the Department of Mines and Energy of Kandal Province, said by telephone that he should first go through the management and not visit by himself.
Regarding the above case, Mr. Heng Chanthuon, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Mines and Energy, told through Watsapp that the sand depot is controlled by the provincial authority, while the transportation is not clean, the road is not covered, the implementation of Circular No. 03/10 of the Ministry of Mines is suspended. He does business for one week, the first time, the second time, if there is a third time, the ministry will cancel the sand depot license.
According to the report, there are more than 10 sand depots on Street 21A in Takhmao City, and each depot has a powerful owner and a lot of merit, so they are not afraid of the provincial authorities or relevant authorities. While it is known that some people receive religious rewards in exchange for the smooth running of the business and without any distractions.
