(Tbong Khmum): During the construction of the flagpole to dedicate the merit to the Duke of the Supreme Disciple Vivathana Bun Seangly, who is the grandmother, Venerable Hun Manet, this morning, May 08, 2020, continued to visit Ben Bat in the village In his hometown with other monks as usual.
This is the second day of the veneration of Venerable Hun Manet after the construction of the front of the fire as a priest for the Venerable's grandmother who passed away recently. According to several photos obtained by Fresh News, it was observed that during the Ben Bat ceremony in Venerable Hun Manet's hometown, a large number of Buddhists came out to offer food to the Venerable and many monks. .
According to the plan, Venerable Hun Manet can build a shrine in 7 days, which is a traditional Khmer tradition and is commonly known as "veneration" when a relative dies.
It should be noted that Duke Prit Moha Upasika Thommanhan Vivathana passed away at 2:12 AM on the 13th day of the month of Pisak in the year of Chuot, the Buddhist era 2563, which is the 4th day of May, 2020 at the age of 96 years old. Buried at 3:33 pm on May 6 at his hometown in the second village, Rokar Khnor commune, Krouch Chhmar district, Tbong Khmum province.
