(Preah Sihanouk): The fire at the foam box factory on the evening of May 7, 2020 in Prek Pros village, Teuk Thla commune, Prey Nob district, Preah Sihanouk province has been extinguished after the authorities used 28 trucks of water to intervene and rescue.
A report from the Sihanoukville Provincial Police confirmed that the factory, which was 54 meters wide and 70 meters long, was made of steel and galvanized iron, with a corrugated iron roof, brick walls and concrete floor, and belonged to the Song Horn factory.
In particular, the cause of the fire was an electric shock with a welder on the roof. In the rescue operation of the Police Inspectorate of Prey Nup District, Preah Sihanouk Province, Kampot Province, 7 fire trucks were sprayed, including 3 fire trucks from Preah Sihanouk Province and 4 fire trucks from Kampot Province, using 28 water trucks.
