(Ratanakkiri): Mr. Bou Lam, Member of Parliament for Ratanakkiri Constituency, said that because Cambodia is peaceful, our people have celebrated with joy and sincerity.
Mr. Bou Lam said this on the occasion that he and she, as well as the director and deputy director of some departments were invited to a blessing ceremony on the occasion of Vesak at Wat Udom Ratanaream, also known as Wat O Cheng in Ta Ong village, Ta Ong commune, Kon Mom district, Ratanakkiri province on the afternoon of the 15th. Born in the month of Pisak, the year of Chuot Tosak POS 2563, which is on May 6, 2020.
Mr. Bou Lam expressed his pleasure to participate in the festival, one of the religious festivals that Buddhists throughout the Kingdom of Cambodia always celebrate every year on the 15th of Roach Pisak.
Today is also the day that the United Nations has designated Pisak Bochea as an International Day since December 15, 1999, which is a universal recognition of the contribution of Buddhism to the world over 2,600 years ago. And will continue to contribute to uplifting the spirit of humanity. United Nations offices everywhere are closed on this sacred day.
