After tightening traffic law enforcement, the number of driving test candidates increased, the Ministry said as a good sign (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): The number of driving test candidates increased significantly after the Royal Government Introduce measures to restrict the enforcement of road traffic laws with high fines.
According to data from the Ministry of Public Works and Transport, before the government introduced measures to restrict the implementation of this law, the number of people taking the driving test was small, only more than 100 or 300 people a day. . But after the introduction of this measure, the number of people taking the driving test is high, some days there are more than 1,000.
According to the report, from April 1 to May 6, 2020, the number of people taking the driving test was 4,037. There are about 490 candidates for the driving test for motorcycles, motorcycles, trailers, tuk-tuks or tricycles or four-wheeled motorbikes, and about 2,890 for light vehicles.
Heang Sotheayut, a spokesman for the Ministry of Public Works and Transport, assessed that the increase in driving test scores was due to two reasons. The first reason is the understanding and spirit of participation in the implementation of traffic laws of the people and the second reason may come from the people worried about the fines of the traffic police force after the Royal Government began to implement measures to restrict the implementation of traffic laws.
For whatever reason, Mr. Heang Sotheayut expressed his happiness and satisfaction with the increase in the number of people applying for a driver's license.
The young spokesman for the Ministry of Public Works and Transport (MPWT) emphasized that taking a driver's license exam is not only a test of a driver's ability to hold the steering wheel, but also a time to test his ability. Knowledge of the theory and understanding of traffic rules of the driver as well.
Mr. Heang Sotheayut stated that during the exam, there were more than 300 questions on the theory and rules of the road traffic, and more than 40 questions were answered for the examiners to answer electronically with accuracy. Do not take bribes or mediate in this contest.
It should be noted that after seeing a huge increase in the rate of traffic accidents and the death toll of the Cambodian people increased in 2019, the Royal Government of Cambodia has decided to make 2020 a year of emergency and a year of strict enforcement of road traffic laws. Land. Not only restricting the implementation of the law, the Royal Government has also decided to amend the sub-decree to punish serious violators, both in terms of penalties and financial fines.
Measures to tighten traffic law enforcement began on May 1, 2020. During the six days of implementing the traffic law enforcement measures, the traffic police force fined 12,732 vehicles, including 9,915 motorcycles and 2,817 vehicles.
Misconduct while driving for motorcycles is marked as mostly lack of helmets, violation of license plates and lack of license plates. The car, on the other hand, involved speeding, not wearing a seatbelt, not having a driver's license and driving with a mobile phone.
The implementation of traffic law enforcement restrictions over the past six days, despite some opposition and some dissatisfaction from the drivers, there has been a lot of support. Supported by the fact that the beginning of the enforcement of traffic laws, many drivers are beginning to wake up to obey the traffic rules and have a high spirit when driving.
