Cambodian Embassy in Kuwait intervenes to repatriate four Cambodians after more than a month in the United Arab Emirates
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Hun Han, Cambodian Ambassador to Kuwait, sought and intervened for the return of four Cambodians after visiting the United Arab Emirates and staying for more than a month due to Prevalence of Kovid 19 disease.
In a letter to Deputy Prime Minister Prak Sokhon, Minister of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation, obtained by Fresh News on Thursday, May 7, 2020, Mr. Hun Han said that the four Cambodians will Departed from the United Arab Emirates on May 7 and flew like Incheon, South Korea. Only on May 8, flew from South Korea to Cambodia.
According to Mr. Hun Han, the four Cambodian families traveled to the United Arab Emirates on March 13, 2020 and are scheduled to return to Cambodia on March 28, 2020. . Unfortunately, their father, who was one of the four, had a health problem that required him to stay there for a while until March 25, 2020.
However, as the global epidemic crisis COVID-19 worsened, all of the country's airlines suspended flights, leaving one Cambodian family stranded and staying in the United Arab Emirates to this day.
After a trip to the United Arab Emirates, a Cambodian family headed by Nguon Sophal sought the intervention of the Cambodian Embassy in Kuwait.
