According to Venerable Satibalo Sok Sophay, who lives at Wat Norodom Vorn, also known as Wat Koul Toteung, the Vesak festival not only commemorates the three special days of Samma Samput, but also to spread to the next generation. Is a special day of Buddhism.
Vesak is not only a Buddhist holiday but also one of the major religious holidays of the United Nations. Vesak was recognized by the United Nations as an international religious festival in 1999.
This festival is always celebrated solemnly throughout the day, with Buddhists gathering at the pagoda and counting the merits and meditations. But as early as 2020, new respiratory infections are spreading around the world, making it impossible for people to get out or stay in crowded places.
For this reason, as a Buddhist, Venerable Satibalo Sok Sophay advised all Buddhists at home to prepare the Buddha's altar in the morning, prepare food for the Buddha and in the afternoon, gather the family to listen or read the Dharma to remember the gratitude of the Buddha. Chip Mong Bank Small and Medium Loans Strengthen the Capacity of Local Producers and Artisans
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Nou Sotheara, Senior Deputy General Manager of Chip Mong Bank's Small and Medium Credit Department, said that the main goal of Chip Mong Bank's SME loans is to strengthen the production capacity of traders and producers to supply demand. Local and increase capacity to compete in the local market.
Chip Mong Bank joins the Royal Government of SMEs in a $ 100 million co-financing project to provide loans to small and medium enterprises for the development of small and medium enterprises, a key driver in Stimulating national economic growth.
Producers, artisans and owners of food processing enterprises can apply for small and medium loans from Chip Mong Bank with an interest rate of only 7% per annum for investment or working capital.
