(Phnom Penh): In the field of Buddhism, on the occasion of the Vesak Festival, Mr. Khieu Kanharith, Minister of Information, and Ms. Tep Rainsy, together with the leaders under the Ministry of Information, brought the suffixes and gifts to the monks. At Wat Nikrot One Kol Toteung in Koh Krabei village, Sangkat Prek Thmey, Khan Chbar Ampov, Phnom Penh, on Wednesday morning, May 6, 2020.
According to the pagoda's chief priest, for this year at the Nikrothavorn Koltoteung pagoda, there is no official big ceremony like every year, because the problem of Kovit 19 can cause infection when Gather many Buddhists at the foot of the pagoda. So it was decided that there would be no celebrations, but only a little privacy.
On this occasion, the Chief Bishop of Wat Preah Sang and the committee of Wat Nikrothavorn Koltoteung expressed their deep gratitude to Minister Khieu Kanharith and Mrs. Tep Rainsy and the leaders of the Ministry of Information for bringing the suffixes and gifts to God. The monks in Wat Nikrothavorn are dedicated to providing for the livelihood of the monks, as well as for Ta Chi Yeay, the students who live in this temple.
For a total of 15 million Riels, of which 5 million Riels will be donated to support the promotion of the Dharma of Koul Toteung Radio Station, 5 million Riels for monks' food and 5 million Riels for Koul Toteung Pagoda Hospital and 1 million Riels For monk teachers.
Please note that the Vesak festival is an important festival that all Buddhists around the world celebrate every year to commemorate the birth, enlightenment and death of Samanakottam, our great teacher. These three epochs occur on the 15th day of the month of Vesak, only one year apart.
Today is also the day that the United Nations has designated International Day since December 15, 1999, the universal recognition of the contribution of Buddhism to the world over two thousand five hundred years and is continuing. Its influence to further lift the spirits of mankind.
The meaning that Buddhists should better understand the importance of the three days of Samanakottam are birth, enlightenment and Nirvana for the benefit of worship and practice in their daily lives.
1: Date of birth: Born as a person, must be determined to do something, create something new in life until it is achieved by studying, training, educating yourself through the 7 steps is the path to success in life as a middle path in the Four Noble Truths That the Buddha has advanced before us and has already achieved.
2: Day of Enlightenment: When you have achieved what you set out to do, you should make that achievement for the benefit of yourself and humanity, and share the decision and the way to achieve that goal to mankind in general.
3: Day of Nirvana: Death is the nature of human-animal. As a person before death, there should be a legacy that the next generation can use to build themselves, society and the environment to be sustainable in the long run.
After notifying the World Health Organization on January 1, 2020, Chinese authorities announced the closure of Hunan Market, a large seafood and wildlife market in Wuhan, Hubei Province, with a population of approximately 11 million people. The closure was announced shortly after the city's hospital found more than 40 patients, with the first report identifying the new patient on November 17, 2019. .
"We do not need to announce the closure. China is already shutting down its country. Not only is it shutting down flights from Wuhan to Cambodia or to other countries. "Or other cities in China close both rail and land to allow for a smaller-scale settlement to prevent it from spreading."
Not only that, Samdech Techo Hun Sen announced that Cambodian students studying in Wuhan should remain in this city normally, in accordance with the instructions of the Chinese authorities. He said this because he believed in the leadership of the Chinese authorities and to show good relations between countries. "We can not be alone when they are happy, but we must also be happy together in difficult times," he added.
The announcement of the head of the Royal Government of Cambodia on this occasion made the people of China and Cambodia very emotional. In particular, the Chinese people have expressed calm in the spirit of friendship, brotherhood between people, as well as country and country. At the same time, some Cambodian and Chinese people, in addition to admiring the prince's spirit, also expressed safety concerns during Samdech Techo's visit.
Concerned and clear about the spirit of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Chinese government agreed to allow him to return to Beijing. The prince was not allowed to visit Wuhan because the city was closed to prevent the spread of the coronavirus.
February 5, 2020 is the day when the Prince and several Cambodian delegations visit Beijing, Republic of China. The visit of the head of the Royal Government of Cambodia is considered by Chinese President Xi Jinping as a strong show of support for China. "Cambodia is a loyal friend of China," Xi stressed.
"The prime minister's visit is a great confidence boost to China. Not only that, Samdech and the Cambodian government continue to support and trust China. This is according to the quote of the President of China through the Facebook account of Samdech Hun Sen on February 5, 2020.
The visit, at a time when some nations were discriminating against China, was deeply moved by the Chinese people. With the great excitement and enthusiasm of the Cambodian leadership, the Chinese people nicknamed the prince "handsome man walking in reverse."
Due to the COVID-19 problem, the whole world is short of raw materials to supply the international market. Because China, the world's largest producer of raw materials, has shut down all its industrial activities. And Cambodia also faces a shortage of raw materials.
Shipments of raw materials, while China is in a state of closure to prevent coronavirus, are limited to Cambodia in the world. This proves that China really considers Cambodia as a steel friend with a common destiny.
At the end of March 2020, China, the first country to be affected by the new respiratory disease, Covid-19 began to shine a new light, with no new infections in its country. And this hope has continued to the present time that China has no new cases in the country, only cases of imports. The situation is under the control of the management and the Chinese medical team.
After success in curbing the spread of a new type of respiratory disease, China did not delay. The Chinese leadership has sent medical experts and other essential medical equipment to help many countries in the world, including Italy.
Meanwhile, Cambodia, a country affected by the 19 imports of smallpox, is also receiving a lot of attention from the Chinese leadership. This attention was made by sending seven medical experts to advise the Ministry of Health of Cambodia, as well as many necessary medical equipment. To meet the needs of medical staff as well as medicines for treating patients.
In addition to providing assistance to the Ministry of Health through the Government of the Republic of China. The Chinese Ministry of National Defense has also sent four more specialists, along with the necessary medical equipment, to prevent the spread of COVID-19 to the Cambodian Ministry of National Defense twice. The first time, there were 4 medical teams and more than 2 tons of necessary medical equipment, and the second time provided 16 tons of necessary medical equipment.
In addition to the government and the Ministry of National Defense, it is observed that many Chinese private companies have brought the necessary medical equipment to prevent COVID-19 to many public and private institutions in Cambodia. All these actions can prove that both the Chinese government and the Chinese people really care about the well-being of the Cambodian people. As written on the case of medical supplies:
This shows the sweetness and understanding between Cambodia and China in the gloomy state of the world after the relationship between the two countries reached the 62nd year.
However, by the end of April 2020, the prevalence of Kovid 19 respiratory disease in China had decreased, with no new cases in the country other than imports. That such a situation can be controlled by the Chinese authorities. However, Kovid 19 respiratory disease has killed more than 4,000 people and infected more than 80,000 in China.
In Cambodia, a total of 122 cases were reported and 119 were cured, while three patients were hospitalized. According to a report by the Cambodian Ministry of Health, there were no deaths from Kovid 19 respiratory disease.
It should also be noted that Kovid 19 respiratory disease is not the first infectious disease that the world has experienced. For example, the Spanish flu, which struck in 1918, killed tens of millions of people and is considered the world's largest pandemic in human history. Then came the plague, which broke out in 1348 and killed 25 million people, about a third of the world's population at the time.
Then came the AIDS epidemic in Africa. Outbreaks appear to be exacerbated during 2003 in China. The H1N1 bird flu virus, which originated in the Americas or Mexico, broke out in 2009. Ebola originated in Africa and broke out in 2014. Mumps originated in the Middle East in 2015 and Sika disease originated in Brazil in 2016.
