Mr. Nop Channarin continued that such practices are beneficial for themselves and their families, such as preventing the transmission of Kovid-19 and ensuring the management of daily life, not difficult to pay rent or find a job. Because our country is an agricultural country and on the other hand, the Royal Government of Cambodia under the leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen has put in place all measures so that no Cambodian citizen dies of starvation unknowingly.
Mr. Nop Channarin, Undersecretary of State of the Ministry of National Assembly-Senate Relations and Inspection, made the remarks during a face-to-face meeting with 60 families from five villages in Koh Dach commune. Khan Chroy Changva, Phnom Penh, this morning, May 6, 2020.
Mr. Nop Channarin confirmed to the people that at present, the local authorities and the Royal Government team, together with the party working group to help Koh Dach Sangkat, regularly monitor all the living conditions of the people and conduct a census in the backyard to find the needy. From Kovid-19, such as those who have lost their jobs in the private sector and lack real livelihood to deal with in time.
He said that, obviously, like the people who are already here, the Koh Dach Sangkat administration, the Royal Government working group, the monks, the well-to-do people and some companies have contributed material funds to share their needs.
According to the report of Mr. Pat El, Koh Dach Commune Chief, until now, the local people are aware of the impact of smallpox-19, along with regular publicity on the announcement of The Ministry of Health has made it possible for us to completely avoid the spread of Kovid-19.
