Recent Achievements of the Royal Government to the People in Rolea Bier District, Kampong Chhnang Province
(Kampong Chhnang): Residents of Rolea Bier district, as well as people throughout Kampong Chhnang province, have expressed their happiness and enthusiasm for the many new achievements that have taken place in their locality, especially the three new paved roads. The cable, which is under construction like never before, is now gradually appearing in three lines, more than 9 kilometers long, connecting three communes in Rolea Bier district.
These three paved roads are the bond of the Royal Government of Cambodia to the people in Rolea Bier district, which is currently being built by the Ministry of Rural Development about 50%. The three paved roads above are also a grant from the People's Republic of China.
The people's representatives described that they were very excited to receive the paved road stretched across in front of their houses, which made it easy to travel because from childhood to old age in the commune. Theirs, which is a rural area, has never had a paved road in their village like now. People said that in the beginning, there were only dirt roads and cart roads.
According to the people, now under the leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia has turned carts and dirt roads into paved roads, as in their base above. These achievements make them extremely happy, even though they are old, for the next generation.
Mr. Yang Sao Vuthy, Governor of Rolea Bier District, confirmed that the three red gravel roads, which are more than 9 kilometers long, will be paved to 12 meters wide, 1.5 meters to 2 meters high, with drains and bridges. Many widths and canals along the road. These three roads are provided by the Royal Government through a grant from the People's Republic of China and built by the Ministry of Rural Development.
