* Two strange events
Two bizarre events have taken place in recent weeks: the three-week disappearance of North Korean leader Kim Jong Un, leading to some rumors that he is dead and others that he is a plant. And so on.
The latest incident was the exchange of fire between South and North Korean troops at the demilitarized zone between the two countries on Sunday. The retaliation first erupted from the North Korean side.
North Korea has not commented on either Kim Jong Un's disappearance and the shootings with South Korean troops. It was as if nothing had happened and they were not worried about what had happened. However, such a thing is already a habit of North Korea, that is, "not answer is the answer."
North Korea often never explains what it is doing, and when its provocative actions are a major mistake that is difficult to ignore, North Korea will lie despite the evidence. Field either. For example, the sinking of a South Korean warship in 2010 and the bombing of a South Korean airline plane in 1987, North Korea went unnoticed.
* Why is it difficult to communicate with North Korea?
The non-response is an answer to why North Korea is isolated, why it is difficult to communicate with North Korea. The leaders of this country never care or get a headache for what everyone is thinking. Moreover, the thing that makes it difficult to communicate with North Korea is that this country is ruled by a dictatorial family, not a communist regime.
Not only that, what worries neighboring countries like Japan and South Korea is that North Korea has nuclear weapons, but never cares about international law or universal morality. All they care about is for North Korea to be under the leadership of the Kim family.
