PRASAC officially listens to the bond sale on the Cambodia Securities Exchange
(Phnom Penh): Following the successful publication in April, PRASAC Microfinance Institution's corporate bonds were listed on the Cambodia Securities Exchange, allowing trading to begin. The bond will be traded on the Cambodia Securities Exchange under the symbol "PRA23A".
PRASAC Corporate Bonds are listed for sale under the ASEAN + 3 Multi-Currency Issuance Framework (AMBIF) through the use of the Common Document Form for Application for Issuance in Cambodia in accordance with the ASEAN + Bond Market Forum Initiative Program. 3 (ABMI).
This transaction is an era in which not only represents the single largest capital increase in the history of Cambodia's capital market, but also a market-based transaction and is fully subscribed by both investors. Domestic and foreign, which is a contribution to the development of the securities market in Cambodia.
The bond is issued in riel, and CGIF supports the government's efforts to promote the riel in Cambodia's economy. It is very important to support the capital needs of the largest microfinance institutions to allocate finance to the smallest, medium and small enterprises and individuals in the country during this difficult time.
PRASAC MFI is the largest depository institution in Cambodia. In March 2020, PRASAC continued to lead the market in terms of assets, gross credit, customer deposits and net profit. By expanding to 180 branches and 138 ATMs covering the whole country, PRASAC provides a wide range of financial products and services to sustainable rural communities and small enterprises.
