(Phnom Penh): A suspect was arrested by the police on May 4, 2020 in connection with a breach of trust case and sent to court today for legal action.
According to the authorities, the suspect is named Kuch Try, 63 years old, currently living at 227E0, Street 182, Village 1, Sangkat Teuk Laak 1, Khan Toul Kork, Phnom Penh. The arrest was made following a complaint by the victim, Chheang Pheach, a 63-year-old female.
Suddenly, the suspect escaped until he could not be contacted and refused to take the car identification card to hand over to the victim. Only after the search did the victim find out that the suspect had taken the car identification card as collateral at the microfinance institution since February 10, 2018. Because the suspect's actions make the victim pay for the benefit, the victim decided to file a complaint to the authorities to help find justice.
