(Phnom Penh): Criminal Police Department arrested a man posing as a two-star police officer at the Ministry of Interior after threatening to kill, threatening to defame, using illegal weapons and cheating. This transaction took place on May 4, 2020 in Sangkat Chroy Changva, Khan Chroy Changva, Phnom Penh.
Colonel Mom Chek, Director of the Administration Office of the Criminal Police Department, told Fresh News on the afternoon of May 5, 2020 that the operation took place on the orders of General Dr. Neth Savoeun, National Police Commissioner. , Lt. Gen. Neng Chuor, Director of the Department and led the operation by Brigadier General Cheav Vibol, Deputy Director of the Department.
According to Colonel Mom Chek, the suspect arrested by the specialized police force was 47-year-old Seng Sopheaktra. The arrest was also mediated by Mr. Keo Sothea, Prosecutor of the Phnom Penh Municipal Court.
The suspect confessed that he had indeed disguised himself as a two-star national police officer at the Ministry of Interior and took $ 10,500 from the victim to run for the National Police, but was unable to do so. When the victim called to ask for money, he sent a threatening death message if he continued to ask for money. On May 4, 2020, he was arrested along with a Glock26 handgun without a license.
Currently, the Criminal Police Department has prepared the case file and sent the suspect to the Phnom Penh Municipal Court for further proceedings.
