A report by the National Road Safety Committee noted that the number of victims of road accidents was still 78 percent, 34 percent were workers, 33 percent were farmers, 10 percent were students. 11% of the victims were under the age of 17, 70% were between the ages of 18 and 45, and 19% were 46 years old or older.
Of the 78 percent of motorcyclists, 1,186 were not wearing helmets, accounting for 77 percent.
Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng, Deputy Prime Minister, Minister of Interior and Chairman of the National Road Safety Committee, after seeing the high rate of traffic accidents in 2019, decided to choose 2020 as the year of emergency and put strict measures in Traffic law enforcement.
Along with the introduction of hot measures to restrict the implementation of the traffic law, a new sub-decree on fines for traffic offenders was signed by the Prime Minister of Cambodia, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, on March 17, 2020. The new road traffic offenders will be fined and fined two to three times by sub-decree.
Samdech Techo, the head of the Royal Government, announced that the decision to impose severe fines on illegal drivers is not to extort money from the people, but to put in place measures to protect the lives of the people who died on the streets. Every day.
Since the enforcement of road traffic laws with high fines on May 1, 2020, it has been observed that car owners have been more vigilant in enforcing and obeying traffic laws. By questioning most drivers, they show that they are very careful when driving on the road by checking traffic signs and traffic signs.
Not only is there a high level of awareness when driving a vehicle on the road, before starting to drive a vehicle, they have already checked the characteristics before departure, such as checking whether wearing a seat belt or not? Already wearing a helmet? And other precautions to avoid breaking the law while driving on the road.
Another argument that shows that vehicle owners are vigilant in complying with the road traffic law is that since the authorities announced the tightening of the implementation of this law, they have seen many vehicle owners take the vehicle to check the technical characteristics and get a driver's license.
A report from the Ministry of Public Works and Transport shows that from April 23 to May 4, 2020, up to 31,259 vehicles were inspected.
For those who change or renew their driver's license at the Aeon 1 and Aeon 2 driver's license centers, there are also an unprecedented number. According to the report, from April 30 to May 4, the two centers issued 2,976 driver's licenses.
Another good thing is that after the traffic law enforcement four days ago, the report shows that the accident rate has dropped by half. Officials see the drop in accident rates as a result of tightening traffic rules.
Restrictions on traffic laws with severe fines are not limited to Cambodia, neighboring Cambodia and many other developed countries in the world have already done so to bring order and order to the streets as well as reduce rates. Traffic accident.
However, the strict enforcement of traffic laws over the past four days, there have been some conflicts between traffic police officers and people breaking the law. Resentment may be due to the behavior of a small number of traffic police officers who lack coordination and patience when offenders do not follow the law.
Although this is not the first time for Cambodia to start enforcing the law, most people still do not understand the traffic law and the spirit of respect for the law is still low. Therefore, the implementation of this law can not be done by force, it must be done slowly, like rain, with the principles, explanations, guidance and education as much as possible so that vehicle owners understand and accept the intentions of law enforcement.
The message is that the Minister wants the traffic police force, which is law enforcement, to be flexible and soft, not to be forced to enforce the law, which leads to strong confrontation with the people who own the vehicle.
