(Phnom Penh): Mr. Chrek Sonim, a well-known Cambodian real estate expert and president of the Cambodian Association of Appraisers and Realtors, expressed the view that the Kovid 19 crisis is an opportunity for buyers of real estate with a lot of cash flow. Can buy real estate at a cheaper price.
The president of the Cambodian Association of Appraisers and Realtors said that as the Kovid 19 crisis unfolded, the economies of each country were in decline, not only in Cambodia, but also in the real estate sector. A good one for those who have a lot of cash flow to seize the opportunity to invest in such a situation.
In fact, in the program "Special Guest of the Week" of Fresh News TV, Mr. Chrek Sonim stated that after the outbreak of Kovid-19, the real estate sector in Cambodia has decreased by about 30%. In buying and selling, which caused the real estate sector in some areas to decline.
In addition, real estate experts say that in a situation where the country is facing the Kovid-19 crisis, it is a good time for those who want to buy real estate, because now may be easier to negotiate the price. Negotiable at a cheaper price Compared to emerging economies, the real estate sector is not easy to negotiate a price reduction.
"We see that in the real estate sector in Cambodia as a whole, trading seems to be declining by about 30 percent in trading, but it is an opportunity for investors to start all opportunities," said Chrek Sonim. This. "If you have a good cash flow, you can invest because now is a good time."
