(Phnom Penh): Bi Cheng Rup Wek Company has donated 155,000 USD to the Royal Government of Cambodia to help fight and prevent the spread of Kovid 19 disease.
The handover ceremony took place on May 5, 2020 at the Ministry of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation, chaired by Deputy Prime Minister Prak Sokhon, Minister of Foreign Affairs, and Tycoon Thai Tino, a representative of Bicheng.
On behalf of the Royal Government of Cambodia, Deputy Prime Minister Prak Sokhon expressed his deep appreciation and gratitude to Beicheng Brands for providing a total of US $ 155,000 to join the Royal Government in the fight against Kovid 19 with the Royal Government.
The Deputy Prime Minister considered that these funds were provided in a timely manner as 19 Kovid cases were rampant in the country. He said that these funds will be handed over to the Royal Government through the National Commission for Combating Kovid 19 in the near future.
It should be noted that on May 5, 2020, the Ministry of Health announced that there were no cases of Kovid 19 infection and no cases were cured, while a total of 120 Kovid 19 patients were cured. As of this morning, May 5, 2020, only two of the 122 infected people are being treated for Kovid.
