Vendors selling pork in Trea market, Preah Sdach district, Prey Veng province, protested, accusing veterinary officials of applying non-transparent law
(Prey Veng): Vendors selling pork in Trea market, Preah Sdach district, Prey Veng province, erupted in protest, accusing district veterinary officials of applying the law in a non-transparent and irregular manner, banning the sale of pork and claiming that Pig disease.
The pig owner confirmed that the pigs he sold were the main pigs he raised in his cage at home, weighing more than 200 kilograms, a healthy pig that had been raised for more than five years. Pork traders claim that based on their more than 20 years of experience in slaughtering pigs for the past 20 years, it is not the end of the pig hogs, but the fat fibers that mostly occur on long-term sows.
However, on the same day, Mr. Chen Visal, director of the Prey Veng Provincial Veterinary Office, as well as relevant district officials with the district and provincial committees, still accused the pig of being a pig and burned it. At the same time, he explained to the traders who own pigs and warned to close the business if the traders continue to be stubborn.
The above story was told by the public, especially traders in Preah Sdach district, that the enforcement of the law by the veterinary authorities seemed to be non-transparent and unusual, especially accusing a young veterinarian named Neng, because in the past, the official This always uses inappropriate, unethical words, working in a resentful manner with traders.
Residents as well as all pig traders in Trea Market, Preah Sdach District, request Mr. Ouk Samnang, Director of Prey Veng Provincial Department of Agriculture, especially Mr. Chen Visal, Director of Prey Veng Provincial Veterinary Office, to help and check this official so that he does not make any noise The rainstorm in Preah Sdach district was too strong.
Very symphonic! A fire engulfed a wooden house with a corrugated iron roof, killing two children in O'Chum district, Ratanakkiri province.
(Ratanakkiri): A fire engulfed a wooden house made of zinc, causing the death of two boys and a girl. The incident happened at 21:30 at the hydropower point in O'Chum village, O'Chum commune, O'Chum district, Ratanakkiri province.
According to the description of Srul Yeam, a 26-year-old woman from Tampoun, a neighbor, the cause of the gasoline fire was that the gas canister caught fire.
The O'Chum district police inspector confirmed that the damaged items included a 5-by-6-meter wooden house, two Honda motorcycles and some other items.
In the above operation, the police force used 3 fire trucks and water trucks. With the fire that killed two children and caused a lot of property damage, the Ratanakkiri provincial authorities have asked people to be very careful, such as candles, incense sticks, wiring is technically correct to avoid such risks. Today.
