ICRC hands over 1,200 booklets on prison rules in Thai, Vietnamese, English and Chinese to the General Department of Prisons
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Jingyire Ambekov, Deputy Chief of Prison Project Coordinator of the International Committee of the Red Cross, and General Chan Kimseng, Director General of the General Department of Prisons, Ministry of Interior, presided over the handing over ceremony. Sub-section on the rules of procedure of 1,200 prisons translated into Thai, Vietnamese, English and Chinese to the General Department of Prisons.
The handover ceremony took place on May 4, 2020 at the General Department of Prisons of the Ministry of Interior, and ICRC activities were conducted to facilitate foreign detainees to receive guidance on discipline and living in prisons in Cambodia. .
According to a statement from the International Committee of the Red Cross (ICRC), it commended the authorities for their efforts to ensure equal access to information for all detainees. By contributing to the improvement of prison management and the provision of basic rights to detainees.
Therefore, the ICRC accepted the request of the General Department of Prisons and provided the necessary financial and technical support to achieve the translation of the prison rules of procedure in four languages (Thai, English, Vietnamese and Chinese), as well as child printing. More than 1,200 pamphlets on internal regulations of prisons under design collaboration with the General Department of Prisons.
"Our goal is to support the General Department of Prisons' efforts to ensure that foreign inmates (about 5 percent of all inmates in Cambodia) are admitted Knowledge of official laws and regulations while incarcerated in prisons in Cambodia.
He added that foreign detainees were considered a vulnerable group due to various factors. Also, the main obstacle is language. And this point makes this group receive special attention from our principles like other groups such as women, minors, inmates, the elderly or the disabled who have humanitarian needs under various conditions.
The ICRC has been visiting prisons in Cambodia since 1992, carrying out various activities, particularly visiting more than 10,000 detainees in its target prisons on a regular basis to check their living conditions. They also support the authorities in providing the necessary living conditions to the detainees.
