(Preah Sihanouk): The Preah Sihanouk Provincial Administration on May 4, 2020 came out to confirm the management and land issues in Preah Sihanouk National Park "Ream". The release confirms that after some questions and concerns related to land management and disputes in this area.
According to a press release from the Sihanoukville Provincial Administration, in June 2008, the Royal Government issued a sub-decree defining a sustainable use area of 3,300 hectares in Sihanoukville "Ream" National Park. Land reclamation of state public property to state private property.
In a statement issued by the Sihanoukville Provincial Administration, it was claimed that along with the development, illegal logging and encroachment on forest land in the Sihanoukville "Ream" National Park area had also occurred. Those activities destroyed natural resources, which are the public property of the state, and hindered the implementation of the company's projects, which were legally licensed by the government.
These illegal activities have been instructed and taken action by the authorities and competent officials. Until 2016, Preah Sihanouk Provincial Administration has set up a joint working group to measure and identify the plots of people who have been living and enjoying the affected land in the development investment area of Keychouri Horm Development Development Company and Everbridge Success & Asia Resort Development Co., Ltd.
In 2017, the Royal Government also issued a new sub-decree on the designation of a community area of Sihanoukville Ream National Park on an area of 667.96 hectares in Ream commune, Prey Nob district, Sihanoukville province. Land titles have already been issued to people who actually live in the area. Therefore, both companies are able to continue to implement their development projects.
By 2018, a group of anarchists from the provinces had invaded and encroached on state forest land in the "Ream" National Park. Especially in the investment land of Key Chia Toury Development Company and Evergreen Success & Asia Resort Development Co., Ltd.
