APSARA Authority completes the repair of the road from Jayavarman VII roundabout through the airport to the front of Angkor Wat, nearly 7 km long
(Siem Reap): The project to repair the road from the roundabout of King Jayavarman VII through Neang Pov airport to the intersection of the parking lot in front of Angkor Wat, 10 meters wide, paved with AC rubber, total length 6,712 meters Which the APSARA Authority has been implementing from mid-January 2020 to May 4, 2020 has been completely repaired.
The renovation project is divided into three sections: the first section from National Road No. 6 at the roundabout of King Jayavarman VII to the front of the airport with a length of 2,181 meters. The second section from the front of the airport to the front of Neang Pov temple is 985 meters long. The third section from Neang Pov temple to the front of Angkor Wat temple is 3,546 meters long.
This road offers a lot of potential to serve the travel of people in / out of Siem Reap, safe transportation and save time, especially national and international tourists visiting the Angkor resort.
