Nearly 100 Families Protest for Cutting Nearly 300 Hectares of Cashew Land Into Broadcasting Station in Kampong Thom Province
(Kampong Thom): Nearly 100 families have erupted in protest over the cutting of the cashew land they enjoy every year for the past three to six years. Their cashew land was cut by the Tonle Sap Lake Forestry Administration Inspectorate and relevant authorities into the area of the Forest Rehabilitation and Rehabilitation Station in Anlong Thmor area, Boeung Lvea commune, Santuk district, Kampong Thom province.
In this regard, nearly 100 families have insisted on the intervention of the leadership to help provide them with cashew plantations after enjoying since 2006 and 2011 and so far have potatoes and cashews along with mixed crops. Many others.
The villagers stated that they wondered why they had not been banned in the past until the end of 2018 until 2020, when they came to inform and destroy the crops that are their strength. Living in poverty, there is no way to travel when people are productive and still claim to be degraded forest land for reforestation.
Residents of the village live in fear, harassing and threatening residents to hand over land to tie the knot and causing violence, beating people on March 10 and causing two gunshots on the 18th. April 2020 at 4:30 p.m.
One of the victims described that he had been cultivating cashews on his farm for eight years and enjoying every season for five years.
The villagers call on the Royal Government and relevant ministries to help resolve to get back the land and enjoy the blessings from afar, wishing both of you good health to continue to lead the nation and the people below. Peace roof.
