Cambodian Embassy in Malaysia informs the Malaysian government about the facilitation of those trapped there, especially those whose visas have expired.
(Phnom Penh): The Cambodian Embassy in Malaysia on May 4, 2020, issued a statement to the Cambodian people on the Malaysian government's facilitation of foreigners stranded in the country, especially those who have run out of money. Visa validity during the travel inspection regulations is still valid until May 12, 2020.
* First, all foreigners whose visas have expired from January 1, 2020, can continue to stay in Malaysia until the government's travel inspection regulations are finalized and are not listed. Black or pay a fine and can leave Malaysia within 14 days after the government's travel regulations are finalized.
* Second: All foreigners whose passport has expired from February 1, 2020 can renew at the nearest immigration office no later than 30 days after the Royal Malaysian government closes travel regulations
* Fourth: All immigration services at public service centers in urban areas across the country will reopen after the travel inspection regulations are closed.
