Senior Minister Sun Chanthol: During the Techo Sen era, roads were connected at all lanes and could travel anywhere without having to go back.
(Phnom Penh): Senior Minister Sun Chanthol, Minister of Public Works and Transport, said that during the Techo Sen era, roads were connected to all corners of the country and the region, meaning that we could travel anywhere in the country without having to go back. Also.
Senior Minister Sun Chanthol said this this morning, May 4, 2020, on the occasion of leading a delegation of the Ministry to inspect the progress of the construction of National Road No. 11 with the participation of professional officials, representatives of construction companies, representatives of consulting companies. Technical and stakeholders as well.
The purpose of this inspection is to look at the remaining shortcomings as well as some technical issues related to the construction to encourage the construction contractor to make adjustments, supplement the technical specifications correctly and in accordance with the load book to improve the quality of this road. Sturdy, durable.
Senior Minister Sun Chanthol said that despite the 19 cases of Kovid, which is a global problem, the construction of road and bridge infrastructure is still operating normally, except for National Road No. 2 and National Road No. 22 due to the arrival of Team accessories are slow.
According to the senior minister, after passing the quality control of the road for a while, National Road No. 11 and National Road No. 3 are of good quality according to the standards and in accordance with the technical specifications and the charge book, not a thin, thick concrete. The senior minister also informed the construction companies that if they do not want to rebuild or be blacklisted, they must build in accordance with technical standards and charge books.
Senior Minister Sun Chanthol also instructed all road users to join the Royal Government in preserving the national property, especially those who live along the national road, not to encroach on the land, to respect the law and not to overload. Weight limit by law.
On that occasion, the construction company of National Road No. 11 also promised with Senior Minister Sun Chanthol to help widen the road at Svay Antor roundabout in Svay Antor district, Prey Veng province to facilitate people's travel more easily. Also free.
