In the morning of the same day, Siem Reap branch of Consumer Protection, Competition and Anti-Fraud Branch also continued to investigate non-compliance with consumer goods at another supermarket, Chao Saing Hok, one of the largest supermarkets in Siem Reap. Officials also did not find any unusual items on display there.
Mr. Khieu Panhavath, President of the Siem Reap branch of the CPP, said that with the good cooperation of the Siem Reap Provincial Administration and the sub-national professional units of the Siem Reap branch of the CPP, the survey was carried out. Non-compliance with food and non-food products sold in the market and online shopping network is consistently bearing fruit.
In fact, in the first quarter of this year, more than 335 kilograms of non-compliant food and non-food goods were found and confiscated by the Siem Reap branch of the CPPCC. A total of 2,998 kilograms of compliance is ready to seek permission from prosecutors for demolition.
According to the head of the non-compliant merchandise branch, that includes expired food, foods that use banned chemicals, and especially unsafe alcohol, which Cambodians are consuming, while Kovid-19 virus is spreading. The world.
The foreign workers are currently undergoing interrogation at an immigration detention center, along with 42 others who were tested positive for COVID-19 on April 25.
