(Ratanakkiri): The Governor of Ratanakkiri Province, Mr. Thong Savun, called on and encouraged the people and workers working in the province to take time to grow crops in their free time to support themselves and earn extra income.
The appeal of the provincial governor was made during a meeting with workers and review the work progress of the company in Krong Bok in Ta Veng Leu commune, Ta Veng district on May 4, 2020.
Mr. Thong Savun said that due to the context of the country facing the epidemic of Kovid-19 virus, 2020 could not celebrate International Labor Day by organizing a rally, however, the provincial leaders held a meeting. Visit the site, maintaining a safe gap to prevent the transmission of Kovid-19 virus.
He also informed the company management and workers about the latest situation of Kovid-19 virus in Cambodia. In the recent period, the Royal Government has managed to prevent any new infections, with only two patients remaining. However, he also called on workers to be hygienic and vigilant because the percentage of infections is still high.
Mr. Thong Savun expressed his appreciation to the management of the company who worked hard and provided many job opportunities for workers, despite the global problem of Kovid-19 virus, but still maintain jobs and salaries to workers. Not lost.
On that occasion, the provincial governor continued to bring gifts in the form of food and some materials to the workers at the back of the house in the construction site organized by the company. He urged workers to take time off from work to grow vegetables to support their livelihoods and the family economy, rather than spending their free time doing useless things or gambling.
It should be noted that Krong Bok Company has invested in the agro-industrial sector and rubber production on more than 6,000 hectares. At present, it has planted more than 5,000 hectares and provided employment opportunities to nearly 1,000 workers.
