Senior Minister Sun Chanthol: National Road No. 11 is built according to the technical standards and is scheduled to be completed by the end of 2020
(Phnom Penh): Senior Minister Sun Chanthol, Minister of Public Works and Transport, confirmed that the construction of National Road No. 11 from Neak Leung to Tbong Khmum province, which is 96 kilometers long, is expected to cost about $ 98 million. Construction at the end of 2020 with the quality of construction in accordance with the technical standards set by the Ministry.
Senior Minister Sun Chanthol stated this this morning, May 4, 2020, on the occasion that he led a team to inspect the progress of the National Road 11 project.
The senior minister further stated that in order to know the quality of the road, the team paved the road to see the rubber thickness without setting a place, in fact, the rubber thickness is correct according to the technical standard set by the Ministry. Some are even thicker than the limit.
Senior Minister Sun Chanthol further stated that from now on, the Ministry of Public Works will no longer have roads, as the people say, they will be thinner, thicker, thicker and thinner, and the roads will be of better quality and will not be paved. Until then.
He added that some of the roads were damaged not because of poor quality construction, but because of overcrowding. The road is damaged so quickly, and we must all respect the law, do not carry more than the limit, so that our road can be used for a long time.
Senior Minister Sun Chanthol emphasized that he would continue to send special teams to inspect road construction without prior notice to ensure that road construction is of high quality and accurate. According to the technical standards, in the past, some companies did not build according to the technical standards, the Ministry required them to repeat and were warned repeatedly.
Please note that the construction project of National Road No. 11 is a 5 cm thick AC concrete road, raising and widening the road width from 9 meters to 11 meters, laying the foundation layer both above and below, 60 cm thick, with 2 traffic directions. The lane (1 to 1) is equipped with traffic signs, traffic markers, kilometer markers and road safety poles.
