(Kep): While the study of master planning for tourism development in Kep has been progressing gradually, the Ministry of Tourism has expressed confidence that this master plan will help Kep become a quiet, high-end luxury tourism destination. Attraction and competition in the region and the world.
This statement was made at a meeting to promote the master plan for tourism development in Kep, chaired by Mr. Tith Chantha, Permanent Secretary of State of the Ministry of Tourism on behalf of Minister Thong Khon, together with Mr. Chea Bora, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Tourism and Mr. Ken Satha, Governor Kep Province at Kep Provincial Hall on May 04, 2020.
Mr. Ny Phally, Undersecretary of State of the Ministry of Tourism and Chairman of the Secretariat of the Inter-Ministerial Commission for the Study and Development of the Kep Tourism Master Plan, stated that in order to support the study of the Kep Tourism Master Plan on January 15, 2020. The Royal Government has established an inter-ministerial commission to study and prepare a master plan for the development of tourism in Kep and Mondulkiri provinces.
Mr. Ny Phally continued that the process of studying and planning the master plan for tourism development in Kep province has been implemented since December 2019, and from now on, there will be participation and input from The provincial administration, departments, specialized units at the provincial level to ensure that the master plan is comprehensive and has shared responsibilities.
On that occasion, Mr. Tith Chantha also instructed the working group to study the master plan to consider both positive and negative and risk management on the environment, water system, construction, cadastre, public works and other related sectors to make Tourists remember the special points after visiting this province.
The Ministry of Tourism also requested the Kep Provincial Administration to establish a specialized working group to support and participate in research with the national working group to ensure that the master plan for tourism development in Kep is achieved accurately, equitably, transparently and sustainably. .
Mr. Ken Satha expressed his support for the proposal of the Ministry of Tourism and proposed a number of projects to be included in the above master plan, such as the development of new tourist beaches (from the wastewater treatment station to the mangrove forest) and Angkor Beach. Located in Angkol commune, Damnak Chang Eur district, as well as the establishment of a small tourist port on Koh Tonsay, the arrangement of rope baskets for tourists to ride from one tourist destination to another.
According to Mr. Ny Phally, the draft plan for tourism development in Kep province is scheduled to be completed by the end of July 2020 and may be submitted to the meeting of the Inter-Ministerial Commission in August 2020. Following the revision or approval of the Head of the Royal Government, the Kep Tourism Development Master Plan will be implemented from 2021 to 2035 and may be revised for implementation in the following years.
