(Phnom Penh): Nearly 3,000 saplings of rare trees have been planted by the Phnom Penh Forestry Administration at various locations in Phnom Penh to improve the city's aesthetics and as a green cover to prevent climate change. In the planet.
At the same time, the authorities of the Phnom Penh Forestry Administration also called on people to plant trees, and if there is a shortage of seedlings, please make a request to the Forestry Administration.
This was stated by Mr. Koam Seiha, Director of Phnom Penh Forestry Administration and in the planting ceremony of additional trees in the National Children's Hospital in Sangkat Toek Laak 1, Khan Toul Kork, Phnom Penh this morning, May 4, 2020.
Mr. Koam Seiha added that trees are important to help keep the environment around the hospital greener, especially to reduce climate change on the planet to help eliminate toxins. He said the trees also provide shade and help get rid of carbon dioxide, which pollutes the air and increases oxygen.
At the same time, he also asked people to plant trees, if there is a shortage of seedlings can ask the Forestry Administration to distribute.
Dr. Lian Kem Sreng, in charge of the emergency department of the National Children's Hospital, encouraged people to love and care for the tree, because it is a shade for people who bring their children to check their disease, and also help reduce other toxins. Come to the hospital as well.
