General Sem Sovanny, director general of the National Center for the Management of Peacekeeping Forces, Demining and Remnants of War, told Fresh News this morning, Monday, May 4, 2020, that he had received an e-mail from the UN mission. Cheat said that two Cambodian Blue Hat forces have returned to normal health, and the other continues to receive treatment with high attention from doctors.
The Chief of the Cambodian Blue Hat Army, General Sem Sovanny, praised the Cambodian doctors and medical team for their good cooperation with the United Nations team in treating and caring for patients. Professional care and high sense of responsibility, and also the first time for the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces to cure the deadly epidemic COVID-19 has healed.
General Sem Sovanny added that so far the UN team has asked the Cambodian team to continue their treatment and keep the three separate for another 10 days while waiting. Remember to take a sample for testing to confirm that there is no further infection.
General Sem Sovanny also said that the National Center continues to monitor and guide regularly and remind all forces to increase vigilance and continue to strictly implement the instructions of the Ministry of Health and the Royal Government in the fight. Against COVID-19.
It should be noted that currently, Cambodia's five Blue Hat forces, a total of nearly 800 people, including nearly 80 women, have been carrying out peacekeeping missions under the United Nations umbrella in four countries, including: Lebanon, South Sudan, Mali and the Central African Republic.
