SEOUL, May 3 (Xinhua) - North Korean leader Kim Jong Un has not undergone any heart surgery or surgery as previously rumored, the South Korean Yonhap news agency reported on Sunday. To claim no.
Yonhap made the report based on a source it obtained from a senior South Korean presidential official on condition of anonymity. The official emphasized: "Of course! "It is reported that President Kim underwent surgery based on his walking activities ... We have reason to believe that he did not undergo any surgery, but we can not say why." .
On Saturday, North Korean state media released photos of the actions of North Korean leader Kim Jong Un made his first public appearance after a 20-day absence. Kim Jong Un appeared in public at a ribbon-cutting ceremony for the inauguration of a fertilizer factory, and the crowd applauded when Kim Jong Un appeared.
Poor People in Muk Kampoul District, Kandal Province Receive Humanitarian Donations from Samdech Techo Hun Sen's Team
(Kandal): The humanitarian team of Mr. Has Vary, Advisor to Samdech Techo Hun Sen, this morning, May 3, 2020, distributed the humanitarian donation of Samdech Techo Hun Sen to the people in Spean Thmey Village, Roka Kong II Commune. Muk Kampoul district, Kandal province, which is extremely poor, homeless, living under the roof of their house to help them live while the world is suffering from Kovid 19.
The distribution ceremony was also attended by Mr. Lim Lin, Personal Assistant, Mr. Has Vary, Mr. Koy Run, Roka Kong II Commune Council, Deputy Chief of Roka Kong II Administration Post, Village Chief, Deputy Commander of Muk Kampoul District Military Operation Area. . At the same time, the working group also brought 200,000 Riel from Samdech Techo to pay condolences to the family of 89-year-old Im Bo, a resident of Doeum Chrey Village, Roka Kong II Commune.
On that occasion, Mr. LIM Lin also brought a message from Samdech Techo Hun Sen and Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen, President of the Cambodian Red Cross, who always took care of their well-being. And the lives of people, especially vulnerable people.
Mr. Limlin also urged people to be very careful about Kovid 19 by working together to prevent it and to follow the instructions of the Ministry of Health, do not meet often, wash your hands often. With soap, alcohol or gel to kill germs, especially newcomers and those from abroad, take him to be tested for Kovid 19 and put him in isolation for 14 days.
The families who received the donations also thanked and wished Samdech Techo Hun Sen and Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen, President of the Cambodian Red Cross, as well as sons, daughters, grandsons and granddaughters, happiness and prosperity. Forever story, I would like to wish and thank Mr. Has Vary and all the team for bringing Samdech Techo's gift to his family as well.
