APSARA Authority plans to plant and distribute 110,000 saplings by 2020
(Siem Reap): In order to increase the forest cover in the Angkor resort even more, in 2020, APSARA Authority will continue the campaign to plant and distribute 110,000 trees. APSARA Authority is busy planting and caring for the seedlings ready for planting in the coming rainy season.
Mr. Ley Kimsy, Technical Officer of the Department of Forest Management, Landscape, Culture and Environment and in charge of Nursery and Plantation, said that the four nursery stations of APSARA Authority are very busy in planting mixed seedlings to prepare. Planted in 2020. A total of 110,000 saplings are ready to be planted and distributed in the coming rainy season, including luxury trees, ornamental trees and fruit trees.
In the context of Kovid 19 disease, the plans for large-scale campaigns that have been organized in the past are unclear. Mr. Ley Kimsy explained that if the situation of Kovid disease improves, there will be large-scale programs involving the outside public, but if the situation is as it is today, the APSARA Authority will arrange to plant seedlings internally. According to the planned goal.
