Understand the law: Co-ownership building
(Phnom Penh): The real estate sector in Cambodia in recent years, we have observed that there is a remarkable growth momentum, these are part of driving the national economy to grow and raise the image of the Kingdom of Cambodia on the stage. International as well.
Due to all these factors combined with political stability in Cambodia, local and foreign investors have been looking at the investment market for many construction projects in potential areas, including high-rise projects of interest to the people. Cambodia is like a foreigner who comes legally to work and stay in the Kingdom of Cambodia.
This modern living style, which everyone calls a condo or apartment, is not a foreign loan for Khmer, it is called a co-ownership building. What are the rights and obligations of all individuals living in a condominium?
Therefore, for this week, FRESH NEWS Legal Awareness Program, in collaboration with the Cambodian Bar Association for International Cooperation, would like to raise the topic of "Co-ownership Building" to present to the following students:
Before interpreting the content of the article, we would like to present some of the following terms: Co-ownership is the ownership of real estate by several people, divided into lots, each of which is partly private and partly part of the common property. . Individuals with ownership of private equity are known as co-owners.
Each co-owner has full rights to manage his private equity, such as sale, exchange, lease, gift, inheritance, permanent lease, usufruct, use of rights, mortgage (mortgage) and mortgage but not Can create an easement and is strictly prohibited from disturbing or obstructing the joint use of other co-owners.
In the event that any co-owner damages or loses the original condition of the joint venture, the co-owner shall be guaranteed to restore the original part or in the event of a seizure of the joint venture to work. This type of occupation will be considered illegal occupation. At the same time, the authorities have the authority to force the person to dismantle and to ensure that the damaged part is restored to its original state.
The special co-owner shall comply with all the obligations and / or burdens set forth in the internal regulations of the co-ownership building and / or the law in force. In any case, the plot of land on which the co-ownership building is located cannot be the subject of ownership of the particular co-owner. For co-ownership buildings built on land leased from third parties, foreigners have the same right to permanently lease private shares as Cambodian citizens.
In summary, a co-ownership building refers to a building in which several owners live, and the co-owners are obliged to maintain the private and common parts in accordance with the internal regulations and regulations, but in the case of any co-owner affecting the joint part of the building. That property will be subject to a fine in accordance with the provisions of the law.
An Australian lobster farm in Oddar Meanchey province plans to expand farming to 100 hectares, Agriculture Minister recommends expanding hatchery for sale to farmers
The Australian female shrimp farm has been operating since 2016, with the gradual development of a variety of ponds (breeding ponds, breeding ponds and broilers), hatcheries and in-farm infrastructure. Currently experimenting with hatching and breeding in accordance with the agricultural environment in this area in order to achieve the production plan to produce 1 ton / day of lobster and increase continuously.
At present, there are about 600,000 seedlings that can produce about 50 tons in six months and plan to produce 5-10 million seedlings next year. This type of lobster costs $ 25 per kilogram at a trader's farm for resale at $ 30-35 per kilogram.
He expressed support for future production plans because it really contributes to job creation for local people, increase household income and reduce poverty, increase the potential supply of land to participate in the implementation of policies and development plans. Agriculture and especially create opportunities in accordance with the words of Samdech Techo Hun Sen.
With the provincial governor, he asked the company to examine the possibility of expanding production to other areas with good natural water sources, because the province has natural conditions favorable to raise this new species of shrimp.
He suggested that the company should expand the incubation of lobster seedlings and sell them to farmers to raise by providing technology and buy back lobster through contract farming to expand the market in the future. The Fisheries Administration and the Royal University of Agriculture should send officers and students to study and gain technical experience to promote this lobster production widely throughout the country. Six killed in Bolivia plane crash
Director of the Department of Mines and Energy: Every village in Kampong Cham province will have electricity in 2020 while achieving almost 100%
(Kampong Cham): Director of Kampong Cham Provincial Department of Mines and Energy, Mr. Ly Chanthy, said that all villages in the 10 districts of Kampong Cham province will have all the electricity network by 2020, while now this work is almost 100 percent completed. .
The confirmation of the Director of the Department was made while accompanying Mr. Un Chanda, Governor of Kampong Cham Province, to inspect the Kampong Cham Provincial Power Distribution Substation in Krala Commune, Kampong Siem District on May 2, 2020.
Mr. Ly Chanthy said that in Kampong Cham province, there are 37 public and private electricity suppliers and distributors with electricity licenses. At present, the company has connected 178,705 houses to electricity, covering 895 villages out of 916 villages, accounting for 97.71 percent.
He added that there are 21 villages that do not yet have access to electricity and that all of them will be connected by 2020.
