(Phnom Penh): Lt. Gen. Rath Sreang, Deputy Commander of the National Gendarmerie and Commander of the Phnom Penh Municipal Gendarmerie, on the morning of May 2, 2020, held a meeting with officers and deputies of the Royal Gendarmerie. Phnom Penh to disseminate the instruction of General Sao Sokha, Deputy Commander of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces, Commander of the National Gendarmerie on the Law on Road Traffic.
Based on the instructions of General Sao Sokha, which was issued to the Capital-Provincial Commanders to implement, Lt. Gen. Rath Sreang issued the following instructions to all members of the Phnom Penh Armed Forces as follows:
1. Officers, deputies and soldiers of the Phnom Penh Municipal Gendarmerie who drive the steering wheel of all types of vehicles on the road must have sufficient driver's license and legal documents in accordance with the provisions of the Law on Road Traffic. If you do not have or do not have enough, do not hold the steering wheel, control the vehicle and go to school or meet the qualifications.
2. To participate in the strict implementation of the law on road traffic, in case of committing an offense, shall be punished twice by receiving the fine according to the law and the punishment of the unit in accordance with the internal regulations.
3: As a law enforcement officer, you must be an example to the people and must participate in disseminating and urging the public to implement the law on road traffic at all times!
Lt. Gen. Rath Sreang also reminded all members of the Phnom Penh Military Police not to relax or neglect the Kovid virus and to continue to implement the protective measures that the Phnom Penh Military Police has put in place at all times.
