In his message, Samdech Techo Hun Sen expressed his great pleasure and warmly congratulated the media and all national and international journalists who are working in the field of journalism in Cambodia and around the world on the occasion of Freedom Day. Global Press, held on May 3 every year.
Samdech stated that the World Press Freedom Day aims to promote freedom of expression, freedom of the press, guarantee the independence of the media and ensure that journalists perform their duties without fear and promote their role. Of the media to be more active to contribute to the promotion of social welfare, peacekeeping, sustainable development and harmonization in the whole world.
Minister of Agriculture Instructs Fisheries Administration and Siem Reap Provincial Department of Agriculture to Contact Traders to Help Release Stocked Fish
(Siem Reap): Mr. Veng Sakhon, Minister of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, on May 2, 2020, inspected the activities of raising catfish, trout and trout at Mr. Ly Haing Seng Fish Farm in Svay Prey Village, Svay Dangkum Sangkat. Siem Reap City and Mr. To Leang Theung in Aranya Village, Sangkat Siem Reap, Siem Reap City, Siem Reap Province.
Accompanied by Mr. Un Sam Ath, Secretary of State, Mr. Eng Chea San, Royal Government of Cambodia Delegate in charge of Fisheries Administration, Mr. Keo Omalis, Royal Government of Cambodia Delegate in charge of Forestry Administration, Mr. Ngan Phirun, Deputy Governor, Mr. Tea Kim Soth, Director of the Department of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries and colleagues.
Mr. Haing Seng informed the Minister in detail that he has been engaged in fish farming since 2017 until now. 30 people. Follow the principles of fish farming techniques such as feeding, cleaning fish ponds, spawning, management, use and cleaning of water, etc. Obtained from professional officers of the Department and Fisheries Administration.
Leaving Ly Haing Seng's farm, he continued his journey to Puto Leang Theung's fish pond in Aranya village, Siem Reap commune. Mr. To Leang Theung has been raising catfish as a family since 2011 in an 8,600-square-meter pond, using domestic labor and renting from outside.
More importantly, Siem Reap is a tourist destination. Demand for food (rice, fish, meat, vegetables, fruits) is increasing year by year, but due to the global epidemic of Kovid-19, market demand and fish prices are declining. From 12,000 riel per kilogram to 10,000 riel per kilogram.
They both hope and believe in the near future after the epidemic returns to normal, both the market and prices will continue to improve. After examining the aspects and activities of fish harvesting in both places, the Minister and Deputy Governor praised and appreciated the efforts to adopt fish farming to contribute to meet the needs of the market in the province and reduce imports.
Although market demand and prices have declined slightly, the Minister encouraged them to continue to keep this business waiting for better conditions, because this is a strong career and a source of income in our family experience and down Lots of investment, so be patient, wait for a good opportunity.
Taking this opportunity, he advised the Fisheries Administration and the Provincial Department of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries to contact traders in Phnom Penh and markets outside of Siem Reap to help free up fish stocks. In optimal conditions should help plan production and apply the right techniques to ensure the sustainability of supply and lead to the processing of fish fillets for export.
Please be informed that throughout Siem Reap in 2019, it is possible to supply fish to the local market, both from natural water sources and from aquaculture (raising in 1,150 ponds, 810 ponds and raising in 63 plastic tents) in total 17,144 tons. The provincial market needs 13,185 tons of fresh fish to be processed into prahok, dried fish, animal feed, fish sauce and exported to markets outside the province.
