Major countries such as the United States, India and Nigeria have blamed China for not doing well since the new Coronavirus outbreak. As of Saturday afternoon, May 2, 2020, more than 3.4 million people on earth have been infected with COVID-19, of which more than 239,000 have died and more than 1 million have recovered in countries and territories. Total land 210.
Around the demand for compensation from China, international experts have similarly said that "it is an impossible legal step" and not a good strategy because China is given a status. Already a new superpower in this universe. "Under such circumstances, countries should promote international cooperation rather than blame each other," the experts said.
To sue China over the COVID-19 pandemic is an impossible legal process under international law. For current legal principles, no country can be sued without the consent of national and international courts. This means that only if China agrees to sue from other countries can they have the right to file a lawsuit against China.
China's manufacturing sector is the largest in the world and China is also the world's largest creditor. This means that much of the world is dependent on China as countries are doing more trade with China or getting more investment from Beijing.
As China needs countries to recover its economy, the world must also rely on China to recover its economy as a whole. As one of the largest owners in the world, China holds about 20% of its total debt in Africa. Blaming China (around COVID-19) will create risks as many poor countries in the region will find it difficult to apply for more loans from China in the future.
In addition, China is the largest source of medical supplies to fight coronavirus, including mass. If the COVID-19 vaccine is developed, China will also play an important role in the production and distribution of the world, or possibly as a vaccine developer.
* Promote global cooperation
The COVID-19 outbreak should be an opportunity for the international community to work together to find the best solution. In the past, international coordination to address climate change, refugees and other global issues has already taken place. Therefore, it is time for countries to establish strong cooperation to combat COVID-19.
After all, blaming or suing each other only worsens the situation, and it will affect efforts to stop the spread of coronavirus and treat millions of patients. Already infected. Continuing to blame each other may cause countries to deviate from what they have to prioritize.
(Kampong Chhnang): Four heavy-duty jeeps transporting cattle from Thailand, three from Thailand and one from Battambang province, owned by Angkor Sok Sen Chey Company, passing through Kampong Chhnang Province to Vietnam were attacked by the Production and Veterinary Office. Of Kampong Chhnang Provincial Department of Agriculture cooperated with the force of General Department of Animal Health and Animal Production on the night of May 1, 2020 to check some relevant documents in transportation.
Mr. Kreung Sam Ath, Director of Production and Veterinary Office of Kampong Chhnang Province, told Fresh News this morning, May 2, 2020 that the four cattle trucks are the specialized force of the General Department of Animal Health and Animal Production in cooperation with officials. The Production and Veterinary Office of the Provincial Department of Agriculture arrested them for the purpose of inspecting documents such as animal health certificates.
"As of this morning, May 2, 2020, the experts found that the four cattle trucks did not have animal health certificates, and the experts also found See that these 4 cars are overloaded as well. "Obviously, there is only one car in the document, it is allowed to carry only 10 cars, but loaded up to more than 30 cars, so the other three cars also have more than the same number."
On the morning of May 2, 2020, a representative of Angkor Sok Sen Chey told Fresh News by telephone that his company has been transporting cattle to Vietnam for more than 10 years. His company has a valid permit from the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, with the principle of transporting cattle once a year, depending on the company's procurement.
He did not refuse, and he will be ready to go to work with professional officials in accordance with the law without hesitation. However, he also requested and asked the relevant officials to expedite the application as soon as possible, but you have pity on the animals that have been without water and food for many days, especially buffaloes. Need regular soaking water.
On the other hand, he was afraid that his cattle would die, so he asked all relevant officials to speed up the work to get to the destination as soon as possible to avoid danger. Their lives.
