Letter to readers: "Screaming in the cage, worried about the freedom of the birds on the tree"
(Phnom Penh): While the world is fighting fiercely against Kovid 19, the common enemy of humanity on earth, there are a number of local and foreign media outlets in Cambodia that hire foreign servants as well as groups claiming to be As an independent analyst, he criticized the government of Samdech Techo Hun Sen for taking the Kovid 19 issue to suppress the freedom of the press in Cambodia.
They see measures against false information and measures to provoke or restrict some freedom of assembly in Cambodia as undermining the freedom of the press or freedom of expression. But they forget that some of the measures that the Phnom Penh government has put in place in the past are small and light compared to the measures in other Asian countries, especially in Europe and the United States.
We can also say that the first wave of Kovid 19 was successfully controlled by Cambodia as many countries in the region and the world continue to be fully attacked by this deadly virus that has infected humans. More than 3 million people have been killed and more than 220,000 around the world.
The most ridiculous thing is that these unscrupulous people accuse Cambodia of using Kovid 19 to suppress the freedom of the press while they have been living in their homes for a long time. This weeks or months ago. In other words, it is no different from a creature trapped in a cage and screaming about worrying about the freedom of a bird flying freely in a tree.
All in all, Cambodia is healthy, Cambodia has managed Kovid 19 well, Cambodia has no deaths from the virus, and the Cambodian people, as well as the media, are being completely free without being imprisoned like Sarika.
Cambodia has not suffered as much economic impact as countries in Europe and the United States. Cambodia's socio-economic situation is almost normal, with little impact. Cambodia has not declared a state of emergency, as some false media outlets have slandered and intimidated.
