According to a report by the Rice Federation of Cambodia, Cambodia achieved more than 300,000 tonnes of rice exports in the first four months of 2020, accounting for more than 48% of total exports in 2019.
Exports in the first four months amounted to 300,252 tons, an increase of 41% compared to the first four months of 2019, which exported only 213,763 tons. This is one of the most significant growth in Cambodia, achieving the highest export figures in the first four months of the year in the last 10 years.
In particular, for April 2020, despite the Royal Government of Cambodia's efforts to pay close attention to food security for the people of Cambodia by suspending the export of "white rice" for a short time, Cambodia's fragrant rice exports have been achieved. More than 69 thousand tons, which provides a high value for traders and traders in the rice sector.
Cambodia's rice exports in April 2020 observed that more than 39% were exported to European countries, more than 30% to China, more than 13% to ASEAN member countries, especially Malaysia and Brunei, and 18%. To other regions, including Australia and New Zealand, there has been a significant increase. Exports increased by more than 61% compared to April 2019.
"What we have seen in the last four months of strong growth is our new markets and the recovery of the European Union, our new markets are Hong Kong and Australia is booming," said Song Saran. "There has been a sharp increase."
