The use of digital systems and technology in Cambodia, despite the many developments in recent years. But this development is still seen as limited in both the public and private sectors.
But after Kovid 19 spread to Cambodia as a precautionary measure to prevent the spread of Kovid 19 by keeping gaps and reducing the number of encounters, both public and private institutions began to be forced to take action. Use technology and digital systems to facilitate work.
In addition, some meetings have shifted from face-to-face meetings to online meetings and job discussions, instead of online ones.
Not only in the field of employment, both public and private, in the field of education also turned to promote the use of digital to serve education.
Recognizing the value of digital and the evolution of digital in the world during the Fourth Industrial Revolution, the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports has pushed for the development of digital education in educational institutions. However, due to limited investment, the digital development in educational institutions has not progressed much.
