Court Detains 5 Murderers for Killing Women in Front of Wat Koh Kindergarten and Shocking Victims in Boeung Keng Kang District
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Hok Pov, Investigating Judge of the Phnom Penh Municipal Court, on the morning of April 30, 2020, issued an order to detain 5 defendants in the case of killing a woman in front of Wat Koh Kindergarten and shocking a person. The victim died in Boeung Keng Kang district for murder under Article 199 of the Penal Code.
The decision to detain the five defendants came after Phnom Penh Municipal Court Prosecutor Heng Pheng opened an investigation and decided to formally charge him after criminal investigations by the Ministry of Interior. The group was arrested one by one in Phnom Penh after a group of suspects attacked and killed a woman in front of Wat Koh Kindergarten.
Please be reminded that the 5 perpetrators were arrested by the Criminal Police Office of the Criminal Police Department in cooperation with the Inspectorate Force of Daun Penh, Khan Meanchey, Khan Boeung Keng Kang, Criminal Police Force of Phnom Penh and Kandal Provincial Police. The night of April 25, 2020. Visit the gallery of international events of April 30, 2020 (Photo inside)
