During the launch, the team brought humanitarian donations to seven vulnerable, elderly and helpless families, with each family receiving rice, noodles, fish sauce, soy sauce, sugar, salt, cooking oil, hand soap and some money. Ministry of Tourism sets new tourism business standards in Kovid era
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Tourism has started to set new standards in the Kovid era for three tourism businesses: accommodation services, catering services and community-resort tourism services to re-launch tourism activities or tourism movements in the country, which ensures safety and health. Of all citizens and tourists.
The new tourism business standard will be officially announced by the end of May 2020. Tourism businesses that are still valid must apply to the new standard, while businesses that apply for a new license must also comply with the new standard.
The statement was made during a meeting between the Ministry of Tourism and the private sector in the tourism sector to find a solution to the impact of tourism due to the crisis of Kovi 19 under the chairmanship of Mr. Thong Khon, Minister of Tourism on the morning of 30 April 2020 at the Ministry of Tourism.
Along with the revival of domestic tourism activities, the Ministry of Tourism also requires tourism business owners in those areas to follow the regulations and guidelines on health safety recommended by the Royal Government and the Ministry of Health in the most accurate. Its business base.
At the meeting, Minister Thong Khon advised, "In the face of the fact that the new standard has not been issued yet, if there are tourists to visit or there is a need for tourism services, the Department of Tourism, Tourism Business must receive guests as usual, whether national tourists or No foreign tourists.
Another necessary task for tourist resorts is to develop aesthetics, pay attention to hygiene standards, clean bathrooms, the yard must have a clean environment.
The Minister of Tourism also warned that if any tourism business owners do not follow the policies, regulations and hygiene standards of the Royal Government, the Ministry of Health and the relevant ministries, they will face the suspension of business activities or lead to To close the business completely.
