Rural Development Bank Continues to Promote Low Interest Rate Loans under the Royal Government's $ 50 Million Special Financing Program in Banteay Meanchey Province
(Banteay Meanchey): Mr. Kao Thach, Director General of Rural Development Bank and Agriculture and his colleagues this morning, April 30, 2020, attended a presentation on the possibility of providing low interest rate loans under the Royal Special Financing Program. The government will provide $ 50 million to farmers raising fish, chickens, ducks, vegetables and small and medium-sized enterprises in the agro-processing industry.
According to the Governor of Banteay Meanchey Province, there are 41 farming communities in Banteay Meanchey Province with a total of 4,668 members and 331 family members are engaged in vegetable and fruit growing business, aquaculture, fish farming and frog farming. There are a total of 442 families in the livestock business, 235 families.
In addition, with the attention of General Ke Kim Yan, Deputy Prime Minister and Chairman of the National Authority for Combating Drugs, Banteay Meanchey Provincial Administration has organized three working groups to help farmers, including:
* Group 1: Inspect the reservoir and promote agriculture and animal husbandry * Group 2: In charge of the fund of General Ke Kim Yan, Deputy Prime Minister to support the agricultural production of farmers * Group 3: In charge of promoting Farmers' agricultural production market.
Loans Under this special program, the Rural Development and Agriculture Bank can provide up to 80% of the value of the collateral, which is the real estate, and the acceptance of the collateral is also very flexible by accepting equipment, machinery, inventory, guarantee letter from the parties. Buyers or other guarantees, certificates of deposit other than real estate (land and buildings).
In addition to the Royal Government's special loan of US $ 50 million, the Bank for Rural Development and Agriculture also offers a variety of low-interest loan products, and Mr. Kao Thach also encourages aspiring farmers. Credit may consider making an application.
The Director General of the Bank for Rural Development and Agriculture also thanked the Governor of Banteay Meanchey for facilitating the meeting to disseminate the low-interest credit policy under the special program of the Royal Government, especially for farmers, fish, chickens, ducks, vegetables. And handicraft groups of small and medium enterprises in the field of agricultural product processing, agro-industry, community agriculture in Banteay Meanchey province.
