Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng: Authorities will not stop people traveling in accordance with traffic laws to ask for documents (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng, Deputy Prime Minister, Minister of Interior and Chairman of the National Security Committee Road traffic confirmed that the authorities will not stop the compatriots who travel with respect to traffic laws to ask for documents.
Samdech stated that the right traveler can travel smoothly, except when traveling in violation of the law at any point, such as not wearing a helmet or violating traffic lights, then the authorities prevented from traveling and began to ask for documents.
He stressed that for this reason, the National Road Safety Committee has decided to set 2020 as the year to increase law enforcement than any other year, which is not a measure. Put the burden on the people in the difficult situation of Kovid 19 but for the safety, security, public order and social security.
When announcing the measure, the prince added that some views suggested that the measure was an administrative control measure. The prince explained that this was not the case and did not mean that the Ministry of Interior, the General Commissioner or the traffic police unit, which led and enforced the law, wanted money from the people. Instead, it is about keeping money and keeping people safe.
Samdech reminded that in the past, the Khmer Rouge regime had taught a clear lesson that the political leadership that did not meet the needs of the people created havoc for the nation and soon the regime collapsed.
