Equipped 434 police officers to transfer duties and appoint positions in Preah Vihear province
(Preah Vihear): 434 National Police officers of Preah Vihear Provincial Police have been promoted and transferred on April 30, 2020 in the presence of Major General Sous Sok Dara, Preah Vihear Provincial Police Commissioner. Attended by Deputy Commissioner and many other police officers.
Major General Sous Sok Dara congratulated the 434 National Police officers who have been promoted, transferred and appointed, and this is in return for the merits of our National Police officers. In fulfilling the task of maintaining security and order for the people and the society.
Lt. Gen. Sous Sok Dara advised all new police officers, whether new or old, to continue to work hard and not to threaten their newly acquired roles, duties and merits. The weak must perform their duties and responsibilities in accordance with the laws and regulations, and if they violate the laws and regulations, their superiors will inevitably be punished for their crimes.
The Major General confirmed that after receiving the new position and merit, please do not commit any crime, violate the rules and instructions of the leadership, please work together to implement the task as soon as possible for the unit. Family and myself as well.
The Commissioner continued that all must respect the traffic law, and from May 1, this is the day that the Royal Government, Ministry of Interior, National Police General Commission announced the restrictions on the implementation of the road traffic law, so we all We must all respect each other properly.
Major General Sous Sok Dara issued an order to the National Police officers in Preah Vihear province regarding the use of irregular or incomplete license plates, including civilian "People's" license plates, state license plates and the National Police, especially if known. That the license plate is not normal, must be removed immediately, and the first to implement is a police officer in Preah Vihear province.
The commissioner also stated that many other measures have been put in place for provincial police officers to implement, such as providing public services as soon as possible, and taking measures to solve problems for the people in a timely manner. Citizens are happy with all plans to crack down on all illegal crimes, including gambling, drugs, gangsters, on time and without exception.
