(Stung Treng): A total of 58 fishing communities across Stung Treng province and representatives of fishing communities at the district and provincial levels, a total of 58 people, attended a meeting with officials of Stung Treng Provincial Fisheries Administration to discuss and find common solutions. Campaign to protect all species of fish during the closed fishing season in 2020.
Please note that the closed fishing season every year in Stung Treng will be implemented from May 1 to September 30. Pursuant to the Notification No. 198/20 dated 17 April 2020 of the Stung Treng Provincial Administration on the closed fishing season in Stung Treng Province, fishing with all kinds of nets is strictly prohibited for the convenience of fish. All kinds of offspring can circulate to lay eggs.
The notice also strictly prohibits the use of illegal fishing equipment such as electric shocks, fish poisons and explosives.
According to Mr. Tum Niro, Director of Stung Treng Fisheries Administration, the campaign in 2019, which was the year to start restricting fishing in the off-season, found that the implementation was about 70 to 80% effective, which could help. More than 3,000 tons of all species of spawning fish have spawned and could hold tens of millions of juveniles.
According to many communities, fishing offenses in Stung Treng province have been reduced by no less than 70%, while the remaining offenses today are the most covert.
Finally, both fisheries experts and local communities call on and urge all fishermen to immediately stop fishing that leads to the destruction of fishery resources and to jointly protect these rare resources to Ensure sustainability for future generations. Sar Thet lays the foundation stone for the construction of a new CPP headquarters in Sangkat Boeung Tumpun I, Khan Meanchey
