First: Support from various philanthropists totaling 14,011,557 US dollars. Second: Leaders and public officials donated a salary of 38,165,053,367 riels or about 9.3 million US dollars. Ministry of Economy launches "Cambodian Entrepreneurship Assistance Package" to facilitate small and medium enterprises and start-ups from the effects of the Kovid-19 crisis
The Cambodian Entrepreneur Assistance Package is a strategic solution to some of the challenges that small and medium enterprises and start-ups in Cambodia are currently facing. The package aims to partially support small and medium enterprises and start-ups to return to normal operations after the situation of the Kovid-19 crisis has eased.
The Cambodian Entrepreneurship Assistance Package will provide support to small and medium enterprises and start-ups in various forms, such as investment assistance funds, the provision of training, risk management consulting and joint office space.
Cambodian Entrepreneurs believes that the Cambodian Entrepreneurship Assistance Program will be one of the strategic assistance activities and projects of the Royal Government of Cambodia to support entrepreneurship and the Cambodian economy during and after the impact of the global crisis.
Cambodian Entrepreneurs was established as an operator of the Entrepreneurship Development Fund (CSF) under the auspices of the Ministry of Economy and Finance to implement support programs and work directly with partner institutions and beneficiaries.
