(Phnom Penh): On April 30, 2020, it has been 21 years since Cambodia became a member of ASEAN. The fact that Cambodia has become a member of ASEAN is a diplomatic achievement of Cambodia under the leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister, and the Deputy Prime Minister, Hor Namhong, who was then the Senior Minister and Minister of Foreign Affairs as an outstanding staff.
The recognition of Cambodia as the 10th ASEAN member was made when Vietnam hosted the ASEAN Summit. Mr. Hor Namhong led the delegation to complete the procedures to become a member of ASEAN on April 30, 1999.
Deputy Prime Minister Hor Namhong reminded that since Cambodia became a member of ASEAN, Cambodia has worked hard to meet the needs of ASEAN. In particular, made several diplomatic movements to ask ASEAN member countries to support Cambodia's candidacy.
Deputy Prime Minister Hor Namhong expressed his excitement and honor that he was honored by Samdech Techo Hun Sen to represent Cambodia and become a member of ASEAN. The Deputy Prime Minister, who is considered a talented diplomat, recalled that he was very excited when the Cambodian flag was slowly hoisted to equal the flags of other ASEAN member countries. .
