Royal Government Prepares $ 300 Million for Social Protection and Food Security During the Kovid-19 Crisis
(Phnom Penh): Ms. Chou Bun Eng, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Interior and Permanent Vice President of the National Committee for Combating Human Trafficking (NEC), said that the Royal Government has prepared a budget of $ 300 million to support social and security. Food during the Kovid-19 crisis.
Ms. Chou Bun Eng made this statement on April 29, 2020, on the occasion of the National Committee for Combating Human Trafficking in collaboration with the International Organization for Migration (IOM) on a meeting on cooperation in response to the Kovid 19 crisis among migrant workers. Districts and communities at the Ministry of Interior, with the participation of UN agencies, IOM leaders and officials, as well as relevant national and international partner organizations.
According to Ms. Chou Bun Eng, the Royal Government of Cambodia has even considered both workers who are abroad and in the country. In the case of migrant workers, it is the responsibility of the target country to provide for them in times of need during the 1940 Kovid crisis, but in the case of repatriated workers, it is the responsibility of the Royal Government of Cambodia.
She said the government already has a policy in place to provide social protection assistance as well as to improve the living standards of migrant workers on food security issues. As for the implementation of the policy, it is a national action, which means that both the protection of Kovid 19 and the promotion of health is the Ministry of Health of Mr. Mam Bunheng led the work in this area.
