(Kampong Chhnang): Farmers who are engaged in farming have started to plow their fields gradually after a heavy downpour to irrigate their fields. .
The fact that farmers started plowing and sowing their fields at the beginning of the season was due to natural conditions, with early rains, which gave them the opportunity to plow and sow rice at the beginning of the year and There is time to travel and do other business.
A brother who is a farmer living in O'Kambon village, Chrey Bak commune, Rolea Bier district, described that our farmers who are engaged in farming have to sow the seedlings first before removing the seedlings for transplanting. Further, for sowing the seedlings, it also needs to be watered to plow the soil, leave the weeds to die before plowing a second time and sowing rice.
But now about 80 percent of our farmers no longer sow seedlings to transplant as before, and as long as it rains, they can plow sharply, they just plow the land and sow the rice and clear it when the rice grows. Once the fertilizer is applied, the fertilizer should be applied and then sprayed with herbicide only once or twice.
