Brokers use tricks to encroach on more than 100 hectares of Tuol Ponrei reservoir land in Kraing Yov commune, Kandal province, residents urge authorities and officials to take immediate action
(Kandal): A group of brokers (land brokers) used tricks by using some villagers as a shield to encroach on more than 100 hectares of Tuol Ponrei reservoir land in Kraing Yov commune, Saang district, Kandal province. Residents who own land there have urged the relevant authorities and officials to take immediate action against these brokers.
According to the Fresh News Agency, which received information from local authorities and the families of the victims, the traders had been buying the land from residents but had only handed over the deposit. Twenty percent, and the rest of the money is not handed over, everyone does this at once, do not know if they take these 20 percent agreement to run anything else.
Letter of deposit The land broker completes the contract and gives one to each party. As for the deed of sale and transfer of land tenure, the land brokers ordered the villagers to give their thumbprints without filling in the blanks, and the land brokers did not hand over the land to the landowners. No, they say, to get the company to fill out a card application.
At this point, it is the trick of the traders by using the people as a shield to swallow the land of the Tuol Ponrei reservoir, which is state land as legal ownership land. The reason why the company is doing this is in line with Mr. Ty Sokun, the head of the national working group to help Kraing Yov commune, who had previously announced that he would ask the Ministry of Land Management, Urban Planning and Construction to promote the issuance of land titles to people in Kraing Yov commune.
But so far, the contract has expired, considering the period of some pre-sale and post-sale sellers more than half a year ago, but the company not only did not return the money under the contract, but also reduced the price per hectare $ 10,000. Ten thousand dollars).
Residents state that these are the problems that make them very worried: firstly, they are worried when they agree to reduce the price and the company still refuses to pay the full amount and secondly, they are afraid of losing their land because the company took their land. They resell to other companies because they have already given their thumbprints on the deed of sale and the deed of land tenure.
