(Phnom Penh): After a careful search, the gunman who shot a man in Daun Penh district, Phnom Penh, on April 26, 2020, was cracked down by the police along National Road No. 41. Chum Kiri, Kampot province, where the assailant was fleeing on the afternoon of April 28, 2020.
Brigadier General Cheav Vibol, Deputy Director of the Criminal Police Department, said that the crackdown was carried out by the Criminal Police Department in cooperation with the Kampot Provincial Police, Daun Penh District and the Phnom Penh Municipal Police at Kampot Village, Sre Cheng Commune, Chum Kiri District, Kampot Province.
The operation was carried out under the direct command of General Dr. Neth Savoeun, National Police Commissioner, Lt. Gen. In Bora, Deputy National Police Commissioner, and with the guidance of Lt. Gen. Neng Chuor, Director of the Criminal Police Department. Method from Mr. Keo Sothea, Prosecutor of the Phnom Penh Municipal Court.
Brigadier General Cheav Vibol told Fresh News this morning, April 29, 2020, that the suspect who was detained by the police was named Keo Rathavitya, 29 years old, a police officer working in the Drug Office of the Commission. The Phnom Penh Municipal Police has the rank of lieutenant colonel.
Based on the results of the investigation of the suspect's confession, the Criminal Police Department concluded that Keo Ratthavithya actually exploded a weapon, causing serious injuries in front of House 50, Street 51, Village 10, Sangkat Phsar Thmei 3, Khan Daun Penh, Phnom Penh. On April 26, 2020.
According to Brigadier General Cheav Vibol, the specialized force of the Criminal Police Department is currently building a case to deal with the procedure and ready to send the suspect to the Phnom Penh Municipal Court on April 30, 2020 tomorrow. Singer Khat Sokhim, a representative of many families, gathered in front of the Siem Reap Provincial Court to demand that the case of Mr. Dim Suon Nath, President of Inarita, be expedited
