(Phnom Penh): So far, all public and private institutions in Cambodia are working closely together to prevent the spread of COVID-19. The religious sector has also played an important role in disseminating educational content to guide its followers to follow the guidelines of the Royal Government.
At a press conference on "Update on the COVID-19 disease of the Christian community" organized by the Spokesperson of the Royal Government on the afternoon of April 28, 2020, Mr. Heng Cheng, Senior Priest of the Christian Church, affirmed That Christians in Cambodia have taken action and are committed to joining the Royal Government in the fight against Kovid 19.
Mr. Heng Cheng said that after the Ministry of Cults and Religions convened a meeting with representatives of each religion, the evangelicals organized according to the Ministry's set and guidelines to continue education in each church, especially all pastors. In particular, the guidelines of the Ministry of Health.
The Christian High Priest also said that this April, Christians always commemorate two festivals, but this festival is not held by large gatherings and worship, but to honor. According to the Royal Government's preventive measures to prevent COVID-19 in Cambodia. He said they turned to worship at their respective homes.
He also claimed that Christian leaders had published posters and produced videos to distribute and disseminate to churches about daily hygiene guidelines and measures. There are also broadcasts on Christian social media and radio.
"We Christians listen to what the Ministry of Health is doing, and we are listening to the Ministry of Cults and Religions in line with government policy," said Heng Cheng. "We have stopped a lot of worship, and in particular each church has started to focus on educating the community around it and starting to care about vulnerable people, especially the low-income people."
