How to cut trees so as not to touch the temples in Angkor?
(Siem Reap): Ta Prohm is commonly known as a temple rich in large trees growing in the temple area, because those trees are attractive to tourists, but it is also a source of risk to the temple because the trees They can collapse due to various natural factors, such as wind.
When the trees fall on the temple, the work of removing the trees is a big challenge for the forestry team, because if the work of removing the trees is not technically correct, it can easily cause the rocks to fall. Therefore, high techniques are needed to remove those trees.
Meak Bora, technical officer of the Department of Forest Management, Landscape, Culture and Environment, said that the cutting of large trees that fall on the temple needs to be strong at the bottom and cut the tree into small pieces. Lift the meat to lighten the weight and easily lift it. This will keep both the team safe and avoid damaging the temple.
