(Phnom Penh): On April 28, 2020, Mr. Kouch Chamroeun, Governor of Preah Sihanouk Province, led professional officers and Prey Nup District Authority to inspect the location of Heng Heng Company's shrimp farm in O Ta Sek Village, O Oknha Heng Commune, Prey Nup District, Preah Sihanouk Province.
Mr. Kouch Chamroeun supported Heng Heng Company, which raises shrimp naturally in Prey Nob District, Sihanoukville Province to supply the local market, and encouraged the company to expand its breeding to supply the local market and export to foreign countries.
On that occasion, Mr. Kouch Chamroeun advised the commune authorities, districts, departments, specialized units to take care to facilitate the company to develop this natural shrimp farm to be more active. He believes that raising shrimp will help increase employment for local people, reduce the import of shrimp from neighboring countries into Cambodia.
Mr. Ly Teav Sear, President of Heng Heng Company, said that the company has raised 100 hectares of natural prawns by setting up 20% drainage ponds, so the remaining 80 hectares are shrimp ponds.
He said that his company started raising shrimp in June 2019 until now, gradually benefiting. Raising this shrimp for 3 months can be harvested. He said that per hectare of land can harvest shrimp from 2.5 tons to nearly 3 tons and can be harvested three times a year.
After harvesting, we have to clean the pond to put in the new shrimp. The company now has its own hatchery. He added that the shrimp that are being raised today are only for the local market and have not been exported yet.
