The planting activities and the following activities took place throughout April 27, 2020, with the participation of Mr. Moeng Soklat, Representative of Mr. Chea Sophara, Deputy Prime Minister, Minister of Land Management, Urban Planning and Construction, Mr. Soy Touch, Krouch Chhmar District Governor, as well as relevant departments, teachers, students and citizens.
At the same time, the Deputy Governor of Tbong Khmum Province also called on all media to protect the flooded forest, prevent the burning and clearing of flooded forest land in order to encroach on the land for illegal agriculture, which causes damage to the place. Fish spawning grounds and encourage people to plant more trees to improve the environment and for the benefit of our society.
According to Mr. Soy Touch, planting the seedlings on the entire flooded forest area is under the guidance of Mr. Chea Sophara in the vision of serving the spawning fish in the rainy season, we can pick the leaves. This bud or fruit can be used as a pickle for soup and in the direction of preserving the forest name not to be lost.
Krouch Chhmar District Governor added that the vision will develop from Prey Ronam, a wetland spawning ground, to become a conservation area, science, ecotourism and a biodiversity laboratory of Tbong Khmum province for the next generation of Cambodians. Others study, do internships as well.
