Authorities say the reason for the arrest of the Nigerian man was based on a complaint filed by a pregnant Cambodian woman and her Nigerian husband, who allegedly vandalized her property. He was beaten and stabbed with a knife, causing injuries, and escaped with $ 3,500 at 11:30 pm on April 27, 2020.
Police said that after receiving a complaint from the Deputy Prosecutor of the Phnom Penh Municipal Court, they surrounded a house in New World Borey Chamkar Dong and arrested the Nigerian.
The suspect is currently being held in custody at the Dangkor District Inspectorate for questioning to build a case to be sent to the Phnom Penh Municipal Court for legal action.
