(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Social Affairs, Veterans and Youth Rehabilitation on the morning of April 28, 2020, presented the difficulties and acknowledged the challenges in managing homeless people living in public places as they tried to avoid Live in a properly managed district.
Speaking at a press conference on "Progress and Continuation of the Ministry of Social Affairs" organized by the spokesman of the Royal Government, Mr. Touch Channy, spokesman of the Ministry of Social Affairs claimed that the Ministry has cooperated with relevant institutions to collect homeless people in public places. Take to live in the center to manage.
Mr. Touch Channy emphasized that after entering the center, all the homeless people always try to escape from the center without wanting to live under the control. He added that the reason they are trying to flee is because living outside can earn money by begging in public.
With this challenge, the spokesperson of the Ministry of Social Affairs said that despite the situation, the relevant ministries and institutions still use joint mechanisms to solve this problem, trying to explain to all homeless people to learn to live. In the center to get different knowledge and skills from the manager.
However, through this press conference, a reporter from Fresh News also asked a question related to the procedure for paying money to the families of veterans who seem to be late until the report from the people to the media. Well.
In response to this question, Mr. Touch Channy explained that he acknowledged that there was a delay in the past, which involved procedures and professional work, had to fill out the form and send it to the Ministry of Economy to get the money back in 2 days. Or 3 months.
But so far, he claimed that the relevant ministries and institutions are looking for a joint solution to expedite the payment. He added that the money was given directly to the family to repay the benefits, so it will not be too late.
