(Oddar Meanchey): The Sa Kaeo Dam in Chong Kal Commune, Chong Kal District, Oddar Meanchey Province has been extended by another 1.5 km to draw more water to meet the needs of the people to use and irrigate their crops.
Senior Minister Kun Kim, head of the Oddar Meanchey Provincial Assistance Team, said that Chong Kal commune is a remote area in Chong Kal district that does not have a source of water for extraction and irrigation. A few years ago, the authorities decided to build the Sa Kaeo dam to store water for people to use and irrigate their crops.
The senior minister said that until now, the number of people is increasing and the demand for water for irrigation is only increasing, so the water in the Sa Kaeo dam can not meet the needs of the people. In addition, the government plans to redevelop the area to accommodate more veterans, increasing the demand for water.
"People in this area need water for their daily use and for irrigating their crops. "Therefore, the demand for water here is very important, which is why we are considering expanding the Srah Keo dam to extract water and store more water for his people to use." This was confirmed by Senior Minister Kun Kim.
After seeing the need, Mr. Kun Kim also requested the intervention of Mr. Lim Kean Hor, Minister of Water Resources and Meteorology, to build and expand the dam. After requesting and seeing the need for water resources in the area, Minister Lim Kean Hor also assigned the director of the Provincial Water Resources Department to arrange the construction immediately.
Construction of the dam began on April 27, 2020. The construction of the additional dam was opened directly by Senior Minister Kun Kim, with the participation of Mr. Pen Kosal, Oddar Meanchey Provincial Governor, Director of the Department of Water Resources, Mr. Nhen Kuon and provincial authorities.
Mr. Nhen Kuon, Director of Oddar Meanchey Provincial Department of Water Resources and Meteorology, said that the dam will be 1.5 km long, 6 meters wide and 1 meter high. There is also a 45-meter-long, one-meter-high concrete drainage system.
The director of the department said that the construction of the additional dam is scheduled to take about two months. Once completed, the dam will be able to store up to 8.5 million cubic meters of water, irrigating about 450 hectares of people's rice fields and 50 hectares of mixed crops.
On behalf of the National Task Force to assist Oddar Meanchey province and on behalf of the people who benefit from this dam, Senior Minister Kun Kim thanked Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, for always caring for the people in the suburbs. Domain in Oddar Meanchey province and always help solve and meet all the needs of the people in this province.
The Senior Minister also thanked Mr. Lim Kean Hor for expediting the construction of the dam after receiving the request one day.
Water is an indispensable source of water for people in rural areas, especially in remote areas without water sources, such as in Chongkal district for consumption and irrigation. After seeing the national team led by Senior Minister Kun Kim and the relevant authorities to jointly build and expand the Sa Kaeo Dam, the people in the area were very excited and happy.
The people in that area would like to thank Samdech Techo, Senior Minister Kun Kim, Mr. Lim Kean Hor, as well as all relevant authorities who always think about their well-being and solve all their problems.
