(Phnom Penh): The Prime Minister of Cambodia Samdech Techo Hun Sen on the evening of April 27, 2020 confirmed that the Royal Government has now decided to allow more than 200 workers who are staying in Malaysia to return to Cambodia if the Malaysian authorities confirm that There is no Kovid 19 disease.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that if Cambodian workers living in Malaysia are found to have Kovid, they need to be treated there before they can be allowed to return to Cambodia. Separately, for those who do not have Kovid 19 when they arrive in Cambodia, they also need to have a 14-day cataract (living separately) to continue to monitor their health.
(Siem Reap): The crisis of the Kovid-19 epidemic has severely affected Cambodia's tourism sector, with international tourists unable to travel abroad and national tourists staying at home. Going out makes the tourist resorts face a shortage of tourists, including Siem Reap-Angkor is no different.
But a new kind of tourism venue has also emerged in Angkor-Siem Reap, with most locals and tourists flocking to the World Heritage Site for cycling or jogging.
They cycled from Siem Reap to Angkor Park, mostly passing in front of Angkor Wat, Phnom Bakheng, entering Angkor Thom through the gates of the Om River, Bayon Temple, Baphuon Temple, the Terrace of the Elephants. Arriving at this place, some people take a break and others continue to travel along the small circle through the gate of the garden of the Apsara Authority, Takeo, Ta Prohm, Banteay Kdei, Srah Srang, Kravan.
Meanwhile, some continue from the Terrace of the Elephants to the main ring road through the gates of the pottery, the temple of Kralo Romeas, the temple of Preah Khan, the northern baray with the Neak Pean temple in the middle, the Kralokor temple, the Ta Som temple, the eastern baray and the Mebon Khang temple. Born in the form of a temple in the form of Srah Srang, etc., and continued to Kasindhu, east of Angkor Wat.
According to Mr. Ngov Sengkak, there are not many foreign tourists in Siem Reap at present, most of the tourists who like to ride the exercise bike are mostly from Siem Reap and other districts in the Angkor area, while the international visitors are also Residents of Siem Reap for many years, while some are teachers, businessmen, businessmen, individuals, NGOs and so on.
Residents and tourists, most of whom live in Siem Reap, have expressed their enjoyment of such sports tourism.
A spokesman for the APSARA Authority also urged residents as well as tourists who enjoy cycling in the Angkor resort area not to bring bicycles or other vehicles near the temple or any structure of the temple, such as stone. The gates, walls, temples, etc., by the people, tourists can rest or park their vehicles in a suitable place, this call is also to prevent risks as well as for the personal safety of tourists.
The director of the Siem Reap Provincial Department of Tourism, Mr. Ngov Sengkak, praised that the participation in the exercise of cycling in the Angkor area has also contributed to the traders in Angkor to get some income by selling cakes, coconut water, pure water, drinks. Other food for cyclists, exercisers, and traders who sell bicycles and accessories in Siem Reap are the happiest.
