Heng Sour made the remarks at a press conference on the current status of the factory workers who take time off during the New Year holiday. This conference was organized by the Spokesperson of the Royal Government at the Office of the Council of Ministers on the afternoon of April 27, 2020.
Heng Sour said that when countries in Europe and the United States were affected by Kovid-19, they closed their markets and people no longer had to spend money, which increased the demand for clothes. Shoes, textiles and other goods were drastically reduced.
Mr. Heng Sour said that this has led to a large number of textile, garment and footwear factories in Cambodia have applied to suspend production and closed. However, due to the coordination efforts between the relevant parties, both the Royal Government, the employers and the workers have facilitated the request for closure to a temporary suspension.
According to Heng Sour, so far, more than 130 factories have applied for suspension, including nearly 100,000 workers affected by the suspension, and the government has taken a series of measures to Keep jobs, save some income for those workers as well.
Although the parties seem to be easing each other, the export of textiles, clothing and footwear is also gradually affected by the first quarter of 2020, the export of textiles, clothing and footwear. And shoes are about 80 percent more compared to the same period in 2019.
Mr. Heng Sour stated that as of April 27, 2020, Cambodia has not yet received orders from buyers for May and June, as well as the next period, which can be concluded that Cambodia's exports of textiles, clothing and footwear will be hit hard in the second quarter of 2020.
(Phnom Penh): While the Royal Government of Cambodia encourages educational institutions to continue to help students to further their knowledge, including electronic or remote learning to avoid Kovid 19, the Australian Center for Training (ACE) has launched a curriculum using New and modern e-learning technology and programs.
By providing 200 full-year scholarships, this venue will provide this quality education opportunity to students who may be struggling to continue their education or have financial difficulties during this difficult time.
