(Phnom Penh): The Head of the Royal Government of Cambodia, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, has issued a decision on the establishment of a technical working group for the harmonization of the registration system and management of social protection data. This is according to the decision that Fresh News received on April 27, 2020.
According to the decision, the technical working group for the harmonization of the registration system and management of social protection data has the following roles and responsibilities:
* Study on the overview and challenges of the registration system and the information technology system related to the social protection work that has been underway
* Develop strategies and action plans on the possibility of connecting or integrating the registration system or information system related to the existing social protection system to a level that does not affect the privacy of personal information.
* Advise the Executive Committee of the National Council for Social Protection and coordinate with relevant institutions, including state institutions, development partners and private institutions on the work related to the installation and modification of the registration system and information technology system related to the social protection system to be able to Interoperable with each other
* Regularly report to the Executive Committee and the National Council for Social Protection on the progress of the development of registration and information technology systems related to social protection.
Perform other duties as determined by the National Council for Social Protection.
