Ministry of Planning Prepares to Implement Identification of Poor Families During Combat COVID-19
(Phnom Penh): The Honorable Dr. Chhay Thorn, Senior Minister and Minister of Planning, on April 27, 2020, chaired a meeting to prepare for the implementation of the identification of poor families as requested during the fight against Kovit-19.
Senior Minister Chhay Thorn stated that almost all countries in the world, and in particular for Cambodia, we are affected by the spread of Kovid-19, which the Royal Government of Cambodia is looking to provide immediate and immediate intervention to all Cambodians. Affected by using poor household data produced by the Ministry of Planning's poor household identification procedure.
Poor household data is used for interventions and policies, especially for the National Social Protection Policy Framework 2016-2025, along with a proposal for the development and series of poor household data, the Ministry of Planning has identified family identities. Poverty systematically implemented by 8 or 9 provincial capitals per year and updated every 3 years.
At the same time, the Ministry of Planning has continued to revise the questionnaire and database of poor families to diversify the data, such as: poor families with HIV and AIDS, poor families with disabled members, families of veterans, poor families who There is old age and so on.
As a result, as of 2015, ministries, institutions, the Royal Government, national and international organizations have used data on poor households for 136 projects and programs, equivalent to 63% of total national development projects and programs, as a basis for providing assistance and services to families. Poor.
The Ministry of Planning is very proud that poor family identification data is widely used by the Royal Government and development partners for interventions to help poor people or poor families, such as:
Since the beginning of 2020, almost all countries around the world, including Cambodia, we are affected by the spread of Kovid-19, and the Royal Government of Cambodia is looking to provide immediate and immediate intervention to all affected Cambodians. This impact is based on the Ministry of Planning's data on poor households, especially the poorest and most affected households.
To facilitate people's livelihoods and reduce the impact of the Kovid-19 epidemic, the Royal Government has decided to provide cash assistance to poor families who already have equity cards and some poor families who are absent through data collection and Some families have just been affected by loss of income and falling into poverty due to Kovit-19 disease.
The results of the meeting decided that the Ministry of Planning should update the data on poor households, which are (1) rural areas to be completed before the end of May 2020 and (2) urban areas before the end of June 2020 using Mechanisms for identifying poor households on request and in consultation with villages and communes in case of removal of dominant families.
Therefore, in order to achieve this success, Senior Minister Chhay Thorn proposed to the Director of the Department of Planning as follows:
The Department of Poor Family Identification of the General Department of Planning, Ministry of Planning, will soon hold a training course on the procedures for identifying poor households as requested during the Kovid-19 outbreak, as decided by the Ministry of Economy and Finance.
