China is building a telescope to detect spacecraft signals to be sent to Mars by 2020
BEIJING: China is building a telescope for Asia's largest rotating radio receiver, with its antenna plate 70 meters in diameter, to receive data from its first exploration mission. On Mars, which will be launched this year. This was released by the Xinhua news agency on Monday afternoon, April 27, 2020.
The giant telescope system is under construction in Tianjin, near Beijing. Its construction began in October 2018 and is expected to be completed this year in line with the Mars reconnaissance mission.
The telescope will be a key location for receiving scientific data sent back to Earth by Chinese spacecraft on Mars, which will be at a distance of up to 400 million kilometers from our planet. Will be weak to require modern and large equipment to absorb.
