This decision was made after the Constitutional Council held a meeting on the morning of April 27, 2020 to review and decide on the request of Samdech Heng Samrin, President of the National Assembly, to review the constitution of the law on governing the country. In an emergency.
Please be informed that the draft law on "governing the country in a state of emergency" passed the Senate with the approval of 54 to 54 votes on the morning of April 17, 2020 to pave the way for this draft law. Reaching the announcement in the near future.
The "Draft Law on the Management of Emergencies in Emergencies" consists of 5 chapters and 12 articles prepared by the Royal Government to guide the country when placed in a state of emergency, approved by the National Assembly in its morning plenary session. April 10, 2020.
The "Draft Law on Emergency Management" will provide a legal basis to ensure the implementation of the new Article 22 of the Constitution and a legal basis to determine the Royal Government's authority to take the necessary measures. To respond to the country's emergency situation, to protect security, public order, protect the life and health of the people, as well as protect property and the environment.
(Kampong Chhnang): A surprise occurred at Thmor Kral Waterfall Natural Resort, located in Chamka Moch Village, Chiep Commune, Teuk Phos District, Kampong Chhnang Province, after a group of four Cambodian tourists went for a walk. In the forest and lost for 9 hours, the authorities found.
Of the six tourists, four, including a woman, walked up to the top of the mountain, a waterfall called "Sre Taek", which they climbed from 2 p.m. At 8 pm, they could not find their way back, so the two people below were upset and called the police to come and help with the search.
He added that after hearing this news to the Governor of Kampong Chhnang, Mr. Chhour Chandoeun, the provincial governor also ordered the forces, including district authorities, district inspectors, tourism officials, local authorities, local people to protect the environmental forces stationed in the area. Many people came to explore different areas, the search lasted until 10:47 pm, only to find the four were walking in the forest on the top of the mountain.
When the coalition forces brought them back down, the wanderers said that they were happy here, they did not go back, and even wanted to escape the coalition forces, but were stopped by the search team and Comforting them to come back down with only one side, they decided to come down with that search force.
It should be noted that while the coalition forces were searching for the four above in the forest, an old man, an elder in the area, predicted that the four of them were going for a walk in the mountains. No danger. He said do not worry, and when the four of them came down, he also sprinkled water on them for peace and prosperity.
Mr. Seng Saly also stated that all tourist sites and resorts in Kampong Chhnang Province are not banned by the Ministry of Tourism, but the Ministry of Tourism also recommends national and international visitors. Entertainment at various resorts in accordance with the safety principles of the authorities.
Thmar Kral Waterfall is a good natural resort in Kampong Chhnang province, but tourists are not familiar with it because this natural resort is hidden until they can make their way there.
Thmor Kral Waterfall Natural Resort is located in Koh Khtom Village, Chiep Commune, Teuk Phos District, Kampong Chhnang Province. If you travel from Phnom Penh on National Road No. 5 to Kampong Tralach District around School No. 5, Thmor Kral Waterfall Natural Resort is located on the left hand side of this road, that is, this resort is located in the western part of Kampong Chhnang Province, about 50 Km.
Wanting to visit the natural rock waterfall resort is not difficult because the community of the area has created easy access roads. Tourists can also use motorbikes or cars to drive on the black asphalt road and continue on the red gravel road until this ideal location.
Phnom Penh Capital Hall and US Embassy Plant Nearly 1,000 Trees Along National Road 6A, Expand Green Cover and Environment to Reduce Urban Climate Change
(Phnom Penh): Nearly 1,000 heavy trees have been planted by Phnom Penh authorities along National Road 6A from Brahma 4 roundabout to Wat Varin, Sangkat Prek Leap in Chroy Changvar district in order to enhance the green beauty. And promote the aesthetics of a clean environment in Phnom Penh.
The tree planting ceremony will be held this morning, April 27, 2020, in front of Wat Mongkul Serey Kien Khleang, presided over by Mr. Nuon Pharath, Deputy Governor of Phnom Penh, on behalf of Mr. Khuong Sreng, Governor of Phnom Penh, and Mr. Michael Ubiel, Ambassador of the United States Embassy in Phnom Penh. In Cambodia, with the participation of Mr. Khleang Huot, Governor of Chroy Changvar District and Mr. Koam Seiha, Director of Phnom Penh Forestry Administration.
Mr. Nuon Pharath continued that the planting of trees now is a small step in a long step for the development of Phnom Penh, green cover, which will expand and contribute to the beauty of Phnom Penh, as well as reduce the impact of Climate change, too.
"Phnom Penh, we have organized a smart city with a green cover," he said. "We already have plans for urban development projects 2015 ~ 2035, such as road construction projects as well as drainage canals, and this project has already been established, that is, still implemented successfully."
He added that a small number of people hate trees because the trees in front of his house affect their business and daily business, but most people love trees because of the trees outside. The green shade is beautiful and it further reduces the toxins in the environment, meaning there are trees, there is hope.
Michael Yubiel, US Ambassador to Cambodia, said the tree planting was to mark the 70th anniversary of Cambodia-US relations, which this month focused on environmental issues.
Michael Yubiel stated that the planting of trees is to confirm the long-standing relationship between the two countries.
The director of the Phnom Penh Forestry Administration confirmed that along National Road 6A, the Phnom Penh Capital Administration plans to plant 1,000 trees. But for now, we have planted 886 trees, which are pure thnong trees, starting from the base of the Chroy Changva bridge to the border of Kandal province.
He said that nearly a thousand heavy trees, which are between 4 and 6 years old, which the Phnom Penh Capital Administration received from the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries through the Forestry Administration were planted along the national road. No. 6 from Chroy Changvar roundabout to the border of Kandal province.
