(Phnom Penh): Dr. Hang Chuon Naron, Minister of Education, Youth and Sports, reminded young men and women students to increase self-study in the digital age to increase job opportunities that are full of competition.
In an interview on "Digital Education" via the Ministry of Education's Facebook page on Sunday, April 26, 2020, Minister Hang Chuon Naron said that young people must be adequately prepared for the labor market in In this digital age, because it is constantly changing and needs new skills constantly.
"Young people must strengthen their own activities, including self-study skills, research skills, the ability to use information technology, know how to use digital devices and other skills," he said.
"Young people need to be prepared for a labor market that is constantly changing," he added. "In this job market, we see that they will need new skills."
Dr. Hang Chuon Naron said that they do not know how the labor market will change in the next 20-30 years? Because technology is evolving so fast. Therefore, young people must have a strong foundation, have the qualities, have a positive attitude, and most importantly, lifelong learning.
The Minister also saw that to strengthen the knowledge capacity of young people in the digital age requires strengthening and management in schools. In other words, all schools need to improve school culture and improve the "learning and teaching" environment.
In the interview, Mr. Hang Chuon Naron also asked teachers and principals to be prepared to provide an education for young people to become good and active citizens, including skills, skills, behavior, fitness, good health to contribute. Socio-economic development in this digital age.
According to the Minister, in this digital age, the Ministry of Education has launched a number of educational programs. In fact, the Ministry has launched a new curriculum, a new generation of schools, in order to improve education in Cambodia, as in some countries in the region and the world.
There are currently 10 schools and are implementing this new generation school curriculum. There are 4 primary schools and 6 secondary schools. The curriculum focuses on integrating technology into the education of both learners and teachers, as well as providing a wide range of learning materials. North Korean media report Kim Jong Un's actions amid rumors that he is "dead" (Video inside)
