(Phnom Penh): Public servants are generally known as individuals who work in government ministries and institutions and play an important role in enforcing laws and regulations. During their missions, public officials often face obstacles, sometimes with a small number of individuals using violence and other forms of corruption to counter and prevent successful law enforcement.
Charges against public officials are enacted with the aim of preventing all abuses against public officials during the mission and ensuring the successful completion of the mission. According to Article 503 of the Penal Code of the Kingdom of Cambodia, "Opposition to a public official is an act of violent confrontation with a public official acting to enforce a public authority order or court decision." .
In summary, charges against public servants are enacted to prevent all abuses against public officials during the mission and to ensure the success of the mission, as well as to punish the perpetrators of the violence. All images on public officials and affect the public interest.
