(Kandal): Four military officers shot and killed his wife and then transported the body from Phnom Penh to Kandal province and called the police to arrest him without escaping.
The commissioner said that the murder occurred on National Road 2, Sangkat Chak Angre, Khan Meanchey, Phnom Penh.
According to Brigadier General Chhoeun Socheat, after shooting his wife in the car, the husband took his wife's body from the scene to Prek Run village, Prek Koy commune, Saang district, Kandal province. When he reached this point, he called the police to arrest him.
The suspected killer is 58-year-old Kim Sary, a military official at the Ministry of National Defense. The victim's wife, Som Sariep, 50, was born in Banteay Meanchey province.
