(Kampong Chhnang): The new port is used as a tourist station and a place to sell agricultural products, fish and other meat in Chhnuk Trou village, Chhnuk Trou commune, Baribo district, Kampong Chhnang province, about 70% completed. The new port is built on a land of about 6 hectares and has a height of 5 meters.
Mr. Saing Kimsorn, Chief of Chhnuk Trou Commune, said this morning, April 26, 2020, that the construction of this new port will make it easier for people to do business in Chhnuk Trou Commune, Boribo District. He added that although the country is in the midst of fighting against Kovid 19, the process of building the new port is still ongoing.
