A company invests in growing Sisal balm for silk, rope and sack production in Preah Vihear province, the Minister of Agriculture proposes to expand cultivation and open a processing plant as planned in 2021
(Preah Vihear): Mr. Veng Sakhon, Minister of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, accompanied by Mr. Ung Sam Ath, Secretary of State in charge of Forestry Administration, Mr. Keo Omalis, Royal Government of Cambodia Delegation in charge of Forestry Administration and colleagues this morning Come and check the progress of the development of silk crop of China Great Call in Rovieng district, Preah Vihear province.
The General Manager reported to Minister Veng Sakhon that the company develops 5,871 hectares of economic land concessions obtained from the Royal Government of Cambodia through the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries to cultivate Sisal balsam. Used as a raw material for the production of silk, rope, used in sacks, as a water-resistant product that sticks well.
In 2021, it is planned to set up a silk processing and processing plant and expand the cultivated area to increase the quantity to meet the factory demand. Two-year-old silk crop can be harvested three times a year, 25-30 tons per hectare per hectare, 3 tons of silk can be produced and 1 ton of silk is valuable. $ 1500-2000.
He added that it is an easy crop to grow, does not need soil, needs less water, resistant to hot weather and high yields.
After visiting the plantation, Minister Veng Sakhon praised and encouraged the company to expand the cultivated area according to the planned plan and set up a production and processing plant in time to participate in the development of this area. As a silk industry in the future and especially to create jobs and use labor in this area to the fullest extent possible.
