(Phnom Penh): The Higher Education Association, which has 113 member institutions, has appealed to parents of students in financial crisis to apply directly to the school and negotiate with the school for a discount.
In an appeal issued on April 24, 2020, the Higher Education Association noted that in the state of the 19-virus Kovid virus has spread to almost all sectors in Cambodia, including educational institutions throughout Cambodia. Educational services have been suspended since March 14, 2020.
The association pointed out that during the suspension period, 113 member educational institutions of the association experienced difficulties and severe impacts, such as having to continue to pay teachers and staff, continue to pay building fees and continue to pay. Money and bank principal, as well as many other expenses.
On the other hand, the members of the association are also facing more serious difficulties such as the decrease in the number of students, the reduction of fees by the association members themselves and the request for discounts by the parents and guardians of the students. Most of the members of the association dealt with the request for a discount on a case-by-case basis. The result is positive in a win-win way that is acceptable to all.
Responding to the protests of parents of students asking for a discount, the association calls on all parents or guardians of students to apply for a discount by informing the owner of the financial crisis caused by the Kovid 19 pandemic to the owner or Management of each private educational institution to help solve and alleviate as much as possible.
The Cambodian Higher Education Association has expressed strong belief that parents or guardians of students will work together to make concessions to each other and with the utmost patience in a win-win way to overcome this difficult stage. . Preah Vihear Provincial Governor Continues to Distribute CRC Donations to Poor People in Preah Vihear City
