Pailin Provincial Authority Visits and Provides Emergency Donations to People Affected by Typhoon
(Pailin): Mr. Phan Chanthul, Governor of Pailin Province, on April 24, 2020, accompanied by provincial leaders at all levels, as well as working groups and local authorities, visited and brought emergency donations to support the people. Residents reach homes affected by severe strong winds in 19 families in Stung Trang commune, Sala Krao district, Pailin province.
Emergency supplies include: 25 kg of rice, 1 noodle, 1 can of fish sauce, 1 can of soy sauce, 1 can of fish and 1 bottle of hand washing alcohol.
Mr. Phan Chanthul stated that the Royal Government of Cambodia, with Samdech Techo Sen as the Prime Minister, has made the country peaceful and has developed and developed in all fields, and has taken into account the well-being of the people throughout the country. By not allowing any citizen to starve to death unknowingly and unresolved.
Mr. Phan Chanthul warned all people to be very careful about their personal and family safety, as this season there is rain mixed with wind and thunder, which can be dangerous. If there is any problem, report it to the nearest local authority so that the team can help quickly and in time.
