The ceremony was held at the village of Kok village with the invitation of the provincial council, provincial governors, municipal councils, commune leaders, departments around the province, the three armed forces and many other youth groups.
Mr. Mao Thunin brought a message from Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, who always pays attention to the well-being of the people throughout the country, without leaving any of our people without food. That.
He added that working groups at all levels in Pursat province have set up an organic vegetable mechanism in this province in response to Samdech Techo's recommendation, which called on people to work hard to cultivate agricultural production, including animal husbandry, rice production and Combined crops to meet domestic demand in situations where the country is at risk of Kovid 19 pandemic.
Mr. Mao Thunin said that the use of natural fertilizers in the tradition of our ancestors on rice and other mixed crops really get higher yields and more expensive in the market than the use of chemical fertilizers.
He believes that the organic vegetable seeds distributed will be cultivated by the people using natural fertilizers to improve the family's livelihood and eat healthily together. At the same time, the provincial governor also announced the possibility of rehabilitating the natural waterways "lakes, canals or rivers" to use the land or water for agriculture and daily life to avoid being congested.
(Stung Treng): A suspect using illegal fishing gear was arrested by the community fishing force in cooperation with Koh Sampey River at 9:30 pm on April 23, 2020 at the Mekong River in Svay village. Koh Sralay Commune, Siem Bok District, Stung Treng Province.
According to Mr. Oeun Savoeun, River Guard at Koh Sampei Post, on April 24, 2020, his forces, along with fishing communities, patrolled the Mekong River every night, but found the suspect that night. Two boats are illegally fishing. His forces chased a boat, captured one boat, and the other escaped.
Mr. Oeun Savoeun said that the suspect arrested by his forces was Nher Raksmey, a 23-year-old man living in Phum Thmey, Sangkat Samaki, Stung Treng City. The suspect used illegal fishing gear and confessed to the fisheries authorities that he had indeed committed an illegal crime.
On the afternoon of April 24, the suspect and the exhibits were sent to Stung Treng Provincial Court by the Fisheries Special Forces to build a case according to the procedure.
