(Mondulkiri): Officials and residents of 6 district elephants are waiting to release the female elephants that were not allowed to go by the wild elephants, while this problem surprised the people living in Putrom village, Romnea commune, Sen Monorom city. Strongly after a herd of wild elephants rushed near the village to find females, causing safety concerns because the herd of wild elephants tried to follow the females of the females that were tied to the mouth of a stream near the village.
Mr. Prum Vibol Rattanak, Director of Keo Seima Wildlife Sanctuary, said that the herd of wild elephants that came to this female elephant has been 7 since the afternoon of April 22, 2020, of which 6 elephants have entered the forest. On the other hand, while one of the elephants refused to leave the place where the villagers took the four female elephants and tied them as usual.
Fearing a wild elephant would kill the female elephant, a group of five elephants, the owners of the four female elephants, tried to free the female elephant from the wild elephant, but their efforts failed, untying one female elephant. The wild elephants chased the wild elephants for many years and were stuck in the trees for many hours from morning until noon to get down from the trees. Run back to the village.
According to the description of the elephants that came to liberate their elephants, the elephants that tried to contact the three female elephants in the title were very fierce, big and tall, with one side open and big, and always raised their trunks. That it is ready to attack anyone who dares to approach. The group said that when they arrived at the place where the female elephants were tied up, they were able to untie the title of only one female elephant.
As of the afternoon of the 23rd, officials have not been able to rescue the three female elephants from the ferocious wild elephants. According to officials, in this case, they will wait a little longer for the elephant to calm down and return to the forest. But if the situation continues to drag on, professional officers may use a sniper rifle to knock it unconscious to free the female elephant from the scene.
The wild elephants at the Keo Seima Wildlife Sanctuary currently number more than 150 species of Asian elephants, and these wild elephants often leave the forest to enter the village, sometimes to eat crops in the villagers' fields. Subject: Destroy all drug resources! Nationwide drug crackdown for April 24: 25 cases cracked, 59 arrested
