(Phnom Penh): Senior Minister Sun Chanthol, Minister of Public Works and Transport, urged the Ministry's technical work officers to closely monitor companies implementing construction projects in Cambodia. He said that close monitoring by the Ministry's technical team is an effective strategy to encourage construction companies and technical consultants to implement the project properly in accordance with the load book to maintain road quality.
Senior Minister Sun Chanthol said this on April 24, 2020 at the Ministry's office while chairing a meeting to review the progress of the National Road 2 and National Road 22 upgrades. The meeting was also attended by Ministry leaders, leaders of the Department of Public Works and Transport of Kandal and Takeo provinces, project managers and project implementation officers of the Ministry.
Senior Minister Sun Chanthol emphasized that all projects being implemented in the territory of the Kingdom of Cambodia must have regular monthly meetings to regularly review the progress of the project, challenges and solutions aimed at the implementation of the project. Effectiveness, transparency and quality.
The Minister also requested that the technical consulting company report to the Ministry on the activities of the construction companies in order to find a timely settlement procedure in order for the projects to proceed and be completed according to the contract.
Mr. Sun Chanthol encouraged the project implementers to directly monitor the construction and technical provision of the technical consulting company and dare to say that it is wrong if the construction is technically wrong or different from the contract, because it is our way. If the construction is not quality, it is our burden and a waste of the national budget.
(Kampong Cham): Ms. Pang Dany, Deputy Governor of Kampong Cham Province, accompanied by relevant officials, visited and talked about health and hygiene education to more than 200 people from Thailand who were isolated for 14 days. Its home.
The ceremony was held at Vihear Thom pagoda, Vihear Thom commune, Kampong Siem district on April 24, 2020.
On that occasion, the Deputy Governor brought greetings from Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen and Mr. Un Chanda, Governor of Kampong Cham Province to the 208 people. All immigrants who have returned from Thailand have followed the Royal Government's instructions through a 14-day internship at their respective homes in the past.
Ms. Pang Dany explained the safety of migration, stating that legal migration brings safety to oneself, especially reducing risks such as abuse of sexual labor and Human trafficking and so on.
Ms. Pang Dany continued, "Therefore, when you return, you need to find out more about the legal documents, especially for everyone to have the documents with them and keep them with the local authorities so that they have a basis to help solve the problem." When we go to sue. In addition, even if you want to return to work abroad and in the country, it requires you to have a clear profession and career.
