The handover ceremony was presided over by the Deputy Commander of the Kandal Provincial Gendarmerie on behalf of the Commander-in-Chief, Oknha Srey Chanthorn, Mr. Chan Dara, Deputy Governor of Khsach Kandal District and the District Gendarmerie Commander. .
On that occasion, the Deputy Provincial Commander on behalf of the Commander-in-Chief expressed his deep gratitude and best wishes to the Duke and his colleagues for good health and success in all tasks. Follow Samdech Techo's recommendation! Ministry of Agriculture continues to push for increased production of agricultural products to ensure domestic food security as Cambodia blocks imports
(Phnom Penh): According to the recommendation of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister called on the people to work hard to cultivate agricultural production, including animal husbandry, rice and crops to increase the supply to meet local demand and take This opportunity must be created as an opportunity for the agricultural sector as Cambodia shuts down imports to contribute to the prevention and control of the global Kovid-19 epidemic.
In response to this call, the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries has issued a number of important and urgent guidelines to increase and strengthen the focus on production to ensure adequate food security to meet local needs in the context of the country. At risk from Kovid-19.
The meeting was attended by the Secretary of State, Undersecretary of State, Secretary-General, Advisor to the Royal Government of Cambodia, in charge of the Director General of the General Department of Agriculture, Animal Health and Animal Production, Fisheries Administration, Forestry Administration, General Department of Rubber, Director of 25 Departments and Units. Project management.
To begin with, the Minister briefed the meeting on the purpose of the meeting, emphasizing the will of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister, to ensure food security, create opportunities to increase productivity, and ensure domestic production. Supply quantity as required in the current circumstances.
Prepare enough to start the upcoming rainy season and all project managers need to review action plans and key objectives in order to respond to calls. Of Samdech Techo to be effective.
Subsequently, the three specialized units, General Department of Agriculture, General Department of Animal Health and Animal Production, Fisheries Administration, as well as the Project Management Unit, briefed the meeting on the progress of the implementation of the Ministry's instructions, highlighting the important results achieved. Yes and action plans to be implemented for both the short, medium and long term.
After hearing the report, Minister Veng Sakhon expressed his gratitude and appreciation to the leaders of the specialized units and the Capital-Provincial Departments of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries for their active efforts to fulfill their duties and achieve good and true results. Very participated in implementing the recommendations of Samdech Techo Prime Minister in a timely manner.
In order to take responsibility for ensuring food security in the context of Cambodia being affected by the Kovid-19 crisis, Minister Veng Sakhon took this opportunity to offer a number of important recommendations in addition to the previous guidelines, including:
First, in addition to intensifying rice cultivation, diversification of some important crops should also consider growing vegetables around the house and raising livestock to increase income, ensure food security, create employment opportunities and reduce the consequences of the people in this situation. .
Second, use the innovations of new technologies so that farmers can control production. Use less water-intensive technologies, consider post-harvest support infrastructure (technical, maintenance and processing facilities). Select a production site near a water source to prepare a document to submit to the "Rural Electrification Fund" to receive a preference for electricity for pumping water at night.
Third, select communities with sufficient potential and capacity to produce vegetables on a large scale, plan production and supply in accordance with market demand. Establish a marketing network to connect buyers and the production community in order to sustain market supply through the implementation of contract farming.
Seventh, the General Department of Animal Health and the Fisheries Administration must cooperate with the private sector in the production of animal feed, animal husbandry and fish to ensure both quantity and quality to increase production productivity, especially to increase partnerships with farmers.
Eighth, the three general departments, including the 25 departments of the capital-province, must cooperate to prevent the illegal import of agricultural products in order to protect the price of local agricultural products and open opportunities for local producers.
