Minister of Justice briefs the Constitutional Council on the draft law on "governing the country in a state of emergency"
(Phnom Penh): The Constitutional Council held a meeting on the morning of April 24, 2020 to review the constitutionality of the draft law on "governing the country in a state of emergency" after passing the National Assembly and Senate.
Mr. Keut Rith, Minister of Justice, a representative of the Royal Government, accompanied by his colleagues of the Ministry of Justice, also addressed the Constitutional Council on the draft law on "governing the country in a state of emergency" at the office of the Constitutional Council at Chamkarmon Palace. Also to protect this one draft law.
Please be informed that the draft law on "governing the country in a state of emergency" passed the Senate by a vote of 54 to 54 on the morning of April 17, 2020 to pave the way for this draft law to move forward. To be announced for use in the near future.
After review and commentary by the Senate, the draft law will be sent to the Constitutional Council for review before being submitted to the King for promulgation.
