The following is an explanation by Dr. Sok Raphon: Paragon International School calls on parents in financial crisis to apply for a tuition discount
(Phnom Penh): The crisis caused by the spread of Kovid 19 has been causing disputes in private educational institutions with students' parents regarding tuition fees after those schools tried to find ways to ensure the process. Schools with maintaining quality education for students.
Through the announcement received by Fresh News on April 24, 2020, the school council calls on all parents who are experiencing financial difficulties to apply for the tuition discount, along with other supporting documents for Examine and consider each case.
In this announcement, Paragon International School also reaffirmed its position that it will continue to work with parents of students in all possible ways to ensure continued operation and provision of educational services for all students.
Please be informed that in order to understand the difficulties and challenges of the school and the parents of the students during the crisis caused by Kovid 19, Mr. Eang Sophalleth, Honorary President of the school, on the morning of April 23, 2020, coordinated to meet with the parents. Of the 97 protesting students at the Paragon University building in Phnom Penh's Toul Kork district.
In front of the parents of the students, Mr. Sophalleth expressed the purpose and will of the school to provide quality education and quality, the level of quality of education in the school is equal to the world-famous international schools. He said that with the school being recognized by the International School Council, students at Paragon International School can continue their studies abroad without further study or tests such as IELTS or TOEFL.
The former Cambodian student who graduated from Canada reminded that because when he was a student, when he went to study abroad, he was assessed on the quality and level of education in Cambodia and did not want him to study, which prompted him to work hard. Build an internationally recognized quality school.
He said that although Cambodia now has to close its schools to fight Kovid 19, the school has made every effort and means to ensure a quality education. In order to maintain a quality education, the school has decided to invest in distance learning or online learning by writing teaching programs and creating apps for the school itself, installing equipment, technology and training teachers for online learning.
The honorary principal of the school told the parents that the distance learning program that the school has organized still maintains a learning environment similar to that in the classroom. That is, both teachers and students appear on computer screens or electronic devices during teaching and learning hours, and absences are still common.
Through what the school has organized, the teaching and learning of the students ensures the same quality, and most of the students praised the arrangement to provide them with knowledge when the school closed due to Kovid 19.
Mr. Eang Sophalleth emphasized that although the school was not open for teaching, the teachers and other operations at Paragon International School continued to operate normally. In order to run the day-to-day operations and be ready to reopen immediately upon the Ministry's recommendation, the teacher's salary and other school expenses during the crisis remain the same.
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Kith Sophal, Commander of Chbar Ampov District Gendarmerie, and his wife this morning, April 24, 2020, met with people and distributed some materials such as rice, alcohol and soap, and disseminated information on Prevention and spread of COVID-19 virus in Chbar Ampov II commune.
