(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training has decided to allow members of the Cambodian Higher Education Association to suspend the payment of contributions to the National Social Security Fund for six months from April to September 2020 at the request of the Association. Cambodian Higher Education Institution.
The letter from the Minister of Labor, Mr. Ith Sam Heng, received by Fresh News on April 24, 2020, stated that “The Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training allows educational institutions that are members of the Cambodian Higher Education Association to suspend Pay contributions from April to September 2020. ”
The Minister further stated that in case the status of Kovid 19 was terminated before September 2020 and there was a notification from the Royal Government requiring all levels and all types of educational institutions to re-operate, the educational institutions that are members of the Association of Institutions Higher education in Cambodia is obliged to continue to pay contributions from the month of operation.
