Paragon International School invests in online learning to ensure quality education
(Phnom Penh): Kovid 19 has forced the Royal Government to close schools across the country. Paragon International School, Cambodia's only internationally accredited training school by the International School Council (CIS), has made every effort to maintain a quality education at the time of Kovid 19 outbreak. This.
To ensure a quality education, the school has decided to invest more in online learning by equipping students with technology, programming and app development for distance learning or online learning.
Paragon International School leaders see an outbreak of Kovid 19 as affecting education since the outbreak began. After seeing the impact on education, the school began to think and organize online education.
Eang Sophalleth, Honorary President of Paragon International School, told Fresh News that Paragon International School has been developing an app with technical equipment for teaching and training teachers online since January 2020.
The honorary principal of Paragon International School did not disclose the amount of additional investment in online tutoring, but said it was a considerable amount.
Mr. Eang Sophalleth said, "We strive to find all the possibilities and means to provide education to our students. "We want to ensure that our students continue to receive a quality education during this epidemic of Kovid 19."
"We do not want Kovid 19 to come in and destroy the knowledge, the education of our Cambodian children. That's why the school has decided to invest in programming, app development, and additional technical equipment to educate our students. ” Mr. Sophalleth added.
Paragon International School's online tutoring is not a video recording and drop-off for individual students to study at home. But a modern teaching method, as well as famous schools on the international stage used.
The online tutoring provided by Paragon International School is similar to classroom learning, with teachers and students seeing each other face-to-face on their computer screens or electronic devices.
According to Mr. Eang Sophalleth, this online teaching and learning is similar to the classroom hours of the past, with teachers and students having to show up during teaching and learning hours and extracting the normal student presence. He said that since the school was closed under the guidance of the Ministry of Education, the provision of education to students remains the same as the curriculum that the school has through teaching and learning online.
Mr. Sophalleth sees this online teaching as another new opportunity for the school to help train students to learn how to work online, which is a global trend that will evolve into the future. Takhmao City Police Inspector Announces Donation of 400,000 Riel Salary for 6 Months to National Commission Against Kovid 19
