Philippines sends 2,676 tons of garbage back to South Korea
In a statement, Dominguez said the 2,676 tons of raw materials were part of a total of more than 5,000 tons of waste that the South Korean government has pledged to repatriate. They returned after the waste was illegally imported to the Philippines in 2018.
The waste is a thin sheet of synthetic plastic that was illegally imported by a local company based in Cebu, central Philippines. The rubbish has been shipped back to the country of origin in 151 containers, divided into three portions.
Last year, Philippine President Duterte ordered a ban on all imports of waste. The decision came after 103 containers of Canadian garbage were returned to their home countries in May 2019.
