Along with the drafting of the law on "governing the country in a state of emergency", this has led to much debate and question as to what state the country is in a state of emergency and should be addressed. Law on "Management of the nation in a state of emergency" to use?
At a press conference on April 22, 2020, Jean Malin, spokesman for the Ministry of Justice, said that there are four reasons and situations that would put the country in a state of emergency. The four causes and conditions include:
* First: Accidents caused by war and foreign aggression * Second: Accidents affecting national security, stability and public order * Third: Accidents affecting the lives and health of the people * Fourth: Caused by a serious disaster that spread across the country.
According to Jean Malin, in addition to the four reasons above, the law also paves the way for a number of other reasons to put the country under a state of emergency in case of an emergency or necessity.
Please be informed that the law on "governing the country in a state of emergency" stipulates that the deployment of a state of emergency is done once every three months at the request of the top three dignitaries: the President of the Senate, the President of the National Assembly and the Prime Minister. And at the end, also proposed by the top three dignitaries.
The draft law "Governing the nation in a state of emergency" has 5 chapters and 12 articles. In the draft law, Article 4, Chapter 3 stipulates that when a country is declared a state of emergency, the Royal Government has the right to issue the following rules:
The draft law also mentions the responsibilities of the competent authorities when a country is placed in a state of emergency. Article 10 in Chapter 4 states that competent officials who arbitrarily exercise their authority in violation of the law and cause bodily harm or damage to the property of another person shall be liable for the acts committed. In accordance with Cambodian law.
