PARIS (Reuters) - A majority of French people are concerned about the government's plan to ease travel restrictions on May 11, according to a survey. -19 seems to be a little relieved after 5 weeks of closure. This is according to the release by the Xinhua news agency in the morning of Thursday, April 23, 2020.
An electronic survey conducted by the Elabe Institute found that 66% of the 1,000 respondents expressed concern about easing travel restrictions. While 34% are optimistic about life after closing. As for the reopening of schools, 63% think that the government is not well prepared yet.
