(Svay Rieng): The mushroom season has arrived, people in Prey Pdao village, Bati commune, Bavet city, rush to pick mushrooms to sell at a reasonable price to increase income to support a living level.
According to a woman who sells mushrooms, for her family, in her spare time, they go to pick mushrooms in the forest and wind oil in the Prey Konokki community in Bavet City to sell.
His family of five picks mushrooms from 2pm until 5am, some picking up 1kg and others picking up to 5kg to different communities with less mushrooms growing. For sale on National Road 1, with passers-by stopping to buy natural mushrooms. The price of 1 kg of mushrooms sold for 20,000 riel to 30,000 riel is quite high.
The same woman continued that in addition to factory work and farming, and this season, there was a rain or two, there were mushrooms growing, and the villagers came to take it to cook and sell it to support their livelihood. Family.
Removing mushrooms is not a regular job like factory work and farming or selling, just a small amount of money to supplement, because the mushrooms grow at the beginning of the year, when the first rains, and the mushrooming period is about 3 months. And also can not be withdrawn every day.
