(Kampong Chhnang): Two more tractors were seized by the police and kept at the Chulkiri District Police Inspectorate on April 19, 2020, while the two tractors were plowing on a field in Kampong Ta Ou point is located in Peam Chkork village, Peam Chkork commune, Chulkiri district, Kampong Chhnang province. This is according to the claims of the people who own the farmland and the local authorities there.
The people who own the land said that all the above fields, they have been enjoying since 1994, every year, never missing a year, some years plowed with cattle. Some years plowing, harrowing and bulldozing, but in recent years they have hired tractors to plow for fear of rain.
They also requested the authorities, professional officials and the judiciary to return the two tractors to them for further subsistence and to acquit them. .
Regarding the above case, on the morning of April 21, 2020, Mr. Long Sitha, Deputy Prosecutor who led the police to seize the machine directly on April 19, 2020, said that this case He asked a professional officer to build a case and send it to the court, and the charges depend on the professional officer who is the plaintiff.
As for the judiciary, he does not yet know who the Deputy Prosecutor will be in charge of this case, so he does not know what to accuse him of waiting for a professional officer to build a case. .
The results of the evaluation of all the joint teams, including village authorities, communes, community leaders, fisheries officials, deputy district governors, as well as two armed forces, consisting of district sub-units and district police inspectors, who went to seize the machinery directly. Along with the Deputy Prosecutor also claimed that the land where the two bulldozers were above is the people's farmland, not flooded forest land.
Fisheries officials also said on the morning of April 21, 2020 that in the case of people plowing their fields that have been used, even if they do not ask for a law, they can do. Except for encroachment on state forest land is illegal.
As for farming, you also have to ask for a law, that is, no, people have the right to farm their fields without asking for any law, but the thing that requires a law is to be afraid that they will take the machinery. Clearing his farmland, which only affects state land.
Therefore, experts must first inspect before they clear the land, but as in the case above, if the joint commission finds that they have plowed their fields, it is not illegal.
