(Phnom Penh): The International Committee of the Red Cross in Cambodia (ICRC) on the morning of April 20, 2020 organized a training course on "Chlorine Disinfection Techniques" for officials of the 28 General Departments of Prisons. Capital to prevent the spread of Kovid 19 in prisons.
The training day was also attended by a delegation from the Deputy Director General of the General Department of Prisons, Mr. Chhun Sanath and Mr. Lim Sokha and Mr. Jingiri Ray Ambekkov, Deputy Director of Prison Project Coordinators at the ICRC, Dr. Nesrin. Ben Amet, ICRC Prison Health Project Manager, including a total of 66 provincial and municipal prison officials and technicians.
This training is a support activity after the event of handing over sanitary ware to the General Department of Prisons to prevent the spread of Kovid 19 disease in the prison at the 1st Correctional Center (M1).
In collaboration with the General Department of Prisons of the Ministry of Interior, the ICRC has continued its mission with the aim of providing medical equipment and sanitation equipment to detainees as well as prison officials through the provision of sanitation facilities, training and Monitor key activities such as setting up sanitary checkpoints on the premises and providing protection to a total of 38,000 inmates and a total of 4,000 prison officials.
The ICRC has stressed the importance of restoring the family ties of detainees, as it is now doing its utmost to prevent the spread of the Kovid 19 virus in prisons.
It should be noted that the ICRC handed over 20 tons of sanitary ware to the General Department of Prisons to prevent the spread of Kovid 19 disease in prisons at the 1st Correctional Center (M1) on the morning of April 10, 2020. The purpose of these materials is to support and contribute to the efforts of the General Department of Prisons in preventing and controlling the spread of Khovid 19 disease in correctional centers and capital-provincial prisons.
In Cambodia, the ICRC has expanded its mission direction in response to the current situation. The charity is also focusing on supporting local authorities to prevent the spread of the 19 Kovid virus in prisons and to ensure that inmates remain in contact with their families.
The ICRC also ensures that rehabilitation centers in Battambang and Kampong Speu provinces remain operational. In addition, support with the National Red Cross Society in raising awareness of hygiene, sanitation and safety measures to prevent the spread of 19 Kovid disease in the 13 affected provinces.
Mr. Roman Paramonov, Head of the ICRC Mission in Cambodia, said that the ICRC team was honored to have the cooperation and contribution of the General Department of Prisons. The ICRC has prepared a $ 230,000 budget for operations to supply the necessary equipment and supplies and provide technical training to prison authorities.
