Ministry of Labor Organizes 10 Charity Centers in Phnom Penh, Only 2 Workers Are Sampled
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training has set up 10 Chattalysak centers in areas with many factories in Phnom Penh to isolate workers 14 days after returning from their hometowns and taking time off. New Year has passed. This is according to Mr. Heng Sour, a spokesman for the Ministry of Labor.
Mr. Heng Sour made this statement on the occasion that he and his team inspected each of the Chatalisak centers on April 20, 2020.
He said that on the occasion of the New Year, about 30,000 workers in the textile, garment and footwear sector across the country, equivalent to 2%, took time off, both legal and illegal, in the capital. There are about 15,000 workers in Phnom Penh, but some workers did not return to work because they wanted to take time off during the New Year.
Heng Sour said that so far two workers had been diagnosed with some of the 19 symptoms of Kovid and their samples had been inspected at the Institut Pasteur. However, Heng Sour could not confirm the whereabouts of their whereabouts.
They are getting the attention of the manager of Chattalysak district, with the police force checking to make sure he does not go out and provide food at a minimum.
These centers are divided into two levels, including Level 1 Centers and Level 2 Centers. The 10 Chattali Sak centers are located at Vattanac 1 Industrial Park, Canadia Industrial Park, Kork Panchan Secondary School, Vattanac II Industrial Park, Chumpouvorn High School, Dangkor Secondary School, Phnom Penh Thmey High School, Phnom Penh Special Economic Zone, Russey Village Primary School and Russey Keo High School.
Mr. Heng Sour said that the level 1's detention center is like being isolated in a house or a private room, but if the landlord or his roommate does not dare to stay in his rented room, then the person can Can stay separately in this center.
The Level 2 Chattalysak Center is for individuals who are sampled for inspection at the Institut Pasteur. If the test is positive, he will be sent to the Khmer-Russian Friendship Hospital for treatment.
He added that the Level 2 building can accommodate only one person, while the Level 1 building can accommodate more than one person, and each level can accommodate a total of about 2,500 people.
The handover ceremony of medical equipment and facilities was held at the Ministry of Health on April 20, 2020.
In particular, it contributes to strengthening the emergency response capacity not only to the current COVID-19 problem, but to be used whenever there is an outbreak of an infectious disease in the future, as well as to improve the quality of life. Of the Cambodian people.
