Amret is offering deferred repayments to more than 120,000 credit customers who are severely affected by Kovid 19
(Phnom Penh): With a strong financial position, Microfinance Institution “Amret” has been easing the burden on credit customers who are severely affected by Kovid 19 disease by providing credit repayment deferrals.
Among the repayment delays that Amret is offering are: Postponement of principal repayment and deferment of both principal and interest, which can last from three to six months, depending on the actual difficulty of Each customer.
Mr. Dos Dean, General Director of Amret Microfinance Institution, stated that as one of the most socially responsible institutions in Cambodia and in this difficult situation, the measures to delay the repayment of loans will contribute to reducing the impact. Customer life.
Dossin said the repayment delays being offered are divided into two main categories: first, most credit card insurers live in rural areas with small loans that are difficult to repay and if This type of small loan customer requests to extend the repayment, Amret will provide automatic repayment of both interest and principal automatically for three months.
Mr. Dos Deen further stated that through direct contact with customers in the past, the customers with low impact are still willing to fulfill their obligations, continue to repay normally. Amret would like to thank and appreciate the less affected customers who continue to pay back to give Amret the opportunity to use its capabilities to help the severely affected customers.
Amret values a good relationship with customers and understands the well-being of customers. Especially in this difficult situation, Amret's loan officer will contact each borrower to find out the difficulties and study the various possibilities that Amret can support.
Finally, Mr. Dos Dean took this opportunity to thank all customers for their continued support and trust in Amret. We will go through it together and we will overcome it one day.
