(Phnom Penh): Samdech Pich Sena Tea Banh, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of National Defense, on April 20, 2020, reminded Cambodian students studying in other countries to take good care of their health, hygiene and social distance. As well as implementing preventive measures during the outbreak of COVID-19 virus after three Cambodian military personnel in Russia became infected with Kovid 19.
According to a report by the Office of the Deputy Attorney General of the Cambodian Embassy in Russia on April 19, three Cambodian military trainees studying in Russia have been infected with Kovid 19 and are now infected. Admitted for treatment in Russia. The discovery of 19 Kovid in the bodies of the three Cambodian military trainees took place after an examination by a municipal hospital in Russia on April 18, 2020.
The cause of the infection was claimed by the Office of the Cambodian Military Attaché because of the infection from other foreign military trainees who were studying together and staying on the same floor. The three military trainees are currently being treated at Kovid 19 Hospital in Russia and are being monitored.
However, the medical condition of the three Cambodian military trainees is not serious yet, as they have reported their health and medical condition to the doctor to be tested for Kovid 19 virus in time.
