Ancient foundations found around Tolai temple buried more than 100 years under modern religious structures
In this regard, in mid-March 2020, archaeologists of the APSARA Authority began researching and discovering the great secrets of many ancient structures, such as gates, floors, ceramics, and walls buried under religious buildings. Since the French colonial period.
The discovery of this enormous structure is to provide new data for archeological research, history, architecture and conservation work, to develop and enhance the value of Tolay Temple.
Tho Thon, head of the excavation team at Prasat Lolay, said the team had dug 10 excavations under the former religious building on the east, north and west sides and found the gate structure in all three directions. The three-story wall surrounds the four towers of the temple.
Regarding the reason for burying the temple structure in this land, Mr. Tho Thon concluded that it was probably due to the later construction, forgetting that there was something underground, because there was soil erased from the ancient building. Later developments did not cause much damage to the ancient underground structures, as the old ones kept the interior with floor tiles and the exterior with laterite for protection.
Twenty-one-hundred-year-old Buddha statues found underground near Angkor Wat
Mr. Long Kosal told Fresh News on April 17 that the discovery of the ancient Buddha statue occurred on April 11 while the team of APSARA Authority is implementing a project to prepare a grass irrigation system. To beautify the Angkor Wat temple complex.
The 21 Buddha statues were broken into 141 pieces buried in the ground to a depth of nearly half a meter. In the posture of standing and sitting, and there is also the Buddha with the dragon roof, most of the head, hands, feet and some other parts are broken.
The spokesman said that some of these statues are more than 100 to 300 years old and also 500 years old, including red stains on some of the statues.
Mr. Long Kosal added that in the future, experts will not continue to excavate, as this discovery is not in the excavation project, but in the implementation of the project to prepare a grass irrigation system in the Angkor Wat temple. And when the experts inspected the site (because it may affect the main part of the temple) also saw these Buddha statues, so the experts decided not to excavate more.
