(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Commerce claims that professional officials of the Ministry have found up to 80 tons of hand-washing alcohol sold in the market made of methanol, which causes serious problems to the health of consumers.
Through the announcement on April 17, 2020, the Ministry of Commerce emphasized that the General Department of Consumer Protection, Competition and Anti-Fraud (CPC) of the Ministry of Commerce has cooperated with institutions. Involves inspecting the quality of hand-washing alcohol circulating and distributing in markets and other places.
The operation uncovered the fraudulent use of more than 80 tons of methanol as an alcohol-based hand sanitizer for Kovid-19.
The Ministry of Commerce has called on businessmen, companies, enterprises and individuals who trade in methanol-based products to stop selling and distributing those products in the market for the common good of all citizens.
The Ministry of Commerce stressed that if the Ministry continues to see that traders, companies, enterprises and individuals are still taking the opportunity to sell and distribute methanol alcohol while Cambodia is facing a global epidemic of Kovid-19 disease Trade will take legal action.
According to the World Health Organization guidelines, methanol is not allowed to be used as an active ingredient in the manufacture of hand sanitizers.
* Methanol is very harmful to the health of consumers. In the short term, it will cause skin irritation, eye irritation, headache, dizziness, drowsiness, confusion, loss of consciousness, vomiting, disturbance of digestion and dizziness.
In the long run, it can be toxic to the body, damage the brain, cause blurred vision or dizziness and can be completely dark. If mixed with wine or with other beverages.
