1: For the owner or director of a factory in Phnom Penh, the Ministry of Labor has recommended the following:
* Arrange a separate room in a suitable location for the presence of workers who return to work after work.
* Assign administrative staff to prepare a list of workers who have returned to work after work to be handed over to the Labor Inspector every day at 2 pm
* Instruct the workers to go for a health check at the health check center according to the instructions of the Labor Inspector, including:
* Workers who are inspected for suspicious symptoms should be sent to the Level 2 Consistency Center for further examination.
Workers who are inspected for asymptomatic symptoms should be kept in isolation at their place of residence for 14 days in accordance with the Chaktalisak Rule at the home of the Ministry of Health and must report to the factory administration by telephone about their health condition. Every day for the factory administration to report to the doctors of the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training
* Workers who do not have a place to stay for any reason, such as a request from the landlord who is not allowed to stay with them, notify the medical team of the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training to contact the level of the center. 1 any.
* There is no obligation to pay any worker who takes time off without the permission of the employer during this period.
* There is an obligation to pay up to 7 days' wages to any worker who is on leave with the permission of the employer during the period of probation. Separately, workers who are present with the permission of the employer due to special business as a delivery system or grandparents, parents, spouses, children are entitled to be paid for 14 full days.
* Continue to monitor health, provide masks and rarely wear masks for workers who have just completed their work or have just started working.
