The Cambodian Microfinance Association issued a statement urging honest and responsible settlement between microfinance institutions and debtors during the difficult times of Kovid 19
(Phnom Penh): The Cambodian Microfinance Association (CFA) on April 17, 2020, issued a statement urging honest and responsible settlement between microfinance institutions and debtors in times of crisis. 19.
In a statement, the Cambodian Microfinance Association, as a professional association, stated its willingness to facilitate and resolve six issues:
2. All members of the association will do their best to respond and support their customers. Of course, during these difficult times, each institution that is a member of the association has different abilities and possibilities to support its customers. The management, shareholders, staff at all levels of each institution have been working hard to the best of their ability to ensure the sustainability of the sector and continue to provide financial services to customers.
4: To get support and solutions, especially credit restructuring, customers need to contact the institution where they borrowed to discuss the situation and possible solutions with the staff. Clients need to provide comprehensive information to find appropriate solutions and win-win together to continue the financial sector and the national economy.
5: For customers who are not affected or slightly affected and have the ability to repay, the Association would like to encourage customers to continue to repay as usual, giving priority to each institution to take the opportunity that it has. Help customers who are severely affected. In this circumstance, being honest and giving concessions to those who are in dire straits is a generous gesture that will earn respect.
6. The Association, together with its members, has been closely monitoring the development of the microfinance sector with relevant partners, as well as taking precautionary measures to prevent and resolve any issues that may arise in the future.
Once again, the Cambodian Microfinance Association strongly believes that when microfinance institutions and clients work together to find honest and responsible solutions, we can ensure the sustainability of the financial sector. The backbone of our national economy.
