"Overall, it means that the law on governing the country in a state of emergency will be implemented after the country is declared a state of emergency," he said.
The "Draft Law on the Management of Emergencies in Emergencies" consisting of 5 chapters and 12 articles prepared by the Royal Government to lead the country when placed in a state of emergency was approved by the National Assembly in the morning plenary session. April 10, 2020. At the same time, this law will be submitted to the Senate for comment on April 17, 2020.
This draft law will provide a legal basis to ensure the implementation of the new Article 22 of the Constitution and a legal basis to determine the authority of the Royal Government to introduce the necessary measures that are indispensable to respond to the situation in the country. Emergency aims to protect security, public order, protect the life and health of the people, as well as protect property and the environment.
