Spring is here! Travelers on National Road No. 1 do not forget to help buy wild fruits in Srah village, Preah Sdach district, Prey Veng province.
(Prey Veng): Travelers on National Road No. 1 from the west of Hun Sen Ta Kork High School, do not forget to stop to buy buffalo milk, rice and water from the villagers of Srah, Romchek commune, Preah Sdach district, Prey Veng province because of the month This is the ripening season, with many villagers selling wild berries on baskets, waiting for travelers to stop their cars or motorbikes to help buy them.
Srah village forest vendors describe how Srah villagers' wild fruits are so famous that they attract many passengers to stop their vehicles to buy and taste this natural forest, which is available only once a year. Almost all of the villagers' houses have from 3 to many trees, some up to 10 trees.
Pring fruit has increased some income for the families of Srah villagers, who can sell for a profit of 50,000 riel or more per day. Each year, the villagers can sell the forest for two months, from the beginning of April to the end of June.
