Bak Kheng police officer shot and killed his brother-in-law because of jealousy with his wife
(Kandal): A murder case occurred when a brother-in-law, a Bak Kheng police officer, shot and killed his brother-in-law out of jealousy.
The murder led to the shooting at 6:30 pm on April 15, 2020 at Chong Koh village, Koh Oknha Tey commune, Khsach Kandal district, Kandal province.
Brigadier General Chhoeun Socheat, Kandal Provincial Police Commissioner, told Fresh News this morning, April 16, 2020, that the dead victim was Mao Bunheng Pros, a 25-year-old Cambodian trader. The suspect, Sen Ranun, a 35-year-old Cambodian man, a police officer at the Bak Kheng Administration Post, escaped. The suspect's wife and the victim are siblings.
The General Commissioner continued that at the time of the incident, the suspect had a dispute with his wife Kong Sokchea, the suspect took an unknown handgun to shoot his wife, then the victim came out to stop, saying that he wanted to shoot his wife Anyway, suddenly the suspect, who was angry and jealous, shot at one of the victims and hit him in the throat, causing his death at the scene. The suspect later took a motorcycle as a neighbor and escaped.
