1: Workers must continue to work as usual in their factories, enterprises, establishments.
2: In case any worker takes time off during this period on his / her own, the worker will be subject to the Health Charter (Separation) for 14 days before returning to work and will not be paid for the period. Do not do this.
3: In case any worker takes time off during this period with the permission of the employer, the worker will be placed in the Health Charter (Separation) for 14 days before returning to work and receiving wages. From the employer during this period.
4. The employer must arrange for a list of workers who are on leave during this period to provide to the competent authority to implement the rules of health care (segregation).
