On behalf of His Majesty King Norodom Sihamoni, King of Cambodia, and on behalf of the Senate, National Assembly and Royal Government of Cambodia, Samdech Vibol Sena Pheakdey Say Chhum extended a warm welcome to Ermenegildo Kupa Lopes, who was greeted by President Timor-Leste. Appointed Ambassador Extraordinary and Plenipotentiary of the Democratic Republic of Timor-Leste to the Kingdom of Cambodia.
The Ambassador expressed his pleasure at the good relations and cooperation between the governments and peoples of the two countries. He praised the progress and progress of the Kingdom of Cambodia. He also thanked the Kingdom of Cambodia for its support for Timor-Leste to become a member of ASEAN in the near future.
In response, the Acting Head of State praised the friendship and cooperation between the two countries and peoples. He is confident that the Ambassador will work to strengthen the friendship, cooperation and promote trade, economy, investment and tourism for the benefit of both countries and peoples.
The Acting Head of State expressed his pleasure to see that the relationship and cooperation between the people and the two countries have been developing steadily. This good relationship is reflected in the exchange of visits by senior government officials of the two countries and mutual support in the framework of international cooperation, especially within the framework of the United Nations.
The Acting Head of State stated that the Senate, National Assembly, Royal Government, Ministries and National Institutions of the Kingdom of Cambodia are always ready to cooperate closely with the Ambassador as well as the Embassy of the Democratic Republic of Timor-Leste in the Kingdom of Cambodia to promote The relationship and the great benefits for the people and the two countries.
